hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4801","Abdullah ibn Said al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from al-Layth, from Ata and Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr and Umar performed tamattu, and the first to forbid it was Muawiyah."
"4802","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Hisham Abu al-Miqdam, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah created Paradise white, and the most beloved thing to Allah is white, so let your living wear it and shroud your dead in it."
"4803","al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Marwan ibn Salim, he said: Abd al-Malik narrated to me, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first thing with which the servant is recompensed after his death is that all those who followed his funeral be forgiven."
"4804","Ubayd ibn Bakhit narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I performed zihar from my wife, then I saw her leg in the moonlight and had intercourse with her before expiating. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Expiate, and do not repeat."
"4805","Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Shuja narrated to us, he said: Khusayf narrated to us, from Ata, Mujahid and Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, raising the hadith, he said: The menstruating woman and the woman in postpartum bleeding perform all the rites except tawaf of the House, until she becomes pure."
"4806","Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Hafs ibn Sulayman, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah forbids you from nakedness, so be shy before the angels of Allah who are with you, the noble recorders who do not leave you except in one of three situations: relieving oneself, major impurity, and bathing. So when one of you bathes in the open, let him screen himself with his garment, or part of a wall, or his camel."
"4807","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Muslim al-Batin, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the morning prayer on Friday: Alif Lam Mim, the revelation (Surah al-Sajdah), and: Has there come upon man (Surah al-Insan)."
"4808","Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Sharik, from Layth, from Ata and Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Umm Salamah ahead at night on the night of Jam from Muzdalifah. Ibn Abbas said: I was with them as well."
"4809","And Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, from Layth, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I often saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while donkeys were moving about in front of him, meaning while he was praying."
"4810","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala informed me, he said: Hisham informed me, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I stoned before shaving? He said: Shave, and there is no harm."
"4811","Azhar ibn Jamil narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him with the baggage at night from Jam with his family."
"4812","And Abdullah ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Thabit ibn Yazid Abu Zayd narrated to us, he said: Hilal ibn Khabbab narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would spend consecutive nights hungry with his stomach empty, while his family found no supper, and most of their bread was barley bread."
"4813","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would dispatch an expedition, he would say: Fight in the name of Allah, fight those who disbelieve in Allah, do not betray, do not mutilate, do not kill a child, nor the occupants of hermitages."
"4814","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach them against fever and all pains: In the name of Allah the Great, and praise be to Allah the Great, the Mighty, from the evil of a spurting vein and from the evil of the heat of the Fire."
"4815","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Sayyar narrated to us, from Yaqub ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two Eids: Concerning what do they question one another (Surah al-Naba), and: By the sun and its brightness (Surah al-Shams)."
"4816","Abd al-Rahman ibn Isa ibn Sasan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things do not break the fast of the fasting person: vomiting, cupping, and a wet dream."
"4817","Ahmad ibn al-Walid al-Karkhi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah al-Uwaysi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that Ali married Fatimah from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for an iron coat of mail."
"4818","al-Abbas ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, he said: Abu Kudaynah narrated to us, he said: Qabus narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from laziness, old age, the punishment of the grave, and the trial of the heart."
"4819","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Abdullah ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that when a matter befell the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would say: There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Mighty; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the heavens and the earth, Lord of the Noble Throne. Then he would supplicate."
"4820","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Jannad narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped, and the cupper complained to him of his tax, so he sent to his masters that they lighten his tax."
"4821","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: Abu Jahl said: If I see Muhammad praying, I will surely tread upon his neck. He said: It was said: There he is. He said: I do not see him. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had he done so, the angels would have seized him openly. And had the Jews wished for death, they would have died."
"4822","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn al-Numan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: Between Adam and Nuh there were ten generations, all upon a law of truth. He said: Then when Allah sent the Prophet and revealed His Book, he said: Mankind were one community."
"4823","And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade (drinking from) gourds and varnished vessels, and said: Do not drink except from a vessel that is tied shut."
"4824","Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Abu Sufyan al-Himyari narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Ibn Shubrumah, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: Wine was forbidden, its small and large amounts, and every intoxicant from every drink."
"4825","Ismail ibn Yaqub narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ali ibn Badhimah, that Said ibn Jubayr informed him, from Qays ibn Habtar, that a man came to Ibn Abbas asking him about nabidh. He said: The first to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about nabidh were people who came from Abd al-Qays. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a fertile land. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make nabidh in waterskins, and do not make nabidh in the naqir nor the hantam."
"4826","Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: al-Dahhak narrated to us, from Abbad, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah curse the Jews; fats were forbidden to them, so they sold them and consumed their price."
"4827","And Khalid narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from al-Dahhak, from Abbad, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of a dog and the earnings of a slave woman."
"4828","Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Umayr ibn Imran narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness."
"4829","Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Silah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs Hajj on behalf of his parents, or settles a debt on their behalf after their death, will be raised with the righteous on the Day of Resurrection."
"4830","Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn Sayf al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Hanzalah, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Exalted said: I accept prayer only from one who humbles himself therein due to My greatness, does not exalt himself over My creation, does not persist overnight upon disobedience to Me, spends his day in My remembrance, shows mercy to the poor, the wayfarer, the widow, and shows mercy to the afflicted. His light is like the light of the sun; I protect him by My might and entrust him to My angels; I make for him light in darkness and forbearance in ignorance, and his likeness among My creation is like al-Firdaws in Paradise."
"4831","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dispense with people even with a toothstick sliver."
"4832","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray toward Bayt al-Maqdis with the Kabah before him, and after he migrated to Madinah for sixteen months."
"4833","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: When it was Thursday, and what a Thursday, then Ibn Abbas wept, during the illness of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which he died, he said: Bring me a sheet and an inkwell so I may write for you a document after which you will never go astray."
"4834","Said ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habibah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the stud fee of the camel."
"4835","And Said ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ismail narrated to me, from Dawud ibn Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade (the sale of) malaqih and madamin and the sale of habl al-habalah."
"4836","And Said ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ismail narrated to me, from Dawud ibn Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that when a dog laps from a vessel, it be washed seven times."
"4837","Said narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that a man divorced his wife, so she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: No maintenance and no lodging."
"4838","Said narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Dubaa that she stipulate in Hajj and say: My place of release is where You detain me."
"4839","Ahmad ibn Mualla al-Adami narrated to us, he said: Jabir ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Sallam Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Zibyan, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that Jibril (peace be upon him) came to the Prophet in the form of a pale traveling man until he placed his hand upon the knee of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What is Islam? He said: That you testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, establish prayer, give zakah, fast Ramadan, and perform Hajj of the House. He said: If I do that, have I submitted? He said: Yes. He said: You have spoken the truth. He said: So we were amazed at his questioning him and his confirming him. Then he said: What is ihsan? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: To fear Allah as though you see Him, for if you do not see Him, He sees you. He said: If I do that, have I done well? He said: Yes. He said: You have spoken the truth. He said: Then inform me, what is faith? He said: Faith in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, the Last Day, Paradise, the Fire, resurrection after death, and the decree, its good and its evil. He said: If I do that, have I believed? He said: Yes. He said: You have spoken the truth. He said: Then when is the Hour? He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the one asked about it knows no more than the questioner, but it has signs: when you see a woman give birth to her mistress, and you see the barefoot, naked, destitute, meaning the Arabs, ruling over people. He said: You have spoken the truth. Then he turned away. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring me the man. He looked and saw nothing. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know who this is? We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: This is Jibril; he came to teach you your religion. He never came to me in any form but I recognized him, except this time."
"4840","Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib al-Raqqi informed us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq al-Bazzar narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I performed zihar from my wife, then I had intercourse with her before expiating. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did not Allah, Blessed and Exalted, say: Before they touch one another. He said: She pleased me. He said: Withhold until you expiate. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas with an isnad better than this isnad, though Ismail ibn Muslim has been criticized, yet many people of knowledge narrated from him. And in this hadith of jurisprudence is that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him with only one expiation."
"4841","Muhammad ibn Harun al-Baghdadi Abu Nashit narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hudud are not carried out in mosques, and a father is not killed for (killing) his child."
"4842","And al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated it to us, he said: Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), likewise. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas except from this angle with this isnad. And as for the hadith of Qatadah, we do not know anyone narrated it except Said ibn Bashir from him. We only mentioned it from Ismail ibn Muslim, though Ismail ibn Muslim has been criticized, because we did not memorize the hadith of Said except from Abu al-Mughirah, so we wanted to show that another narrated it."
"4843","Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Saigh al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out with a piece of gold in his hand and a piece of silk and said: Verily these two are forbidden for the males of my ummah and lawful for its females. And this hadith has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from more than one angle, and all its isnads narrated in that are close to one another, and we have sufficed from clarifying Ismail ibn Muslim due to our prior mention of him."
"4844","al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Tawus al-Yamani, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bathe on Friday, wash your heads, and touch perfume. So Ibn Abbas said: As for perfume, I do not know; as for bathing, yes. And this hadith with this wording we do not know anyone narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Ibn Abbas, and we do not know al-Zuhri narrated from Tawus except two hadiths, this being one of them and the other from Ibn Umar."
"4845","And Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibrahim ibn Maysarah informed me, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that he mentioned to him the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about bathing on Friday, so I said to him: And touch perfume if he finds it? He said: I do not know it."
"4846","And Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us that he heard Tawus and Ikrimah informing, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: Dubaa bint al-Zubayr came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I am a heavy woman and I want to perform Hajj, so how should I enter ihram? He said: Enter ihram and stipulate: My place of release is where You detain me. And this hadith has been narrated from Ibn Abbas through various paths, and we do not know Abu al-Zubayr narrated from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, any hadith other than this one, and its isnad is sound. It has been narrated from Ibn Abbas through many paths, and narrated from Dubaa, and from Ishaq, from others than those we mentioned, and from Jabir."
"4847","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Isa Ibn al-Tabba narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose in the middle of the night for prayer and said: O Allah, to You is praise; You are the Light of the heavens and the earth, and to You is praise; You are the Sustainer of the heavens and the earth, and to You is praise; You are the Lord of the heavens and the earth and all therein, and to You is praise; You are the Truth, Your word is the truth, meeting You is the truth, Paradise is true, the Fire is true, and the Hour is true. To You I submit, in You I believe, upon You I rely, to You I turn, by You I dispute, and to You I refer judgment. So forgive me what I have done before and after, in secret and in public. You are Allah, there is no god but You. And we do not know this hadith narrated except from Ibn Abbas, and it has been narrated from Ibn Abbas from various angles, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Abu al-Zubayr except Malik."
"4848","Ahmad ibn Abdah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad informed me, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Tawus, he said: Ibn Abbas was asked about iqa (squatting) in prostration. He said: There is no harm in it. Tawus said: I do not see it so. He said: Ibn Abbas said: It is a Sunnah. And we do not know anyone narrating this hadith with this wording except Ibn Abbas, nor do we know for it a path other than this path from an established angle for this wording, though something close to its meaning has been narrated."
"4849","Abu Burayd Amr ibn Yazid narrated it to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim that he heard Tawus saying: Ibn Abbas used to say: It is of the Sunnah to place one's buttocks upon one's heels between the two prostrations, meaning iqa. And we do not know anyone narrating this hadith from Abd al-Karim except Zakariyya ibn Ishaq, and he is a trustworthy Makkan."
"4850","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, meaning Ibn Artah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umra (a lifetime grant) belongs to the one to whom it is granted, and ruqba belongs to the one to whom it is granted, and the one who takes back his gift is like the one who returns to his vomit. And I think he said: And it is not lawful for anyone to give a gift and then take it back, except a father in what he gives his child. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas except from this angle with this isnad. This hadith has been narrated by more than one from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for anyone to give a gift and then take it back, except a father in what he gives his child. And this isnad is among the best of what is narrated in that; al-Hajjaj is well-known, except that he is a man given to tadlis, and we do not know anyone abandoning his hadith, and he was a memorizer. As for Abu al-Zubayr, many people narrated from him from Basra, Kufah, Makkah and Madinah, and we do not know anyone abandoning his hadith, and those above them need no mention due to their eminence."
"4851","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled in Ramadan and fasted until he reached Usfan, then he called for a vessel of water in the daytime to show the people, then he broke his fast. He said: So Ibn Abbas used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted while traveling and broke his fast; so whoever wishes may fast, and whoever wishes may break his fast. And this hadith has been narrated from Ibn Abbas and from others than Ibn Abbas, so we sufficed with this isnad, and it is a sound, elevated isnad."
"4852","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the conquest: There is no migration after today, but jihad and intention, and when you are called to mobilize, then mobilize. And this isnad with this wording we do not know anyone narrating it except Ibn Abbas, and this isnad is the best isnad narrated in that from Ibn Abbas."
"4853","Amr ibn Ali and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib narrated to us, they said: Waki narrated to us, from al-Amash, he said: I heard Mujahid narrating from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by two graves and said: They are being punished, and they are not being punished for something major. As for this one, he used to walk about with slander, and as for this one, he would not guard himself from his urine. Then he called for a moist palm stalk and placed one upon this one and one upon that one, then said: Perhaps it will be lightened for them so long as they do not dry."
"4854","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated it to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, and Tawus was not mentioned between Mujahid and Ibn Abbas."
"4855","And al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jahdam narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Habib ibn Hassan, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4856","And Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated it to us, he said: Sufyan informed me, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, and he did not say: from Ibn Abbas. We only mentioned the hadith of Suhayl from Habib ibn Hassan because Suhayl did not narrate from Habib any hadith other than this one, and we mentioned the hadith of Amr from Tawus lest someone say it is from Ibn Abbas, so we clarified that it is not from Ibn Abbas. And we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, except Waki."
"4857","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman used to pray the two Eids before the sermon. And this hadith is narrated from Ibn Abbas from other than this angle, and this isnad is the best isnad narrated from Ibn Abbas in that, and it is a sound isnad with no disagreement in it, and al-Hasan ibn Muslim is among the trustworthy, reliable Makkans."
"4858","Muhammad ibn Umar ibn al-Hayyaj narrated to us, he said: Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim ibn Yannaq, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prescribed two rakahs in travel and four in residence. Ibn Abbas said: So just as you pray after it and before it in residence, so pray before it and after it in travel. And he is Usamah ibn Zayd al-Laythi, a trustworthy Madinan, and the other is Usamah ibn Zayd ibn Aslam; and Usamah ibn Zayd al-Laythi is more established than Usamah ibn Zayd."
"4859","And al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Jarawi narrated it to us, he said: Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai narrated to me, from Usamah ibn Zayd al-Laythi, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), likewise. And this hadith has been narrated from Ibn Abbas similarly from other than this angle and with other than this wording, and this isnad is better and sounder than the other isnad narrated from him, and we do not know al-Awzai narrated from Usamah ibn Zayd al-Laythi, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, any hadith except this one."
"4860","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Circumambulation around the House is like prayer, except that you speak therein; so whoever speaks therein, let him not speak except good. And we do not know anyone narrating this hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Ibn Abbas, and we do not know Ata ibn al-Saib narrated from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, any hadith other than this one. It was narrated by more than one as mawquf, and Jarir and Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated it as marfu. And we do not know anyone abandoning the hadith of Ata ibn al-Saib, for Ata is a trustworthy, well-known Kufan, but he had changed (in memory), so his hadith became confused."
"4861","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Hanzalah, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The measure is the measure of the people of Makkah, and the scale is the scale of the people of Madinah. And we do not know anyone narrating this hadith except Hanzalah from Tawus, nor do we know anyone narrated it except al-Thawri. And al-Firyabi said: from al-Thawri, from Hanzalah, from Tawus, from Ibn Umar. This hadith was narrated by Hanzalah from Tawus, and Hanzalah is trustworthy, and none narrated it from Hanzalah except al-Thawri. They differed upon al-Thawri: Abu Ahmad said: from al-Thawri, from Hanzalah, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas; and al-Firyabi said: from al-Thawri, from Hanzalah, from Tawus, from Ibn Umar. None narrated it except al-Thawri, and Hanzalah is a Makkan of sound hadith."
"4862","Sulayman ibn Sayf al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Waqid al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Hanzalah narrated to us, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: I accept prayer only from one who humbles himself therein due to My greatness, does not exalt himself over My creation, does not persist overnight upon disobedience to Me, spends his day in My remembrance, shows mercy to the poor, the wayfarer, the widow, and shows mercy to the afflicted. His light is like the light of the sun; I protect him by My might and entrust him to My angels. I make for him light in darkness and forbearance in ignorance, and his likeness among My creation is like al-Firdaws in Paradise. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except from this angle with this isnad. Abdullah ibn Waqid was not a memorizer, yet many people of knowledge narrated from him. Abdullah ibn Waqid was a Harranian, chaste, a memorizer learned in the opinion of Abu Hanifah, and he would err and be prompted with the correct, yet not return. He was kunyated Abu Qatadah, and he was a judge."
"4863","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: al-Ala ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Nothing like marriage has been seen for two who love one another."
"4864","Ziyad ibn Yahya al-Hassani narrated to us, he said: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing like marriage has been seen for two who love one another."
"4865","And Ahmad ibn Aban narrated it to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Tawus, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not say: from Ibn Abbas. The hadith is only well-known from Muhammad ibn Muslim, from Ibrahim, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). As for the hadith of Muammal, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Thawri as connected except him, from what has reached us from a trustworthy man. He said: Abu Bakr, meaning for two who love, meaning: when a man loves a woman, he ought to marry her."
"4866","Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed me, from Sulayman al-Ahwal, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed tahajjud at night, he would say: O Allah, to You is praise; You are the Light of the heavens and the earth and all therein, and to You is praise; You are the Sustainer of the heavens and the earth and all therein, and to You is praise; You are the Truth, Your promise is the truth, meeting You is true, Paradise is true, and the Hour is true. O Allah, to You I submit, in You I believe, upon You I rely, to You I turn, by You I dispute, and to You I refer judgment. O Allah, forgive me what I have done before and after, in secret and in public. You are the Advancer and You are the Delayer; there is no god but You, and there is no power nor strength except by You. We only mentioned this hadith, though Abu al-Zubayr narrated it from Tawus, because the wording of the hadith of Sulayman differs from that one, and in it is an addition not in the hadith of Abu al-Zubayr."
"4867","Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed me, from Sulayman al-Ahwal, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: People used to depart from every direction, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none depart until his last encounter is with the House. This hadith has been narrated from Ibn Abbas and from Ibn Umar with something close to it, and women were given concession in the hadith of Ibn Umar. We mentioned the hadith of Sulayman al-Ahwal and sufficed with it over what is narrated in that from Ibn Abbas with other than this isnad."
"4868","Bishr ibn Adam and Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Ubaydah al-Usfuri narrated to us, they said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Ahwal, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man who had pierced his nose."
"4869","Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Jabir al-Jufi, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the Eid without adhan or iqamah. This hadith has been narrated from Ibn Abbas and from others than Ibn Abbas, and we do not know Jabir al-Jufi narrated from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, any hadith other than this one. Jabir al-Jufi is not strong, though trustworthy narrators narrated from him, among them: Shubah, al-Thawri, Israil, Zuhayr, Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, Abu Awanah, Hushaym, Ibn Uyaynah and others. What was held against him was a view by which he opposed the people of his time; it is mentioned that he held the return of Ali. He was a Kufan. These (scholars) bore his hadith and knew him. It is not necessary that when he narrates a hadith containing a ruling, it be used as proof."
"4870","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Mujammi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Karim narrated to us, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a woman in her litter with a child with her. She took the child in her hands and said: O Messenger of Allah, is there Hajj for this one? He said: Yes, and for you is reward."
"4871","Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed me, from Ibrahim ibn Uqbah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that a woman lifted a child and said: O Messenger of Allah, is there Hajj for this one? He said: Yes, and for you is reward. Abd al-Rahman said: Sufyan narrated it to us, from Ibrahim ibn Uqbah, from Kurayb, and he did not say: from Ibn Abbas. This hadith is narrated from Ibn Abbas from these angles, and we do not know it narrated from Tawus except from Abd al-Karim, from Tawus. We do not know anyone narrated it from Abd al-Karim except Ibrahim ibn Ismail, and he is lenient."
"4872","And Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Aban ibn Yazid al-Attar narrated to us, from Amr, meaning Ibn Dinar, and Abd al-Karim, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to prostrate upon seven, and not to gather hair or garment. We only mentioned this hadith, though we had mentioned it from Amr, because Aban combined Amr and Abd al-Karim, and we do not know it narrated from Abd al-Karim except from this angle, so for that we mentioned it."
"4873","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Thabit ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, when the sun eclipsed, eight rakahs and four prostrations, reciting in each rakah. We only mentioned this hadith because we do not know Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, any hadith other than this one, and its isnad is sound. Thabit ibn Muhammad is a Kufan, and he was called al-Zahid."
"4874","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabuwayh al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Haywah ibn Shurayh ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah narrated to us, from al-Masudi, from al-Hakam, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Muadh to Yemen, he commanded him to take from every thirty cattle a tabi or tabiah, a jadha or jadhah, and from every forty cattle a musinnah cow. They said: What of the awqas? He said: He did not command me anything concerning them; I shall ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when I arrive. When he arrived before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he asked him, and he said: There is nothing in them. al-Masudi said: Al-awqas is what is between thirty and forty, and forty and sixty. This hadith is only narrated by the memorizers from al-Hakam, from Tawus, as mursal. We do not know anyone saying: from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, except Baqiyyah from al-Masudi, and none followed Baqiyyah from al-Masudi upon this hadith. Al-Hasan ibn Umarah narrated it from al-Hakam, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, but the hadith of al-Hasan ibn Umarah is not used as proof when he is alone with a hadith."
"4875","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from Ata ibn Ajlan, from al-Mughirah ibn Hakim, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever washes and bathes on Friday, then draws near where he hears the imam's sermon, and when he comes out listens and is silent until he prays it with him, there is written for him, for every step he takes, the worship of a year, its standing and its fasting. We do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except from this angle. Ata ibn Ajlan is not strong in hadith, and al-Mughirah ibn Hakim is trustworthy. We do not know al-Mughirah ibn Hakim narrated from Tawus any hadith other than this one. Ata ibn Ajlan is a Basran; a group narrated from him: Hammad ibn Salamah, Ismail ibn Ayyash, Marwan ibn Muawiyah and many others. He is called Ata al-Attar, and he is not a memorizer."
"4876","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amir ibn Musab, from Tawus, he said: A man asked Ibn Abbas about the two rakahs after Asr, so he said: It is not for a believing man or woman, when Allah and His Messenger have decreed a matter, to have a choice in their matter. We only mentioned this hadith because its meaning is that he forbade the two rakahs after Asr."
"4877","And Abd al-Ala ibn Zayd al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hujayr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, likewise. We do not know Amir ibn Musab narrated from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, any hadith other than this one, nor did anyone narrate it from him except Ibn Jurayj. Nor did Hisham ibn Hujayr narrate from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, any hadith other than this one, nor do we know anyone narrated it from him except Sufyan ibn Uyaynah."
"4878","Abdullah ibn Said al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Teach, make easy and do not make difficult; and when you are angry, be silent."
"4879","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated it to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), likewise. We do not know these words narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle, except a hadith whose isnad has been differed upon. Layth ibn Abi Sulaym is a Kufan worshipper; the people of Kufah narrated from him and bore his hadith."
"4880","Abdullah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, Mujahid and Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed tamattu, as did Abu Bakr and Umar, and the first to forbid it was Muawiyah."
"4881","And Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated it to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Sharik, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), likewise. We do not know anyone narrating this hadith with this wording except Ibn Abbas, nor do we know for it a path from Ibn Abbas except this path. Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah and others narrated from Ibn Abbas concerning the tamattu of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with other than this wording."
"4882","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Maymun ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that he never saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) break his fast on a Friday ever. We do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas except from this angle, though it has been narrated from others than Ibn Abbas with other than this wording."
"4883","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Maymun ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Layth, meaning Ibn Abi Sulaym, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The evil eye is true, and if you are asked to wash, then wash. We do not know these words narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except from this angle with this isnad. Maymun ibn Zayd is a Basran in whom there is no harm."
"4884","Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Ammi narrated to us, he said: Mualla ibn Asad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made his companions partners on the day of Hudaybiyah, seven to a cow. We do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas with this wording from this angle, though it has been narrated from Jabir and others with different wordings."
"4885","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Mualla narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am holding your waistbands, saying: Beware of the Fire. I am going, and I shall precede you at the Hawd. Some people will be brought and seized to the left, so I shall say: O Lord. It will be said: They kept turning back upon their heels. We do not know this hadith narrated except from Ibn Abbas with this wording. They differed upon Layth: others than Abd al-Wahid narrated it from Layth, from Abd al-Malik ibn Said ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Ibn Abbas. Something like his words has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from more than one angle, but we do not know these words narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle."
"4886","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, or Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, raising it, he said: Two greedy ones are never satisfied: a seeker of knowledge and a seeker of the world. Layth had been afflicted with something like confusion, though that was not established from him, yet a softness remained in his hadith for that reason. We do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from an angle better than this one."
"4887","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, and from Nafi, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Five, all of them harmful, the muhrim kills them: the mouse, the kite, the crow, the scorpion, and the voracious dog. We do not know this hadith with this wording narrated from Ibn Abbas except from this angle, though it has been narrated from others than Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4888","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Sharik, from Layth, from Ata and Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Umm Salamah ahead from Jam at night from Muzdalifah. Ibn Abbas said: And I was with them. These words have been narrated similarly with other than its wording, from Ibn Abbas and from others than Ibn Abbas, but we do not know this wording narrated except from Ibn Abbas from this angle."
"4889","Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the grandmother a sixth. We do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas except from this angle, nor do we know anyone narrated it from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, except Sharik. Others than Sharik narrated it from Layth, from Ibn Hubayrah, from Abu Hurayrah."
"4890","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Zuhr and Asr at Arafat. Ibrahim ibn Tahman was originally a Kufan and moved to Khurasan. We do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas from a path better than this one."
"4891","al-Abbas ibn Jafar al-Hashimi narrated to us, he said: Abu Shaykh al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to call the Farewell Hajj the Hajj of Islam. We do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle, nor do we know anyone narrated it from Layth except Musa ibn Ayan. Musa ibn Ayan is a trustworthy Harranian."
"4892","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give the prescribed shares to their rightful owners; what remains is for the nearest male relative. We do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle; we do not know anyone narrated it from him except Ibn Abbas."
"4893","Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ziyad ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), likewise. I know of no defect in this isnad. Wuhayb is a well-known Basran memorizer, and the rest of the isnad need no commendation due to their fame and trustworthiness."
"4894","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of a house called the bathhouse. They said: O Messenger of Allah, it removes dirt. He said: Then cover yourselves. This hadith is only narrated by people from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as mursal. We do not know anyone saying therein: from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except Yusuf from Yala from al-Thawri. Others than Yusuf narrated it from Yala from al-Thawri, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4895","Abu Talhah al-Khuzai Musa ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while fasting, and used snuff. This hadith has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from various angles that he was cupped while fasting, and narrated from Ibn Abbas as well from various angles. We do not know anyone saying: and used snuff, except from this angle. Wuhayb is trustworthy and a memorizer."
"4896","Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not a townsman sell for a Bedouin."
"4897","And Yahya ibn Hakim narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), likewise. Mamar said: I said to Ibn Tawus: What is the meaning of: Let not a townsman sell for a Bedouin? He said: He should not be a broker for him. We do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas except from this angle, though it has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from various angles with different wordings."
"4898","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Mualla ibn Asad narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed for the people of Madinah Dhu al-Hulayfah, for the people of Sham al-Juhfah, for the people of Najd Qarn, and for the people of Yemen Yalamlam, and said: They are for them and for whoever comes upon them from other than their people, for whoever intends Hajj and Umrah; and whoever's family is before the miqat, then from where he begins. We do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except from this angle, with this isnad, by the narration of Ibn Tawus from his father from Ibn Abbas."
"4899","Uqbah ibn Mukram and al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, they said: Umar ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of Hell, the punishment of the grave, the trial of the Dajjal, the trial of life and the trial of death. We do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas with this wording with an isnad better than this isnad."
"4900","And of what Mujahid narrated from Ibn Abbas: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was aided by al-Saba (the easterly wind), and Ad were destroyed by al-Dabur (the westerly wind)."
"4901","And Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated it to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), likewise. This hadith has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and narrated from Ibn Abbas through various paths, so we mentioned these two paths and sufficed with them. We do not know anyone narrated the hadith of Abu Bishr from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas except Uthman ibn Umar; others than Uthman narrated it from Abu Bishr from Said ibn Jubayr as mursal."
"4902","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I passed in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon a donkey while he was praying with the people, and none repeated that prayer on account of that. This hadith was narrated by more than one from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Ibn Abbas. Some said: from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Suhayb, from Ibn Abbas. Ismail ibn Muslim is lenient in hadith; he is a Basran, attributed and called Ismail al-Makki, but he settled in Basra so was attributed to it. Al-Amash, al-Thawri and others narrated from him. This hadith was narrated by others from al-Hakam with other than his isnad."
"4903","al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Zafarani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: When this verse was revealed: So judge between them or turn away from them, he said: So he was given a choice: if he wished he judged, and if he wished he turned away from them and referred them to their laws. He said: Then was revealed: And judge between them by what Allah has revealed and do not follow their desires. He said: So he was commanded to judge between them by what is in our Book. This hadith has been narrated from Ibn Abbas from more than one angle, so we sufficed with this isnad from them, and the isnad is sound. Sufyan ibn Husayn is a trustworthy Wasiti, Abbad ibn al-Awwam is a trustworthy Wasiti, and Said ibn Sulayman is a Wasiti who moved to Baghdad, among the trustworthy."
"4904","Abdullah ibn Said Abu Said al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid Sulayman ibn Hayyan, a trustworthy Kufan, narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Hakam, and Muslim al-Batin, a trustworthy Kufan, from Said ibn Jubayr, Ata and Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My mother died owing two consecutive months of fasting. He said: Tell me, if she owed a debt, would you settle it? She said: Yes. He said: So the right of Allah is more deserving. We do not know this hadith narrated from al-Hakam from Mujahid except from this angle, nor do we know anyone narrated it except Abu Khalid from al-Amash, nor do we know anyone followed Abu Khalid upon this isnad and these words."
"4905","Musa ibn Ishaq ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jubarah ibn al-Mughallis narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Uthman narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the expedition of Tabuk: Fight, you will gain the daughters of the yellow ones. Some hypocrites said: He tempts you with women. He said: So Allah revealed: Among them is he who says: Grant me leave and do not tempt me, to the end of the verse. We do not know this hadith narrated except from Ibn Abbas, nor do we know for it a path other than this path. Ibrahim ibn Uthman is lenient in hadith, and we only mention of his hadith what we do not memorize except from him."
"4906","Musa ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Jubarah ibn al-Mughallis narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Uthman narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Ali and Khalid ibn al-Walid, appointing Ali over the Muhajirun and Ansar, and appointing Khalid ibn al-Walid over the Bedouins, and said: If there is fighting, the command of the people is to Ali. This hadith has been narrated similarly from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from various angles with different wordings, but we do not know it narrated from Ibn Abbas except from this angle. We have already mentioned Ibrahim ibn Uthman, so sufficed from repeating his mention thereafter. Jubarah ibn al-Mughallis is a Kufan Himmani; he had grown old and had been prompted with hadiths, so he was prompted, and his hadith is for that reason. Ibrahim ibn Uthman is the grandfather of Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah; he was a Kufan of poor memory."
"4907","al-Hasan ibn Qazaah narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is not present in the source row; only the isnad is given.]"
"4908","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated it to us, he said: Jarir and Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, the wording being Jarir's, they said: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was given five that no prophet before me was given: I was sent to the red and the black, while those before me were sent to their people; the earth was made for me a mosque and a purifier; I was aided by awe ahead of me a month's journey; spoils were made lawful for me and were not lawful for anyone before me; and I was given intercession, and I delayed it for my ummah, and it will reach whoever does not associate anything with Allah. We do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas except from these two angles, from Mujahid from Ibn Abbas. Some of those who narrated to us from Ibn Fudayl added: from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid and Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas. As for the hadith of al-Hakam, we do not know anyone narrated it except Ibn Abi Layla from him. This hadith from al-Hakam from Mujahid has been contradicted: al-Amash narrated it from Mujahid, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Abu Dharr; Wasil al-Ahdab narrated it from Mujahid, from Abu Dharr; and Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated it from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar."
"4909","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Qutbah ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Yahya al-Qattat, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade inciting beasts against one another. This hadith was narrated by others than Qutbah from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, without mentioning Abu Yahya. Al-Thawri narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Yahya, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, as mawquf. But I heard Musa ibn Ishaq mentioning it from Abu Khaythamah, from Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Abu Yahya, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I heard Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi mentioning it from Ziyad ibn Abdullah al-Amiri, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Minhal, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ziyad erred therein; al-Minhal only narrated it from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4910","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Yahya, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among you is unable for the night to endure it, is miserly with wealth to spend it, and is cowardly toward the enemy to fight him, then let him increase the remembrance of Allah. We do not know this hadith narrated except from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor do we know for it a path from Ibn Abbas except this path. As for Abu Yahya, we know of no harm in him; a group of people of knowledge narrated from him, and he is a well-known Kufan."
"4911","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Yahya, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man and saw his thigh exposed, so he said: Cover your thigh, for a man's thigh is part of his awrah. This hadith has been narrated from Jarhad from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and from others, but we do not know it narrated from Ibn Abbas except from this angle."
"4912","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Yahya, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not for anyone to say: I am better with Allah than Yunus ibn Matta. We do not know these words narrated with this wording except from Ibn Abbas from this angle. It has been narrated from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not for a servant to say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta. So we mentioned each hadith with its wording in its place."
"4913","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Yahya, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Most of the punishment of the grave is from urine, so guard yourselves from urine. Something like his words has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from more than one angle with different wordings, so we mentioned each hadith from them in its place with its wording."
"4914","Muhammad ibn Muawiyah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: O Allah, forgive those who shave. They said: And those who shorten? He said, on the third or fourth: And those who shorten."
"4915","And al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Rashid narrated it to us, he said: Hushaym informed me, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, or Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), likewise. These words have been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from various angles, and the best path narrated in that from Ibn Abbas is what Ibn Abi Najih narrated from Mujahid from Ibn Abbas."
"4916","Abu Salamah Yahya ibn Khalaf narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gifted one hundred camels, among them a camel of Abu Jahl with a silver nose-ring in its nose."
"4917","And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated it to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: I read to Ibn Ishaq, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), likewise. This hadith has been narrated from Ibn Abbas from more than one angle; Miqsam and others narrated it from Ibn Abbas, and the hadith of Ibn Abi Najih from Mujahid is better in origin than the hadith of Miqsam."
"4918","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Aban ibn Salih and Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed three days in Umrat al-Qada. We do not know this act narrated except from Ibn Abbas, and it is of sound path from him."
"4919","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabuwayh and Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, they said: Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar approaching pregnant women, and said: Do not water another's crop. He forbade selling spoils before they are divided, eating domestic donkeys, and every fanged beast of prey. Some of these words have been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from more than one angle, and some we do not memorize from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from a sound angle except from this angle."
"4920","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar the meat of jallalah donkeys, and looting."
"4921","And Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated it to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar the meat of domestic donkeys, pregnant captives being approached until they deliver what is in their wombs, and every fanged beast of prey. As for the hadith of Layth, jallalah donkeys are mentioned therein, and we do not know it narrated in the hadith of any other from Mujahid from Ibn Abbas. It has been narrated from Mujahid from Ibn Umar. As for the hadith of al-Amash, something like its words has been narrated from Ibn Abbas with other than this wording, and we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Amash except Shayban and Sharik."
"4922","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Sinan narrated to us, he said: Yaqub al-Qummi narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is not present in the source row; only the isnad is given.]"
"4923","And Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, he said: Yaqub al-Qummi narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Be cupped on the seventeenth, nineteenth, or twenty-first, lest the blood rage in you and kill you. We do not know this hadith narrated except from Ibn Abbas. It has been narrated from Abbad ibn Mansur, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas. Yaqub, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas is better than the hadith of Abbad from Ikrimah, for Abbad did not hear from Ikrimah."
"4924","Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Yaqub, meaning al-Qummi, narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If there is healing in any of your medicines, it is in the cupper's incision and a draught of honey. We do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas from a sound angle better than this angle."
"4925","Muhammad ibn Muawiyah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have two ministers from the people of heaven and two ministers from the people of earth. As for my two ministers from the people of heaven, they are Jibril and Mikail; and as for my two ministers from the people of earth, they are Abu Bakr and Umar. We do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas except from this angle. Abd al-Rahman ibn Malik is lenient in hadith, though a group of people of knowledge narrated from him and bore his hadith, for he was a man of the Sunnah."
"4926","Musa ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of the conquest the meat of jallalah animals, their milk, and their backs. We only mentioned this hadith and clarified it because Hassan added therein, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, what is not in the hadith of others. Hassan is trustworthy, so due to the addition we mentioned this hadith."
"4927","Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Haddad narrated to us, or some of our companions narrated to us from him, he said: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Abu Kudaynah, whose name is Yahya ibn al-Muhallab, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I saw Jibril (peace be upon him) twice, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for me for wisdom twice. Some of these words have been narrated from Ibn Abbas, but we do not know for it a path with this wording better than this path."
"4928","Musa ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Aban ibn Salih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has angels on earth besides the guardians who write what falls of tree leaves. So when one of you suffers lameness in a desert land, let him call out: Help, O servants of Allah. We do not know these words narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except from this angle with this isnad."
"4929","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah and Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Haddadi narrated to us, they said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Israil, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that he said: Which of the two readings do you see was last? They said: The reading of Zayd. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to review the Quran with Jibril every year; in the year in which he died, he reviewed it with him twice. So the reading of Ibn Masud was the last, or the latter of them. This hadith has been narrated similarly from more than one angle with different wordings, but we do not know it narrated from Ibn Abbas with this wording except from this angle with this isnad."
"4930","al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said to al-Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): Accept Islam, for by Allah, your accepting Islam is dearer to me than al-Khattab's accepting Islam, and that is only because he was dearer to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So accept Islam; your precedence be yours. This hadith has been narrated from Mujahid that Umar said it, but we do not know anyone saying: from Israil, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, except Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban. He was not strong, but since these words were not memorized except from this angle, we found no alternative to bringing it out and clarifying the defect therein."
"4931","4925 - Bishr ibn Mu'adh al-'Aqadi narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: Allah obligated the prayer upon the tongue of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): four rak'ahs in residence, two rak'ahs while traveling, and one rak'ah in fear, in similar wording. And we do not know anyone who mentioned this hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Ibn 'Abbas, and we do not know for it any chain other than this chain, and we do not know that Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas narrated from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, any hadith other than this one."
"4932","4926 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Verily Makkah is sacred; Allah made it sacred on the day He created the heavens and the earth and the sun and the moon. It was not lawful for anyone before me, nor is it lawful for anyone after me, and it was not made lawful for me except for an hour of the day, then it returned. Its herbage is not to be uprooted, its trees are not to be cut, its game is not to be frightened, and its lost property is not to be picked up except by one who announces it. Al-'Abbas said: Except al-idhkhir, O Messenger of Allah, for the people of Makkah cannot do without it. He said: Except al-idhkhir. And this hadith has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas through other chains, and from other than Ibn 'Abbas with different wordings whose meanings are close, and in this hadith there are wordings not found in any other hadith, so we mentioned it for that reason. And Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, we have already mentioned regarding other than this hadith that he is not strong, and we do not know any of the hadith scholars who abandoned his hadith, neither Shu'bah nor al-Thawri nor any of the people of knowledge; rather he was afflicted because there was weakness in his memory."
"4933","4927 - And Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Samurah narrated to us, he said: al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn 'A'idh, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas."
"4934","4928 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived with his Companions as pilgrims, and when he arrived he said: O people, release your ihram; had I known beforehand what I now know afterward, I would not have done this. 'Umrah has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection. And this hadith has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas and from other than Ibn 'Abbas with different wordings, so we mentioned each hadith among them in its place with its wording."
"4935","4929 - 'Ali ibn Sa'id al-Masruqi narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade these vessels, then he permitted them. He forbade the dried gourd, the green jar, the hollowed palm-stump, and the tar-coated vessel, then he permitted them. He said: Drink in whatever you wish, but avoid every intoxicant. And he forbade visiting graves, then he said: Visit them, for in them there is admonition. And he forbade eating sacrificial meat beyond three days, then he permitted it. Mujahid said: 'A'ishah said: We would still have the meat of the sacrifices remaining with us after ten days. And this hadith has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through more than one chain, and in this hadith there is a wording not found in the hadith of anyone else, which is: Visit them, for in them there is admonition; so we mentioned it for that reason."
"4936","4930 - 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, in a raised report, that he said: There are no days in which righteous deeds are better than in these days, meaning the ten days, for they are days of tahlil and takbir. And it has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas with other than this wording regarding the virtue of the ten days, so we mentioned each hadith with its wording in its place. And Abu 'Awanah narrated from Yazid, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Umar."
"4937","4931 - Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Shuja' narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Mujahid and 'Ikrimah and 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, raising the hadith, he said: A menstruating woman enters ihram and performs all the rites except that she does not circumambulate the House until she becomes pure. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated with this wording except from Ibn 'Abbas, and something similar has been narrated from other than Ibn 'Abbas, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Khusayf except Marwan ibn Shuja', and he is a shaykh against whom there is no harm."
"4938","4932 - Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, he said: 'Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: No habitual drinker of wine will enter Paradise, nor a disobedient child, nor one who reminds others of his favors. And this hadith was narrated by other than Rawh from 'Attab, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, without saying: from Ibn 'Abbas, and it has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through more than one chain."
"4939","4933 - 'Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Khuza'i narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to our house, so I handed him a bucket and he drank, then he rinsed his mouth back into the bucket. And this hadith has been narrated from other than Ibn 'Abbas, and it is not narrated from Ibn 'Abbas except through this chain, and we do not know that Qays ibn Sa'd reported from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, any hadith other than this one."
"4940","4934 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Sulayman, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: {O you who believe, fear Allah as He deserves to be feared}, he said: If a drop of zaqqum were to drip upon the earth, it would spoil their livelihood for them, so how about one who has no food besides it. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Ibn 'Abbas with this wording, and we do not know for it any chain other than this."
"4941","4935 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray facing Bayt al-Maqdis with the Ka'bah before him, and after he emigrated to Madinah for sixteen months. And with this wording we do not know anyone who narrated it except al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-A'mash except Abu 'Awanah."
"4942","4936 - Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Shayban, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar the meat of domestic donkeys, and pregnant women being approached in intercourse until they give birth, meaning what is in their wombs, and every predator with fangs, and selling the fifth before it is divided."
"4943","4937 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari and Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Baghdadi narrated to us, they said: 'Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Jabir, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever calls the adhan for seven years seeking reward, a clearance from the Fire is written for him. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from Ibn 'Abbas except through this chain, nor do we retain anything from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from other than Ibn 'Abbas, and we do not know that Jabir reported from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, anything other than this."
"4944","4938 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Muslim al-Mula'i, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that you would become weak, I would have commanded you to use the siwak at every prayer."
"4945","4939 - And 'Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Muslim, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in similar wording. And this hadith has been narrated with similar wording from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through more than one chain with other than this wording, and we do not retain it from Ibn 'Abbas with this wording except through this chain with this isnad. And Muslim al-Mula'i, there is no harm in him; Shu'bah and al-Thawri and al-A'mash and Isra'il and a large group narrated from him, and they accepted his hadith."
"4946","4940 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Muslim, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: There was a freed slave woman of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who would fast during the day, and it was said to him: She fasts during the day and stands at night. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Verily every action has a zeal, and zeal leads to a slackening, so whoever's slackening is toward my Sunnah has been guided, and whoever's slackening is toward other than that has gone astray. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated except from Ibn 'Abbas, and we do not know for it a chain from Ibn 'Abbas with this wording except from Muslim, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas."
"4947","4941 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Warqa' narrated to us, from Muslim, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was aided by the east wind, and 'Ad were destroyed by the west wind, and nothing was sent upon them except like a signet ring. And we have already mentioned this hadith from Mujahid and Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I was aided by the east wind, and 'Ad were destroyed by the west wind. And Muslim added, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas: And nothing was sent upon them except like a signet ring; so we mentioned it only because of the addition. And this wording is only retained from Ibn 'Abbas as a stopped report. Al-Minhal narrated it from Sa'id, from Ibn 'Abbas, and Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, and we do not know anyone who raised it except Muslim."
"4948","4942 - al-Sakan ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Amir 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Amr narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Muslim, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A group of Jews came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: If he informs us of what we ask him about, then he is a prophet. They said: From where does resemblance come, O Muhammad? He said: The man's fluid is thick and the woman's fluid is yellow and thin, so whichever of them overcomes its companion, the resemblance belongs to it, and if they combine, it is from both of them. They said: You have spoken the truth. And something similar to this hadith has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through various chains, and in the hadith of Ibn 'Abbas there is an addition not found in the hadith of others, and we do not know it to be narrated from Ibn 'Abbas except through this chain."
"4949","4943 - 'Abdullah ibn Ayyub al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Mula'i narrated to us, from Muslim, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted in the month of Ramadan one day until nightfall, and when the next day came he fasted until the afternoon, and it was said to him: Fasting has exhausted the people, so he called for water and drank."
"4950","4944 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated it to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Muslim, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed 'umrah in the month of Ramadan. And the hadith of Muslim, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, about the fasting of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the month of Ramadan and his breaking the fast was only about traveling, and it has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas through other than this chain with other than this wording and other than this isnad."
"4951","4945 - Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Ibn Raja' narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Muslim, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bathe behind the rooms, and his private parts were never seen at all. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through a connected chain better than this isnad."
"4952","4946 - Bishr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Raja' narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Muslim, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): {O Prophet, why do you prohibit what Allah has made lawful for you}. He said: This was revealed concerning his concubine. And this hadith has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas through another chain."
"4953","4947 - Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan al-Wasiti narrated it to us, he said: 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Salim al-Aftas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, in similar wording. And we do not know it to have been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas as connected except through these two chains."
"4954","4948 - Musa ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: 'Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Muslim, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding the statement of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: {And those of your women who commit indecency}, he said: They used to be confined in houses until they died, then when Surah al-Nur was revealed and the prescribed punishments were revealed, it abrogated it. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated with this wording except from Ibn 'Abbas, and it has been narrated with other than this wording from 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit."
"4955","4949 - Musa ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyabi narrated to us, he said: al-'Abbas ibn Abi Shamlah narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhubab, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him, his family has become lawful for him. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this chain with this isnad, and al-'Abbas ibn Abi Shamlah is a Madinan, and al-Harith ibn Abi 'Abd al-Rahman narrated more than one hadith from Mujahid."
"4956","4950 - Ja'far ibn Ahmad, nephew of Waki' ibn al-Jarrah, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that he recited Surah Sad and prostrated in it, then he said: {Those are they whom Allah guided, so follow their guidance}, and what prevents him from prostrating in it when Allah has narrated to him the Prophets. And this hadith was narrated by Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham from Shayban, from Jabir al-Ju'fi, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his house while he was reciting Surah Sad and he prostrated in it. And Ibn 'Abbas said: And what prevents him from prostrating in it when Allah has narrated to him the Prophets, and he mentioned among them Dawud, then he said: {Those are they whom Allah guided, so follow their guidance}. And 'Amr did not narrate from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, except this hadith."
"4957","4951 - Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: 'Abd al-Karim informed me that Mujahid informed him, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: Al-Fadl and I came upon a she-donkey, and we passed in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at 'Arafah while he was praying the obligatory prayer, with nothing screening him, passing between him and him. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated except from Ibn 'Abbas, and it has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas through more than one chain with various wordings, so we mentioned each hadith among them with its wording in its place."
"4958","4952 - Mahmud ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from 'Isa ibn al-Mukhtar, from Ibn Abi Layla, from 'Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been forbidden to pray toward sleepers and those talking. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated except from Ibn 'Abbas, and it is narrated from him through two chains, and this chain is the better of the two chains narrated from him."
"4959","4953 - Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan, meaning Ibn 'Uyaynah, informed us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from 'Ata', and Ibn Jurayj from 'Ata', both from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the 'Isha prayer until as much of the night had passed as Allah willed, so 'Umar said to him: The women and children have slept. So he came out saying: Were it not that I would impose hardship on my Ummah, I would have commanded them to pray at this hour. And this hadith has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas and from others with different wordings, so we mentioned each hadith among them in its place with its wording."
"4960","4954 - Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from 'Amr, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he ate food, would lick his fingers. And this hadith has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through more than one chain, and this isnad is among the best isnads narrated in that."
"4961","4955 - Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from 'Amr, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Muslims caught up with a man with a small flock of sheep of his; he greeted them with peace, but they killed him and took his flock. So Allah revealed: {And do not say to one who offers you peace: You are not a believer, seeking the fleeting goods of worldly life} - the flock. And this hadith has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas through other than this chain, and this chain is the best chain narrated from him in that."
"4962","4956 - Ahmad ibn Bakkar al-Bahili narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from 'Amr, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me ahead at night from Muzdalifah among the weak of his family. And this hadith has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas through various chains with different wordings, each of them adding over his companion, so we mentioned each hadith among them in its place with its wording."
"4963","4957 - And Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only walked briskly to show the polytheists his strength. And this hadith has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas through more than one chain, so we mentioned it in this place with this isnad due to the excellence of its isnad and the rarity of its chain."
"4964","4958 - Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from 'Amr, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), regarding the statement of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: {Have you not seen those who exchanged the favor of Allah for disbelief and settled their people in the house of ruin}, he said: They are the disbelievers of Quraysh, the people of Makkah who were killed on the day of Badr. And we only mentioned this hadith even though we did not mention in it anything from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), because we do not retain this statement from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); a Companion narrated it, so we mentioned it for that reason."
"4965","4959 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas."
"4966","4960 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas: {Those who avoid major sins and shameful deeds except lamam}, he said: Lamam is from fornication. And Ibn 'Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If You forgive, O Allah, You forgive abundantly, and which of Your servants has not committed lamam. And we do not know anyone who raised this hadith except Zakariyya ibn Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, and we do not know it to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through a connected chain except through this chain."
"4967","4961 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Ayyub informed me, he said: I heard 'Ata' narrating from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that he said: I bear witness regarding the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - or 'Ata' said: I bear witness regarding Ibn 'Abbas - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out on the day of Fitr or Adha, prayed, then delivered the sermon, then went to the women and commanded them to give charity, so they began to throw."
"4968","4962 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated it to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in similar wording."
"4969","4963 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: 'Asim ibn Hilal narrated to us, from Ayyub, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I bear witness regarding the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he delivered the sermon after the prayer, commanding us and forbidding us, and he thought he had not made the women hear, so he went to them with Bilal, admonished them, commanded and forbade them, and commanded them to give charity, and Bilal spread out his garment, so the woman began to throw the earring and the ring. And this hadith has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas through more than one chain with different wordings, and it was narrated from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, through other than this chain, and this chain is among the best chains narrated from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas."
"4970","4964 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-A'la ibn 'Abd al-A'la al-Sami narrated to us, he said: Hisham, meaning Ibn Hassan, narrated to us, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, would say: O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will of anything thereafter. And this hadith has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas through more than one chain, and they differed regarding Qays ibn Sa'd: some of those who narrated it from Qays said from 'Ata', and some of them said from Tawus, and the hadith is more resembling 'Ata'."
"4971","4965 - 'Uqbah ibn Mukram al-'Ammi and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar and al-Sakan ibn Sa'id narrated to us, they said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: I heard Qays ibn Sa'd narrating from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: al-'Abbas sent me to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in the house of Maymunah, my maternal aunt, so I spent that night with him. He stood to pray at night, so I stood, performed ablution, and stood to his left, so he took hold of me from behind his back and placed me at his right. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Qays ibn Sa'd except Jarir ibn Hazim, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Jarir except Wahb, his son."
"4972","4966 - 'Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Khuza'i narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that he said: Did you not know, O Zayd ibn Arqam, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was gifted a limb of game and he did not eat it, and he said: Verily we are in ihram. He said: Yes."
"4973","4967 - 'Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Khuza'i narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured forth from Muzdalifah, as I think, with Usamah behind him. And this hadith has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas through more than one chain that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took al-Fadl behind him, while the hadith of Qays says he took Usamah behind him, and we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Qays except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"4974","4968 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Baghdadi and 'Ali ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, they said: Aswad ibn 'Amir narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn 'Utbah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of uncertainty. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from Ibn 'Abbas except through this chain, and it has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Ayyub ibn 'Utbah."
"4975","4969 - al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Aswad ibn 'Amir narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn 'Utbah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from 'Ata' and 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah while he was in ihram. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from 'Ata', except through this chain, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yahya except Ayyub ibn 'Utbah, and it has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas through more than one chain."
"4976","4970 - Husayn ibn 'Ali ibn Ja'far al-Ahmar narrated to us, he said: Qabisah ibn 'Uqbah narrated to us, he said: Fitr narrated to us, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast. And we only mentioned this hadith to make clear the disagreement of people regarding 'Ata', for other than Qabisah narrated it from Fitr, from 'Ata', from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disconnected, and we do not know anyone who said from Ibn 'Abbas except Qabisah. 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman and Ibn Jurayj narrated it from 'Ata', from Abu Hurayrah as stopped, except Dawud ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, for he mentioned it from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata', from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Abu Hatim mentioned it from al-Ansari, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata', from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And no one followed him in reporting it from al-Ansari as raised, and Layth narrated it from 'Ata', from 'A'ishah; thus Khalid al-Wasiti and Shayban narrated it. And Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated it from Layth, from 'Ata', from 'Urwah ibn 'Iyad, from 'A'ishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Sallam Abu al-Mundhir narrated it from 'Ata', from Jabir ibn 'Abdullah. So we mentioned the hadith of Fitr to make clear this disagreement in it."
"4977","4971 - 'Uqbah ibn Mukram and Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari narrated to us, they said: Abu 'Amir 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Amr narrated to us, he said: Rabah ibn Abi Ma'ruf narrated to us, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4978","4972 - And Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Layth ibn Sa'd, from Abu al-Zubayr, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was cupped while in ihram."
"4979","4973 - And Ahmad ibn Thabit narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Hasan, and he was among the best of people, narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped at Lahyay Jamal while in ihram. And this hadith has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas through many chains with different wordings, and it was narrated from other than Ibn 'Abbas, so we mentioned these isnads among the totality of what is narrated from Ibn 'Abbas in that. As for the hadith of Abu al-Zubayr, we do not know that Abu al-Zubayr reported from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, any hadith other than this one and one other, and the hadith of Ibn Jurayj, we do not know anyone who reported it as raised except Bishr ibn al-Hasan."
"4980","4974 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn al-Mu'ammal narrated to us, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Abu Musa in an expedition by sea. While they were thus, having raised the sail on a dark night, a caller above them called out to the people of the ship: Stop, I shall inform you of a decree Allah has decreed upon Himself. Abu Musa said: Inform, if you are to inform. He said: Verily Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has decreed upon Himself that whoever makes himself thirsty for Him on a hot day, Allah will give him drink on the Day of Thirst. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from Ibn 'Abbas except through this chain, and it has been narrated from Abu Musa as his own statement, with an addition of words from the statement of Abu Musa."
"4981","4975 - Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib ibn Yahya al-Raqqi informed us, he said: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn 'Abd al-Khaliq al-Bazzar narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan, meaning Ibn 'Uyaynah, informed us, from 'Amr, meaning Ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Verily you shall meet Allah tomorrow barefoot, naked, uncircumcised. And this hadith has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas through other than this chain, and it was narrated from other than Ibn 'Abbas, and we do not know it to be narrated from Ibn 'Abbas with a more authentic isnad than this isnad."
"4982","4976 - Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from 'Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: When the Qur'an would descend upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would recite it to memorize it, so Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: {Do not move your tongue with it to hasten it. Verily upon Us is its collection and its recitation}. And this hadith was narrated by more than one from Ibn 'Uyaynah, from 'Amr, from Sa'id, disconnected."
"4983","4977 - And Ahmad ibn 'Abdah and al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah narrated it to us, from Ibn 'Uyaynah, from 'Amr, from Sa'id, from Ibn 'Abbas."
"4984","4978 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4985","4979 - And Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from 'Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr - I doubt in the hadith of Ibn 'Abdah - he said: from Ibn 'Abbas - or he said: from Sa'id - and he did not say: from Ibn 'Abbas - he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not recognize the end of a surah until: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate was revealed; when: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate was revealed, he knew that the surah had been sealed and another surah was begun - or commenced. And this hadith is narrated from 'Amr, from the hadith of Ibn 'Uyaynah, by a group, disconnected."
"4986","4980 - Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from 'Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that a man was standing upon his mount with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he fell from his camel and it broke his neck while he was in ihram. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in his two garments, do not cover his head, and do not bring perfume near him, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection uttering ihram, or talbiyah."
"4987","4981 - And Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Sa'id ibn Jubayr informed him, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A man in ihram came with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he fell from atop his camel, it broke his neck, and he died. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him with water and lote leaves, dress him in his two garments, and do not cover his head, for he will come on the Day of Resurrection reciting talbiyah."
"4988","4982 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, with the like of the report of 'Amr to me from him."
"4989","4983 - And Maymun ibn al-Asbagh narrated it to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in similar wording."
"4990","4984 - And al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Jazari narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Aban ibn Salih narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in similar wording to the hadith of Ibn 'Uyaynah. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated with an isnad better than these isnads."
"4991","4985 - And Muslim ibn Abi Hurrah narrated that from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated it to us, from Ibn 'Uyaynah, from Muslim ibn Abi Hurrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas. And Muslim ibn Abi Hurrah did not raise any hadith other than this one, and Matar al-Warraq and Abu Bishr narrated it from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, so we limited ourselves to those we mentioned."
"4992","4986 - al-Hasan ibn 'Arafah narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas."
"4993","4987 - And Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas."
"4994","4988 - And Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Amir narrated to us, he said: Qurrah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas."
"4995","4989 - And 'Umar ibn Musa al-Shami narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Zuhr and 'Asr and Maghrib and 'Isha in Madinah without fear, so that he would not impose hardship on his Ummah. And this hadith was narrated from Abu al-Zubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, by a group, so we limited ourselves to those we mentioned among them."
"4996","4990 - And Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Umar ibn Suhban narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in the expedition of Tabuk, would delay Zuhr until it cooled, then pray Zuhr and 'Asr, then not dismount until the twilight disappeared, then pray Maghrib and 'Isha. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith with this wording, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, except 'Umar ibn Suhban, and he is 'Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Suhban, a man from the people of Madinah, not strong, and a group of the people of knowledge narrated from him and accepted his hadith."
"4997","4991 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Salih, judge of Ramhurmuz, narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Unaysah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: We were with Ibn 'Abbas in the mosque, the Sacred Mosque, and something of predestination was mentioned in his presence, so he gestured with his hand - and that was after his sight had gone - and I said: There is none among the people from them. He said: I thought there was one among them, so I would take him by the neck. And that is because I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah did not send a prophet then take him except that He placed after him an interval, and Hell is filled from that interval; verily they are the Qadariyyah."
"4998","4992 - And Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim narrated it to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Sabiq narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Qarm, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in similar wording, or close to it. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except through this chain which we mentioned."
"4999","4993 - 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: 'Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Umayyah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas."
"5000","4994 - And Bishr ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn 'Isa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas. And Ibn Idris said: from Ibn Ishaq, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When your brothers were struck, Allah placed their souls in the bellies of green birds that visit the rivers of Paradise, eat from its fruits, and shelter in lamps suspended in the shade of the Throne. When they found the goodness of their food and drink, they said: If only our brothers knew of what Allah has honored us. So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: I shall convey from you to them. So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: {And do not think those killed in the way of Allah are dead; rather they are alive with their Lord, provided for, rejoicing in what Allah has given them of His bounty, and rejoicing in those who have not yet joined them from behind them, that there is no fear upon them nor shall they grieve}. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated with this wording except with this isnad."
"5001","4995 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Ash'ath ibn Sawwar narrated to us, from Abu Hubayrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: My father sent me to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it was the night at my aunt's house. I came and lay down on the bed, and he said: Has the boy slept? And I had not slept, hearing his speech. He said: He prayed four rak'ahs, lengthening the recitation, bowing, and prostration in them. He said: Then he lay down. He said: Then he stood and prayed five rak'ahs, and I stood, performed ablution, and stood at his left, so he took my hand from behind him and placed me at his right. He said: I understood from his supplication while he was saying: O Allah, place light in my hearing, and light in my sight, and light in my heart, and light in my tongue, and light to my right, and light to my left, and light before me, and light behind me, and light beneath me, and light above me; O Allah, magnify light for me. And this hadith has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through many chains regarding the description of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the narration of Ibn 'Abbas from him, and each mentions from Ibn 'Abbas in his narration what requires repeating the hadith because of it. And we do not know that Abu Hubayrah reported from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, except this hadith, and Abu Hubayrah's name is Yahya ibn 'Abbad, a man from the people of Kufah, trustworthy."
"5002","4996 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah, from Qatadah, from 'Azrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas: {And upon those who can bear it, a ransom of feeding a poor person}. He said: It was a concession for the very old man and the very old woman, while they could fast, to break the fast and feed a poor person in place of each day, then it was abrogated, and it was affirmed that if they cannot fast, they break the fast and feed a poor person in place of each day, and the pregnant woman and the nursing woman, when they fear. And Ibn 'Abbas would say to a pregnant slave mother of his: You are in the position of one who cannot bear it, so expiation is upon you, and there is no make-up upon you. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated with this wording with an isnad better than this isnad."
"5003","4997 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Samad ibn 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from 'Azrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the dawn prayer on Friday: Tanzil, the prostration, and {Has there come upon man}. And this hadith was narrated by Ibn 'Abbas, and we do not know it to have been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas except through two chains: one of them narrated by Muslim al-Batin from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, and Qatadah from 'Azrah, and in the hadith of Muslim there is an addition, so we delayed it to mention it in its place with its wording."
"5004","4998 - And Harun ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: 'Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abi 'Arubah, narrated to us, from Qatadah, from 'Azrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man reciting talbiyah on behalf of Shubrumah, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Recite talbiyah for yourself, then recite talbiyah for Shubrumah. And this hadith was narrated by other than 'Abdah from Ibn Abi 'Arubah, from Qatadah, from 'Azrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas as stopped, and we do not know anyone who raised it from Ibn Abi 'Arubah except 'Abdah, and we do not know that 'Azrah reported from Sa'id, from Ibn 'Abbas, except these three hadiths, and 'Azrah is a well-known man from the people of Kufah; Dawud ibn Abi Hind and Qatadah narrated from him, and he is 'Azrah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman."
"5005","4999 - Abu Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from Sa'id, from 'Ali ibn al-Hakam, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar every predator with fangs, and every bird with talons. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, except 'Ali ibn al-Hakam. And Abu Bishr and al-Hakam narrated it from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn 'Abbas, and they did not mention Sa'id ibn Jubayr between Maymun ibn Mihran and Ibn 'Abbas."
"5006","5000 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no days in which righteous deeds are more beloved to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, than these days, meaning the ten days. They said: O Messenger of Allah, not even striving in the way of Allah? He said: Not even striving in the way of Allah, except a man who went out with himself and his wealth and returned with nothing."
"5007","5001 - And this hadith was narrated by al-Hakam ibn 'Utaybah from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas. Yusuf narrated it to us, from Salamah, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam."
"5008","5002 - And al-Qasim ibn Abi Ayyub narrated it from Sa'id, from Ibn 'Abbas. Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated it to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Asbagh ibn Zayd informed us, from al-Qasim ibn Abi Ayyub, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas."
"5009","5003 - And Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani narrated it from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas. And Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated it to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn 'Atiyyah narrated to us, from Qays, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas."
"5010","5004 - Abu Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother died owing a month of fasting; shall I make it up for her? He said: Tell me, if your mother owed a debt, would you repay it for her? She said: Yes. He said: Then the debt of Allah is more deserving of being repaid. And we do not know anyone who narrates this hadith with this wording except Muslim al-Batin, and Abu Bishr differed from him in his narration. And the hadith of Muslim is not the preserved one from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); rather this hadith in my view, and Allah knows best, is summarized, because he did not inform her how to make it up, whether herself or feeding a poor person for each day."
"5011","5005 - 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Hakam and Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr and 'Ata' and Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My sister died owing two consecutive months of fasting. He said: Tell me, if your sister owed a debt, would you repay it? She said: Yes. He said: Then the right of Allah is more deserving."
"5012","5006 - Abu Musa narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mukhawwal, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas."
"5013","5007 - And Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Mukhawwal, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite on Friday in the dawn prayer: {Alif Lam Mim, the revelation}, and {Has there come upon man}. And Abu 'Awanah added, from Muslim, from Sa'id, from Ibn 'Abbas: And he recites on Friday Surah al-Jumu'ah and {When the hypocrites come to you}."
"5014","5008 - And Muhammad ibn 'Uthman narrated it to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to recite in the dawn prayer on Friday: {Alif Lam Mim, the revelation}, the prostration, and {Has there come upon man}. And we do not know anyone who narrated: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite on Friday Surah al-Jumu'ah and the Hypocrites, except from the hadith of Muslim, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, and we do not know that Abu Ishaq reported from Muslim any hadith other than this one."
"5015","5009 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Muslim al-Batin and al-Minhal, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: Allah sent down the Qur'an to the lowest heaven on the Night of Decree all at once; Jibril would bring it down, meaning upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5016","5010 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, meaning Ibn Harb, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man will enter upon you, entering with the two eyes of a devil. Then a blue-eyed man entered and said: O Muhammad, for what does this one revile me, or for what does he insult me? He said: And he began to swear oaths, so this verse was revealed: {And they swear to falsehood while they know}, the verse and the other verse."
"5017","5011 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Anmati narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Simak, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for thirty mornings in the forenoon prayer."
"5018","5012 - And 'Abdullah ibn Mu'awiyah narrated it to us, he said: Thabit Abu Zayd, and he is Ibn Yazid, narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for thirty mornings. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Simak except 'Amr ibn Abi Qays, and it has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding his qunut through various chains with different wordings, so we mentioned each hadith among them with its wording in its place."
"5019","5013 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas."
"5020","5014 - And 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while I was fifteen years old. And he said in the hadith of Ibn Idris: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken while I was circumcised."
"5021","5015 - Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: He was asked: Like whom were you when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away? He said: On that day I was circumcised."
"5022","5016 - Muhammad ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr with: {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High}, and {Say: O disbelievers}, and {Say: He is Allah, One}. And the meaning of this hadith in our view, and Allah knows best, is that he would place these surahs among what he recited in his witr, and he would call the night prayer witr, and that witr is not valid except as one rak'ah; this is the meaning of the action of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his statement."
"5023","5017 - al-Husayn ibn 'Ali al-Baghdadi, known as Ibn 'Uluwayh, narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was born in the Year of the Elephant. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq except Hajjaj ibn Muhammad, and he was trustworthy."
"5024","5018 - Abu Musa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, and from 'Adi ibn Thabit, from Sa'id, from Ibn 'Abbas, one of them raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Verily Jibril would stuff mud into the mouth of Pharaoh fearing he would say: There is no god but Allah. And another said: Fearing mercy would reach him."
"5025","5019 - Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My mother owes a believing slave to be freed, and I have a black slave girl. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring her to me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah? She said: Yes. He said: Then free her. And this hadith has been narrated with similar meaning from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through various chains with different wordings; we mention each wording among them in its place with its isnad."
"5026","5020 - Muhammad ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from al-'Ala' ibn Salih, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, he said: Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrated to me, he said: A man came to Ibn 'Abbas and said: Ten were revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah and ten in Makkah. He said: From whom did you hear this? He said: It reached me, or I heard people saying it. Ibn 'Abbas said: Ten and five and more were revealed to him in Makkah. And this statement, we do not know it to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this chain, and it has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas with other than this wording."
"5027","5021 - al-Husayn ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, he said: 'Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Minhal, from Sa'id, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5028","5022 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that al-Sa'b ibn Jaththamah gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was at Qudayd and in ihram, the meat of a wild donkey, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned it while it was dripping blood. And this hadith has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas through various chains, so we mentioned each hadith among them with its wording in its place. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-A'mash, from al-Minhal, except 'Ammar ibn Ruzayq."
"5029","5023 - And Abu Mu'awiyah differed from him, narrating it from al-A'mash, from Habib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, adding in it: Were it not that we are in ihram, we would have accepted it from you. And we only mentioned it due to the disagreement of al-A'mash, to make that clear. Abu Musa narrated it to us, from Abu Mu'awiyah."
"5030","5024 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Habib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Zuhr and 'Asr and Maghrib and 'Isha in Madinah without fear or rain. It was said to him: What did he intend by that? He said: He intended not to impose hardship on his Ummah. And in this hadith Habib added: Without fear or rain, while others do not mention rain, though 'Abd al-Karim said something similar. And the memorizers narrate it: Without fear or excuse."
"5031","5025 - Abu Musa narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Be lenient in prayer, for behind you are the weak, the elderly, and the one with a need."
"5032","5026 - Abu Musa narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Habib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of that. And we do not know anyone who narrates it from al-A'mash, from Habib, except Abu 'Awanah."
"5033","5027 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Habib, or 'Adi, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: No man who believes in Allah and the Last Day hates the Ansar."
"5034","5028 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Raja' narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I vowed to sacrifice at Buwanah. He said: Perhaps there is something of ignorance in your heart? He said: No. He said: Then fulfill your vow. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated with this wording from Ibn 'Abbas except through the narration of al-Mas'udi, from Habib, from Sa'id, from Ibn 'Abbas."
"5035","5029 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Habib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first to stand, or the first to be called on the Day of Resurrection, are those who praise Allah in every circumstance. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from Ibn 'Abbas except with this isnad, and al-Mas'udi and Qays narrated it from Habib."
"5036","5030 - 'Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Qabisah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: When: {And warn your closest kindred} was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began calling them tribe by tribe. And we do not know anyone who narrates it from Habib, from Sa'id, from Ibn 'Abbas, except al-Thawri, and we do not know anyone who narrates it from al-Thawri except Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham and Qabisah."
"5037","5031 - Muhammad ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib, from Sa'id, from Ibn 'Abbas."
"5038","5032 - And Abu Burayd narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammal narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued reciting talbiyah until he stoned the Aqabah pillar. And other than Habib narrates it from Ibn 'Abbas from al-Fadl ibn 'Abbas."
"5039","5033 - Usayd ibn 'Asim narrated to us, he said: 'Amir ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub al-Qummi narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while a cloud had shaded us and we were hoping for rain from it, and he said: The angel who drives it entered upon me, greeted me, and informed me that he drives it to such-and-such valley."
"5040","5034 - Isma'il ibn 'Abdullah al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Hasan ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: Khattab ibn Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah narrated to us, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go around among the palm trees in Madinah, and people would say: In it is a sa', in it is a wasq. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In it is such-and-such and such-and-such. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am only a human; whatever I narrate to you from Allah is truth, and whatever I say from my own opinion, I am only a human who errs and is correct. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from Ibn 'Abbas except through this chain with this isnad."
"5041","5035 - 'Ali ibn Harb al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn 'Abdullah al-Ash'ari, and he is al-Qummi, narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, who are the allies of Allah? He said: Those who, when seen, Allah is remembered. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated with this wording except through this chain with this isnad, and other than Muhammad ibn Sa'id narrated it from Ya'qub, from Ja'far, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, disconnected."
"5042","5036 - Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub, meaning al-Qummi, narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not break his fast on the white days, neither in travel nor in residence. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated with this wording except through this chain with this isnad."
"5043","5037 - Abu Hisham Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Rifa'i narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from 'Imran al-Sulami, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The people of Makkah asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to make al-Safa gold for them and to remove the mountains from around them so they could cultivate. It was said: If you wish that We grant them what they asked, but if they disbelieve they will be destroyed as those before them were destroyed. So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: {And nothing prevented Us from sending the signs except that the former peoples denied them, and We gave Thamud the she-camel as a clear sign}."
"5044","5038 - And Abu Hisham narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, he said: Talhah al-Qannad narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in similar wording. And we only heard this hadith from Abu Hisham, the hadith of Talhah al-Qannad from Ja'far."
"5045","5039 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ja'far ibn Abi Wahshiyyah, and he is Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The people of Makkah asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to make al-Safa gold for them. Then he mentioned similar wording. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through an authentic chain except through this chain."
"5046","5040 - Ibrahim ibn Hani' narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub al-Qummi narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a man of the Ansar who was ill, and when he drew near his house he heard him speaking inside. When he sought permission and entered, he saw no one. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I heard you speaking to someone other than yourself. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I entered inside grieving over people's talk due to the fever in me, then a man entered upon me the like of whom I have never seen after you, more honored in gathering nor better in speech. He said: That was Jibril, and among you are men such that if one of them were to swear by Allah, He would fulfill it. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this chain with this isnad."
"5047","5041 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ja'far ibn Abi Wahshiyyah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would raise his voice with the Qur'an and lower it at times, so Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: {And do not recite loudly in your prayer nor silently in it, but seek between that a way}."
"5048","5042 - And Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated it to us, he said: al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ja'far ibn Abi Wahshiyyah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in similar wording. And we do not know anyone who narrates this hadith with this wording with a connected isnad except from Ibn 'Abbas with this isnad."
"5049","5043 - Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ja'far ibn Abi Wahshiyyah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: They disliked giving charity to their relatives while they were polytheists, so was revealed: {Guidance is not upon you}, until it reached: {And whatever good you spend, verily Allah knows it}, so they were permitted. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated with this wording except through this chain with this isnad."
"5050","5044 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: 'Uthman ibn 'Umar narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was aided by the east wind, and 'Ad were destroyed by the west wind. And this hadith is narrated from Ibn 'Abbas through various chains; Mujahid and others narrated it from Ibn 'Abbas. As for the hadith of Abu Bishr, from Sa'id, from Ibn 'Abbas, we do not know anyone who narrated it except 'Uthman ibn 'Umar, and other than 'Uthman narrated it from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, disconnected."
"5051","5045 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fast until we would say he does not intend to break fast, and he would break fast until we would say he does not intend to fast, and he did not fast any consecutive month since arriving in Madinah other than Ramadan. And this hadith has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas through other than this chain, and this isnad is among the best isnads narrated from Ibn 'Abbas in that."
"5052","5046 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the children of polytheists, and he said: Allah knows best what they would have done. And this hadith is narrated from Ibn 'Abbas through more than one chain, and from other than Ibn 'Abbas with different wordings, so we mentioned each hadith in its place with its wording."
"5053","5047 - Abu Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that his maternal aunt gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clarified butter, dried yogurt, and mastigures; he ate of the clarified butter and the dried yogurt but did not eat of the mastigures out of aversion, and it was eaten at the table of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through various chains with different wordings, so we mentioned each hadith among them in its place with its wording."
"5054","5048 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr and Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would teach us the tashahhud as he would teach us the Qur'an: Greetings, blessings, prayers, and good words belong to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. And we do not know this wording to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a connected isnad from him better than this isnad."
"5055","5049 - Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr and Miqsam, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A man of the polytheists was struck down, and the polytheists sought to bury him, offering blood money for him, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) refused. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated with this wording except through this chain with this isnad."
"5056","5050 - 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Hakam and Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr and 'Ata' and Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My sister died owing two consecutive months of fasting. He said: Tell me, if your sister owed a debt, would you repay it? She said: Yes. He said: Then the right of Allah is more deserving. And we have already mentioned this hadith from Abu Mu'awiyah, from al-A'mash, from Muslim, from Sa'id, from Ibn 'Abbas, and Abu Khalid added al-Hakam along with Muslim, and also mentioned it from Mujahid and 'Ata'. And the wording of the hadith of Abu Khalid differs from the wording of Abu Mu'awiyah, so we repeated it for two reasons: the difference of its isnad from al-A'mash, and the difference of its wording."
"5057","5051 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Hamid ibn 'Abd al-Rahman Abu Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Tariq ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5058","5052 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari and Muhammad ibn Harb al-Wasiti narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Tariq ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: O Allah, You made the first of Quraysh taste punishment, so make the last of them taste favor. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from Ibn 'Abbas except through this chain with this isnad, and we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi and Abu Yahya al-Himmani."
"5059","5053 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn 'Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn 'Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: I was sitting with Ibn 'Abbas when 'Urwah came to him and said: O Ibn 'Abbas, what do you say when you give fatwa permitting mut'ah, when you know that Abu Bakr and 'Umar forbade it and disliked it? Ibn 'Abbas said: It was the last covenant of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with which he parted from the people. 'Urwah said: By Allah, O Ibn 'Abbas, Abu Bakr and 'Umar knew the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) better than you. Ibn 'Abbas said: O 'Urayyah, I see punishment will descend upon you; I inform you that it was the last covenant of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with which he parted from the people, and you say: Abu Bakr and 'Umar. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from Ibn 'Abbas with better than this isnad, and Ibn 'Abbas only meant the mut'ah of Hajj, not the mut'ah of women."
"5060","5054 - Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abdullah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5061","5055 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abdullah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: You hear, and it is heard from you, and it is heard from those who heard from you. And this hadith has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas through another chain, and this isnad is better than the isnad narrated in that."
"5062","5056 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abdullah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: When Thursday came - and what is Thursday - then Ibn 'Abbas wept, regarding the illness of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which he passed away. He said: Bring me a sheet and inkwell so I may write for you a document after which you will never go astray. And something similar to this hadith has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas through authentic chains, and 'Abdullah ibn 'Abdullah added over them a word that was denounced against him, so the hadith became denounced because of the word, and we did not mention the word out of reverence for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 'Abdullah ibn 'Abdullah was in Kufah, and he was the judge of al-Rayy, and he has denounced reports not followed upon, and from other than Ibn 'Abbas. And 'Abdullah ibn 'Abdullah is not strong in hadith, because he narrated hadiths not followed upon."
"5063","5057 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Black Stone descended from Paradise whiter than snow or hail, and nothing blackened it except the sins of the children of Adam. And this hadith was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas through more than one chain, so we limited ourselves to this isnad among them."
"5064","5058 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), raising it regarding His statement: {And if you are ill or on a journey}, he said: When a man has wounds in the way of Allah, or sores, or smallpox, and he fears he will die if he bathes, he performs tayammum. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated with this wording except from Ibn 'Abbas with this isnad, and we do not know any trustworthy man who raised this hadith from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib except Jarir."
"5065","5059 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only prayed the two rak'ahs after 'Asr because wealth came to him and he distributed it, and it distracted him from the two rak'ahs after Zuhr, so he prayed them after 'Asr and did not return to them. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated with this wording except through this chain with this isnad."
"5066","5060 - Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, he said: 'Imran ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Jews disputed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, you eat what we kill but do not eat what Allah kills. So Allah revealed: {And do not eat of that upon which the name of Allah has not been mentioned, and indeed it is grave disobedience, and indeed the devils inspire their allies}. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated with this wording with an isnad better than this isnad."
"5067","5061 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Mas'ud narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That Allah's prophet Sulayman, when he stood to pray, would see a tree growing before him and say to it: What is your name? It would say: Such-and-such. He would say: For what purpose are you? It would say: For such-and-such. If it was for medicine, it was recorded, and if it was for planting, it was planted. While he was one day praying, a tree grew before him, so he said to it: What is your name? It said: Al-kharnubah. He said: For what purpose are you? It said: For the ruin of this House. Sulayman said: O Allah, conceal my death from the jinn, so that mankind may know that the jinn do not know the unseen. So he took his staff, leaned upon it, and died while the jinn were working. The termite ate it over a year, then he fell. So the jinn realized that had they known the unseen, they would not have remained a year in humiliating torment. And Ibn 'Abbas used to recite it thus. He said: So the jinn thanked the termite, and would bring it water."
"5068","5062 - Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, in similar wording, and he did not raise it. And this hadith was narrated by a group from 'Ata', from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas as stopped, and we do not know anyone who raised it except Ibrahim ibn Tahman."
"5069","5063 - Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim informed us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Report is not like seeing. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through the narration of Ibn 'Abbas from him with this isnad."
"5070","5064 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5071","5065 - Muhammad ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, he said: 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Verily blessing descends in the middle of food, so eat from its sides and do not eat from its middle. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this chain with this isnad."
"5072","5066 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I have not seen a people better than the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); they did not ask him except about twelve questions, all of them in the Qur'an: {They ask you about wine and gambling}, and {They ask you about the sacred month}, {And they ask you about orphans}. He said: When was revealed: {And do not approach the wealth of the orphan}, they separated their food from his food, so was revealed: {And if you mix with them, they are your brothers, and Allah knows the corrupter from the reformer}. And in this hadith there is other speech besides this."
"5073","5067 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: 'Imran ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out on a festival day leaning upon Usamah, prayed, then delivered the sermon, then went to the women, admonished and reminded them, so they began to give charity. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id, from Ibn 'Abbas, except 'Imran ibn 'Uyaynah."
"5074","5068 - 'Abdullah ibn Abi Thumamah and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, they said: 'Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When I was taken by night, I passed by a pleasant scent and said: What is this scent, O Jibril? He said: This is the scent of the hairdresser of Pharaoh's wife. Her comb fell from her hand and she said: In the name of Allah. Pharaoh's daughter said: My father? She said: My Lord and your father's Lord. She said: Shall I inform my father of that? She said: Yes. So she informed him, and he summoned her and said: Do you have a lord besides me? She said: Yes, my Lord and your Lord. So he brought a hollow vessel of copper and heated it, then she said: I have a need from you: gather my bones and the bones of my children. He said: You have upon us a right for that. So he threw her and her children in until it reached a nursing infant among them, who said: Be patient, O slave girl, for you are upon the truth. So she and her children were thrown into the vessel. Four spoke while small: the witness of Yusuf, the companion of Jurayj, and 'Isa. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated with this wording from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through a connected chain except through this chain with this isnad."
"5075","5069 - Abu Musa narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from 'Adi ibn Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: One of them says: My father accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and was with my father, yet a worn-out sandal is better than his father."
"5076","Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Amrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I send my trained dog and it catches (the game). He said: If it eats (from it) then do not eat, and if it does not eat then eat. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel with this chain; and Hammad ibn Shu'ayb is not strong in hadith, though a group of the people of knowledge narrated from him and accepted his hadith."
"5077","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah ibn al-Nu'man, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood admonishing (the people) and said: O people, you will be gathered barefoot and naked, (then he recited:) As We began the first creation, We shall repeat it, a promise binding upon Us; indeed We shall do it. Verily the first of creation to be clothed on the Day of Resurrection will be Ibrahim (peace be upon him). Verily men from my nation will be brought and taken to the left, so I shall say: O Lord, my companions. Then it will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you. So I shall say as the righteous servant said: And I was a witness over them as long as I remained among them, but when You took me, You were the Watcher over them, up to His saying: And if You forgive them, indeed You are the Exalted in Might, the Wise. Then it will be said: They continued turning back on their heels since you parted from them. And we do not know this hadith narrated with this wording except from Ibn Abbas with this chain, though some of its phrases have been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through other channels."
"5078","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that a bowl of tharid was brought to him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat from its sides, or from its edges, and do not eat from its middle, for blessing descends in its middle."
"5079","Al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah and al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, they said: Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abu Kudaynah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The talbiyah of Musa (peace be upon him) was: Here I am, Your servant and the son of Your two servants; and the talbiyah of Isa (peace be upon him) was: Here I am, Your servant and the son of Your bondwoman; and the talbiyah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, You have no partner. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas except through this channel, and we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib except Abu Kudaynah."
"5080","Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah, meaning Ibn Musa, narrated to us, he said: Farqad, meaning al-Sabakhi, narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in Makkah, and a woman from the Ansar came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, this wicked one (i.e. a possessing devil) has overpowered me. He said to her: If you remain patient upon what you suffer, you will come on the Day of Resurrection with no sins upon you and no reckoning. She said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I shall surely remain patient until I meet Allah. She said: I fear the wicked one may strip me bare, so he supplicated for her. Thereafter, when she feared it would come to her, she would go to the curtains of the Ka'bah and cling to them and say to it: Be gone, and it would leave her. And we do not know this hadith narrated with this wording except through this channel with this chain; and Sadaqah is unobjectionable, and Farqad has been narrated from by a group of the people of knowledge, among them Shu'bah and others, and they accepted his hadith despite poor memory in him."
"5081","Muhammad ibn Umarah ibn Subayh narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mixing raisins and dates together, meaning for making nabidh (infused drink). And Abu Bishr narrated this hadith from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, and others besides Abu Bishr narrated it; and we do not know of Asim narrating from Sa'id ibn Jubayr with a connected chain any hadith other than this one."
"5082","Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the house of Maymunah, and I prepared ablution water for him at night. Maymunah said: Abd Allah ibn Abbas placed this for you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, grant him understanding in the religion and teach him interpretation. And this hadith has been narrated from Ibn Abbas through other channels with different chains and varying wordings, so we have mentioned each hadith in its place with its wording."
"5083","Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Hayyaj narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: Concession was granted to the sick person to perform tayammum with earth when afflicted with smallpox (open sores). And we do not know of Asim narrating from Qatadah with a connected chain any hadith other than this one."
"5084","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Sufyan, meaning al-Thawri, narrated to us, from Hammad, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I find within my breast something such that becoming charred coal would be dearer to me than speaking of it. So the Messenger of Allah said: Allah is Most Great; praise be to Allah who reduced his (Satan's) matter to (mere) whispering. And the like of this hadith's wording has been narrated from Ibn Abbas with a different wording through another channel, so we mentioned each hadith in its place with its wording; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Hammad except Sufyan, nor from Sufyan except Ishaq al-Azraq."
"5085","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Qabisah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Hammad, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married while in ihram. And others besides Qabisah narrate this hadith from Sufyan from Ibn Khuthaym from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, so we wanted to clarify that Qabisah reported it thus."
"5086","Abu Musa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Jabir, from Ammar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever builds a mosque, even like the nesting place of a sandgrouse for its eggs, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas except through this channel with this chain; and Jabir is one about whom we have already mentioned that a group (of scholars) criticized him, yet the people of knowledge narrated from him, and we do not know anyone regarded as an authority who abandoned his hadith; and Ammar from whom Jabir narrated is Ammar al-Duhni."
"5087","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Al-A'mash narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dispense with (asking) people even with (a small piece like) the tip of a toothstick. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim; and al-A'mash narrated several (hadiths) from Sa'id and left others without a connected chain, and we do not know whether this hadith is among what he heard from Sa'id."
"5088","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bazi' narrated to us, he said: Aththam ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Al-A'mash narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stood at night, would begin with the toothstick, or he said: would clean his teeth. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Aththam, and Aththam is trustworthy."
"5089","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that a man insulted a forefather of al-Abbas from the days of ignorance, so al-Abbas slapped him; then his people came and said: By Allah, we shall surely slap him as he slapped him, until they took up weapons, or until they donned weapons. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he ascended the pulpit and said: O people, which people of the earth do you know to be noblest to Allah? They said: You. He said: Al-Abbas is from me and I am from him; do not revile our dead, for you harm (thereby) our living. So the people came and said: O Messenger of Allah, we seek refuge in Allah from your anger; seek forgiveness for us. And we do not know these words narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel with this chain, and its chain is fair (hasan): Abd al-A'la al-Tha'labi is a well-known Kufan, and those after him and before him are trustworthy."
"5090","Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan, meaning al-Thawri, narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever speaks about the Qur'an without knowledge, let him take his seat in the Fire. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel with this chain."
"5091","Yahya ibn al-Fadl al-Khuraqi and Malik ibn Sa'd al-Qaysi narrated to us, they said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Made unlawful through fosterage is whatever is made unlawful through lineage. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Sa'id ibn Jubayr except through the narration of Abd al-A'la, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abd al-A'la except Ibrahim ibn Tahman, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ibrahim except Abu Amir; and others besides Abu Amir narrated it from Ibrahim from Simak from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas."
"5092","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah, from Isra'il, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies while addicted to wine meets Allah as one who worships an idol. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain, nor do we preserve it from anyone besides Ibn Abbas through a sound channel; and Hakim ibn Jubayr was a man extreme in Shi'ism, and some of the people of knowledge refrained from narrating from him, and he narrated several hadiths in which he was not corroborated; yet al-A'mash, al-Thawri, Isra'il and others narrated from him."
"5093","Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had given us our share from Khaybar, and Abu Bakr gave it to us; then when Umar (became caliph) and people grew numerous upon him, he sent for us and said: People have grown numerous upon me, so if you wish I shall give you wealth in place of your share from Khaybar? We looked at one another and said: Yes. Then Umar was stabbed and we had taken nothing, and Uthman took it (i.e. authority) and refused to give us, saying: Umar had already taken it from you."
"5094","Abbad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Hakim ibn Jubayr narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly. Abd Allah ibn Bukayr here is a Kufan given to Shi'ism. And we do not know this hadith narrated with this wording except through the hadith of Hakim ibn Jubayr from Sa'id from Ibn Abbas, and we have already mentioned Hakim, so we have sufficed without repeating mention of him thereafter."
"5095","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) climbed al-Safa one day and cried: O (cry of) morning calamity! So Quraysh gathered to him, and he said to them: If I were to inform you that an enemy will attack you in the morning or the evening, would you believe me? They said: Yes. He said: I am a warner to you before a severe punishment. Then Abu Lahab stood and said: Perish you, O Muhammad, is this why you gathered us? Then there was revealed: Perish the hands of Abu Lahab, and perish he."
"5096","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Maymun narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except with this chain that we mentioned; and we do not know anyone who reported in it from Amr from Abu al-Bakhtari from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas except Yahya al-Umawi, and he is trustworthy; and we do not know of Abu al-Bakhtari narrating from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas with a connected chain any hadith other than this one."
"5097","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Bahrani and Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, they said: Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Salim al-Aftas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that he (Ibn Abbas) passed by people who had set up a hen as a target shooting at it, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade taking any living creature as a target. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Thawri from Salim al-Aftas from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas except Mu'ammal."
"5098","Yahya ibn Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, he said: Qays, meaning Ibn al-Rabi', narrated to us, from Salim al-Aftas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: Khalid ibn Sinan was mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: That was a prophet whom his people neglected. And al-Thawri narrated this hadith from Salim al-Aftas from Sa'id ibn Jubayr without a connected chain (mursal), while Qays narrated it with a connected chain; and we have not heard anyone narrate it from Muhammad ibn al-Salt except Yahya ibn Mu'alla. This hadith is otherwise preserved through the hadith of al-Kalbi from Abu Salih from Ibn Abbas: that the daughter of Khalid ibn Sinan entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Welcome to the daughter of a prophet whom his people neglected."
"5099","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the best of your garments are the white ones, so let your living wear them and shroud your dead in them. And this hadith is narrated from Samurah and from others besides Samurah, and it is narrated from Ibn Abbas with this chain; and we do not know for it any chain from Ibn Abbas other than this chain. And Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym is a well-known Makkan, fair in hadith, and we do not know anyone who abandoned his hadith."
"5100","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the best of your kohl preparations is ithmid (antimony), for it clears the sight and grows the hair. And this hadith has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through other channels, and this chain is among the finest chains narrated in this regard from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5101","Ishaq ibn Buhlul narrated to us, he said: Al-Walid ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly. And we do not know this hadith narrated through the hadith of Uthman ibn Hakim; rather it is preserved from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym. And we have not heard anyone narrate it from al-Walid ibn al-Qasim except Ishaq ibn Buhlul, and we do not know of al-Walid ibn al-Qasim narrating anything from Ibn Khuthaym."
"5102","Bishr ibn Mu'adh al-Aqadi narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at Makkah and said: You are indeed the most beloved of Allah's land to Allah; and had my people not expelled me from you, I would not have left. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas except through two channels: one of them narrated by Talhah ibn Amr from Ata from Ibn Abbas, and we mentioned the hadith of Talhah due to the weakness of Talhah; and we mentioned it from Abd Allah ibn Uthman from Sa'id from Ibn Abbas, since this chain is sounder and worthier of mention. It has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through other channels with different wordings, so we mentioned each hadith in its place with its wording."
"5103","Yusuf ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Umayyah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, as I deem (there is doubt in the hadith), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in Makkah and recited Surah al-Najm until he reached: Have you considered al-Lat and al-Uzza, and Manat, the third, the other; then there flowed upon his tongue: Those are the exalted cranes (gharaniq), whose intercession is hoped for. He said: So the polytheists of the people of Makkah heard that and rejoiced at it, and it weighed heavily upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: And We did not send before you any messenger or prophet but that when he recited, Satan cast into his recitation; then Allah abolishes what Satan casts, then Allah establishes His verses. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a connected chain whose mention is permissible except with this chain; and we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith with a connected chain from Shu'bah from Abu Bishr from Sa'id from Ibn Abbas except Umayyah, and we heard it only from Yusuf ibn Hammad, and he was trustworthy. Others besides Umayyah narrate it from Abu Bishr from Sa'id ibn Jubayr without a connected chain (mursal); and this hadith is otherwise known from al-Kalbi from Abu Salih from Ibn Abbas. And Umayyah is a well-known trustworthy narrator."
"5104","Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Khasif, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr and Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only forbade pure silk; as for that whose warp is silk, there is no harm in it. And he forbade silver vessels. And Ibn Jurayj only narrated this hadith from Khasif from Ikrimah, while Ibn Jurayj joined Ikrimah and Sa'id ibn Jubayr together."
"5105","Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-A'mash, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), regarding: A questioner asked; he said: It was revealed concerning al-Nadr ibn al-Harith ibn Kaladah. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Abu Usamah."
"5106","Al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, he said: Mansur and al-A'mash narrated to us, from al-Minhal, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek protection for al-Hasan and al-Husayn, saying: Your father Ibrahim used to seek protection for Isma'il and Ishaq with these words: I seek protection for you two with the perfect words of Allah from every devil and vermin and from every envious eye. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-A'mash from al-Minhal from Sa'id from Ibn Abbas except Abu Hafs al-Abbar; rather it is known through the hadith of Mansur from al-Minhal, so Abu Hafs joined Mansur and al-A'mash together."
"5107","Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: And Talhah mentioned, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A man from the Ansar married a woman from Bal'ajlan (Banu Ajlan) and spent the night with her; in the morning he did not find her a virgin. Their case was brought before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he summoned the girl, and she said: Nay, I was a virgin. So he ordered the two of them to invoke mutual curses (li'an), and he gave her the dowry. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except through this channel with this chain."
"5108","Abd Allah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Idris ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Talhah, meaning Ibn Musarrif, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: When the Emigrants came to Madinah, they used to inherit through alliance rather than kinship, so this verse was revealed: And blood relatives are more entitled to one another. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Talhah ibn Musarrif from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from him except Idris."
"5109","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered regarding those slain on the Day of Uhud that iron and skins be removed from them, and said: Bury them in their garments with their blood. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Ibn Abbas, nor do we know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib from Sa'id from Ibn Abbas except Ali ibn Asim. And Ali ibn Asim is one about whom a group of the people of knowledge spoke, though they narrated from him; he was obstinate, narrating hadiths in which he was contradicted yet persisting upon them, so his hadith was weakened for that reason."
"5110","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbawayh al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, he said: Warqa narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: When there was revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Messenger believes in what was sent down to him from his Lord, he recited it; and when he reached: Your forgiveness, our Lord, and to You is the return, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: I have forgiven you. When he said: Our Lord, do not take us to account if we forget or err, Allah said: I shall not take you to account. When he said: And do not lay upon us a burden as You laid upon those before us, Allah said: I shall not lay (it) upon you. When he said: And do not burden us with what we cannot bear, Allah said: I shall not burden you. When he said: And pardon us, Allah said: I have pardoned you. When he said: And forgive us, Allah said: I have forgiven you. When he said: And have mercy upon us, Allah said: I have had mercy upon you. When he said: And grant us victory over the disbelieving people, Allah said: I have granted you victory over the disbelieving people. And we do not know this hadith narrated except from Ibn Abbas with this chain."
"5111","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, he said: Al-Firyabi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ghalib Abu al-Hudhayl, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas. (A truncated/bridging entry with the chain ending at Ibn Abbas.)"
"5112","Hawtharah narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn Nuh narrated to us, he said: Al-Mu'alla al-Attar narrated to us, and Abu al-Mu'alla al-Attar narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): Al-Sa'b ibn Jaththamah gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a leg, or the hindpart, of a wild donkey while he was in ihram, so he returned it."
"5113","Abu Sa'id Abd Allah ibn Sa'id al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: Pride is My cloak and might is My lower garment; whoever contends with Me for either of them, I shall cast him into Hell. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ata from Sa'id from Ibn Abbas except al-Muharibi; and others besides al-Muharibi narrated it from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib from al-Agharr from Abu Hurayrah, and the hadith of al-Agharr was narrated by a group from Ata."
"5114","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Does your Lord dye? He said: Yes, a dye that does not fade: red, yellow and white. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith with a connected chain from Ibn Abbas except Ziyad ibn Abd Allah from Ata from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas; others reported it from Ata from Sa'id ibn Jubayr without a connected chain (mursal)."
"5115","Amr ibn Ali and al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, they said: Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas. (A bridging chain entry ending at Ibn Abbas.)"
"5116","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Raqabah, meaning Ibn Masqalah, from Talhah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: Ibn Abbas said to me: O Sa'id, marry, for the best of this nation were those with the most wives. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib except Asbat, nor did anyone narrate the hadith of Talhah except Abu Awanah from Raqabah."
"5117","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Abd al-Malik, meaning Ibn Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I am holding you back by your waistbands, saying: Beware of Hell, beware of (transgressing) the prescribed punishments; beware of Hell, beware of the punishments; beware of Hell, beware of the punishments, three times. When I die I shall leave you, and I shall precede you at the Pond; whoever comes to it will succeed. And groups will be brought and taken to the left, so I shall say: O Lord, (I think he said:) and it will be said: They continued apostatizing upon their heels after you. And the like of this hadith has been narrated with a different wording through other channels; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abd al-Malik ibn Sa'id from his father except Layth ibn Abi Sulaym."
"5118","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl and Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, they said: Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Abu Hashim, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that a funeral passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he stood, and when questioned about it, he said: Death is a terror (a frightening event). And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas except through this channel."
"5119","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Adam, meaning Ibn Sulayman, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: There was revealed: And whether you disclose what is in yourselves or conceal it, Allah will hold you to account for it. He said: That weighed heavily upon them; they said: Which of us does not speak to himself? So there was revealed: Allah does not burden a soul beyond its capacity, along with the two verses after it. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Sa'id from Ibn Abbas except Adam ibn Sulayman, and Adam ibn Sulayman is the father of Yahya ibn Adam."
"5120","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Abd Allah ibn Ya'la al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Al-Minhal ibn Amr narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) expiated his oath with a sa' of dates, and ordered the people to do so; whoever cannot find (a full sa'), then half a sa' of wheat. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Minhal except Umar ibn Abd Allah ibn Ya'la, and he is a man who is not strong; and what is preserved from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through a sound channel is contrary to this wording and contrary to this act. We only mentioned it despite its contents because we have not preserved its wording from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel."
"5121","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Ash'ath ibn Sulaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not look at one who lets his garment trail (in pride). And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Ash'ath ibn Abi al-Sha'tha from Sa'id from Ibn Abbas, and we do not know anyone who narrated it with a connected chain from Shu'bah except Yahya ibn al-Sakan and Ubayd ibn Aqil."
"5122","Al-Hasan ibn Yunus al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sulaym, who is Ibn Abi al-Sha'tha, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (the same hadith about trailing the garment). And Shayban narrated it from Ash'ath from Sa'id from Ibn Abbas in raised (marfu') form."
"5123","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The nations were shown to me; a prophet would pass before me with a group with him, and a prophet with a small band, until there passed before me a great multitude. I said: (Is this) my nation? He said: That is Musa and his nation. Then it was said to me: Look at the horizon; and there was a multitude filling the entire horizon from every side. It was said: This is your nation, and besides these, seventy thousand from your nation will enter Paradise without reckoning. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) then entered (his house) without clarifying to us who they were, so people delved into discussion and spoke much. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are those who do not cauterize, do not seek ruqyah (charm-treatment), do not take omens, and place their trust in their Lord. Then Ukkashah ibn Mihsan stood and said: Am I among them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes. Then another stood and said: Am I among them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Ukkashah has preceded you to it."
"5124","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Husayn, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly. And Shu'bah narrated this hadith, giving part of its wording; while Ibn Fudayl and Ziyad are more complete in narration than Shu'bah. And we do not know of Husayn narrating from Sa'id from Ibn Abbas with a connected chain any hadith other than this one."
"5125","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Ruzayq, from Abd Allah ibn Isa, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: Jibril was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he heard a thud; he raised his head and said: This is a gate of heaven that has been opened, never opened before except today. An angel descended therein and greeted him. Jibril said: This is an angel who never descended to earth except today. He said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Rejoice in what none before you was given: the closing verses of Surah al-Baqarah; I think he said: No one recites them and asks for anything but that he is given it."
"5126","Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi and Ahmad ibn al-Haytham al-Thaghri narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that he said: O my sons, leave Makkah as pilgrims on foot until you return to Makkah, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The mounted pilgrim earns for every step his mount takes seventy good deeds, and the one on foot earns for every step he takes seven hundred good deeds of the good deeds of the Sanctuary. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the good deeds of the Sanctuary? He said: A good deed counts as a hundred thousand good deeds. And we do not know this hadith narrated with this wording except through this channel, though something close to its meaning has been narrated from Ibn Abbas with a different chain."
"5127","Ishaq ibn Shahin al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), regarding the saying of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: And do not compel your slave-girls to prostitution; he said: It was revealed concerning Abd Allah ibn Ubayy: he had a slave-girl whom he used to compel to fornication, so Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: For Allah, after their compulsion, is Forgiving, Merciful."
"5128","Ishaq ibn Shahin al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: Musa (peace be upon him) asked a request, and Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was granted it; His saying: And Musa chose seventy men of his people, up to His saying: So I shall ordain it for those who are God-fearing."
"5129","Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, he said: Al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard Layth narrating from Abu Fazarah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, or Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), raising the hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: These words are an incantation (ruqyah) for every ailment: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah and all His names, general, from the evil of the poisonous and the common, and from the evil of an envious eye, and from the evil of an envier when he envies, and from the evil of Abu Qatrah and his offspring. Thirty-three of the angels came to their Lord and said: An ailment, an ailment; He said: Take dust from your land and wipe your ailing ones with it; whoever takes payment for it, or conceals it from anyone, shall never prosper then, ever. And we do not know this hadith narrated with this wording except through this channel with this chain."
"5130","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: My father informed us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Hakim, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas and Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh (infused drink) of the earthen jar."
"5131","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"5132","Amr ibn Ali and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, they said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Thawr narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Abi Ata, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh of the earthen jar."
"5133","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Hayyan informed us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas and Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"5134","Hamdan ibn Ali al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ali ibn Muqaddam narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn Abi Amrah narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment in which was al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad. When they reached the people they found them dispersed, except one man of great wealth who had not left, who said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. Al-Miqdad attacked him and killed him. A man from his companions said to him: Did you kill a man who testifies that there is no god but Allah? By Allah, I shall surely mention that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When they came to the Prophet they said: O Messenger of Allah, a man testified that there is no god but Allah, yet al-Miqdad killed him. He said: Summon al-Miqdad for me. O Miqdad, did you kill a man who says: There is no god but Allah? How will you fare with: There is no god but Allah, tomorrow? Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: O you who believe, when you go forth in the way of Allah, verify, and do not say to one who offers you peace (or greeting; Abu Sa'id, meaning Ja'far ibn Salamah, doubted): You are not a believer, seeking the fleeting goods of worldly life; with Allah are abundant spoils; thus were you before. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-Miqdad: He was a believing man concealing his faith among a disbelieving people; he declared his faith and you killed him. Likewise you used to conceal your faith in Makkah before. And we do not know this hadith narrated with this wording except from Ibn Abbas, nor do we know for it any channel from Ibn Abbas except this channel."
"5135","Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Kamil, meaning Ibn al-Ala, narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Amrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say between the two prostrations: My Lord, forgive me, have mercy upon me, guide me, recompense me and grant me well-being, or the like of that."
"5136","Muhammad ibn Mu'awiyah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Abu Hashim, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Who is in Paradise? He said: The prophet is in Paradise, the martyr is in Paradise, the newborn is in Paradise, and the girl buried alive is in Paradise. And we do not know this hadith narrated with this wording from Ibn Abbas except through this channel with this chain, though these words have been narrated from the Prophet through other channels."
"5137","Muhammad ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yazid Abu Khalid, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever visits a sick person whose appointed time has not come and says seven times: I ask Allah the Almighty, Lord of the mighty Throne, to heal you, except that he is cured. And we do not know this hadith narrated with this wording except from Ibn Abbas, and its chain is fair (hasan)."
"5138","Muhammad ibn Abd al-A'la al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Abd Allah ibn Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Ibn Abbas. (The preserved text here ends with the chain at Ibn Abbas, without the raised wording recorded in this entry.)"
"5139","Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abd Allah ibn Sa'id, from his father, from Ibn Abbas. (A parallel chain for the preceding entry, likewise ending at Ibn Abbas in the preserved text.)"
"5140","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah and found the Jews fasting the day of Ashura; they were asked about that, and he (one of them) said: This is the day on which Allah granted Musa and the Children of Isra'il victory over Pharaoh, so we fast it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have more right to Musa than you. So he ordered fasting it. And this hadith about fasting Ashura has been narrated from Ibn Abbas through various channels with wordings, so we mentioned each hadith with its wording in its place."
"5141","Al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, he said: Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that a man was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while in ihram when his she-camel struck him (threw/crushed him) and he died. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him with water and lote-leaves, shroud him in his two garments, do not cover his head, do not touch him with perfume, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah (mulabbidan)."
"5142","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Salim al-Aftas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). (The raised wording is continued in the next entry: the hadith of the man in ihram trampled by his camel.)"
"5143","Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"5144","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, he said: Layth wrote to Sulayman ibn Tarkhan: Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah - or they mentioned from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) something like this: O Prophet of Allah, what of what we do? Is it something we initiate, or something already completed? He said: No, rather it is something already completed. He said: The people said to one another: Then (serious) striving is in order. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Habib except Layth, nor did anyone narrate it from Layth except Sulayman al-Taymi."
"5145","Bishr ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: O son of Adam, when you remember Me alone, I remember you alone; and when you remember Me in a company, I remember you in a company better than those among whom you remember Me. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas with this wording except through this channel."
"5146","Muhammad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Missisi narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Khasif, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There shall not enter Paradise (one with) a mustard-seed's weight of arrogance, nor shall there enter the Fire (one with) a mustard-seed's weight of faith. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet except through this channel with this chain."
"5147","Abbad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Hakim ibn Jubayr narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent (an expedition) to Khaybar - I think he said: Abu Bakr - and he returned defeated along with those with him. The next day he sent Umar, and he returned defeated, declaring his companions cowardly and they declaring him cowardly. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall surely give the banner tomorrow to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love; he shall not return until Allah grants victory through him. The people stirred (in anticipation). He said: Where is Ali? And he was complaining of his eye. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spat in his eye, then handed him the banner; he shook it, and Allah granted victory through him. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet except through this channel with this chain."
"5148","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Qays, from Abu Awn, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: Banu Asad came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we embraced Islam while the Arabs fought you, and we did not fight you. So the Messenger of Allah said: Their understanding is scant, and Satan speaks upon their tongues. And this verse was revealed: They remind you that they embraced Islam; say: Do not remind me of your Islam - the verse. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except Ibn Abbas, nor any channel from Ibn Abbas except this channel; and we do not know of Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah narrating from Sa'id ibn Jubayr with a connected chain any hadith other than this one. And Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah is Abu Awn."
"5149","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Sahba narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of my household is like the ark of Nuh: whoever boards it is saved, and whoever lags behind it drowns. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far; and al-Hasan was not strong, though a group of the people of knowledge narrated from him and accepted his hadith, and he was among the worshippers."
"5150","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl, Abd al-Malik ibn Hawdhah ibn Khalifah and Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Sa'igh narrated to us, they said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Abd Allah al-Qummi narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am ruined. He said: What has ruined you? He said: I turned my mount (i.e. approached my wife from behind) last night. He did not answer him with anything. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed this verse: Your women are tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish. He said, meaning: Come from the front and from behind, but avoid the anus and (intercourse during) menstruation. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas except through this channel with this chain."
"5151","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Yahya ibn Zabban al-Anazi narrated to us, he said: Hibban ibn Ali narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one day the dawn prayer then said: Is there anyone here from Hudhayl? Your companion is detained at the gate of Paradise - I think he said: on account of his debt. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas except through this channel, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah except Hibban ibn Ali."
"5152","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Habib - meaning Ibn Abi Amrah - narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), regarding the saying of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: Whatever you cut of palm-trees or leave standing upon their roots, it is by Allah's permission, and that He may disgrace the transgressors. He said: Al-linah is the palm-tree. And: That He may disgrace the transgressors: He said: They brought them down from their fortresses, and they were commanded to cut the palms. They said: We have cut some, so let us ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Is there for us in what we cut any reward, and is there upon us in what we left any sin? So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: Whatever you cut of linah is by Allah's permission, and whatever you left is by Allah's permission."
"5153","Salamah ibn Shabib and Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, they said: Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from his father Ibrahim ibn Umar, he said: Wahb ibn Manus narrated to us, that he heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrating from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head from bowing, he said: Our Lord, to You is praise filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will of things thereafter."
"5154","Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Hushaym ibn Bashir narrated to us, he said: Abu Bishr narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to admit the people of Badr and admit me along with them. Some of them said: Do you admit this youth along with us when among our sons are those like him? Umar said: He is among those who are learned. One day he admitted them and admitted me with them, and asked them about this surah: When the help of Allah comes, and the victory. They said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, commanded His Prophet, when Allah granted him victory, to seek His forgiveness and turn to Him. He said: What do you say, O Ibn Abbas? I said: Not so; rather He informed His Prophet of the approach of his appointed time, saying: When the help of Allah comes, and the victory - the conquest of Makkah - and you see people entering Allah's religion in crowds: that is the sign of your death; so glorify with the praise of your Lord and seek His forgiveness; indeed He is ever Accepting of repentance. So Umar said to them: How can you blame me for him after what you have seen?"
"5155","Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Makkah, Abu Bakr said: To Allah we belong and to Him we return; the Messenger of Allah has been expelled - they will all perish. When this verse was revealed: Permission is given to those who are fought because they were wronged, and indeed Allah is able to grant them victory - those who were expelled from their homes, Abu Bakr knew that there would be fighting."
"5156","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The jinn used to sit toward the heaven listening to the revelation; when they heard a word they would add to it manifold, so the (original) word would be true while the rest would be false - until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent, and they were barred from their seats, and the stars had not been pelted (as missiles) before that. Iblis said to them: This is only on account of some matter that has occurred on earth. So he dispatched his troops, and they found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing in prayer, and they informed him. He said: This is the event that has occurred on earth."
"5157","Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Dharr narrated to us, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Jibril (peace be upon him): Why do you not visit us more often than you visit us? So there was revealed: And we descend only by the command of your Lord - the verse."
"5158","Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Samurah narrated to us, he said: Asbat narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them to stone the pillar (Jamrah) until the sun had risen."
"5159","Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the dawn prayer on Friday reciting: Alif Lam Mim, the Revelation, and: Has there come upon man. And the hadith of Asbat from Ash'ath contains an error by Ash'ath; rather it is from Salamah from al-Hasan al-Urani from Ibn Abbas."
"5160","Abu Burayd Amr ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Sayf ibn Ubayd Allah al-Jarmi narrated to us, he said: Warqa narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A person is commanded to prostrate upon seven bones: his hands, his feet, his knees and his face. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ata with a connected chain except Warqa."
"5161","Zayd ibn Akhzam and Hamdan ibn Ali al-Baghdadi narrated to us, they said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Uqbah ibn Abi Thubayt, from Abu al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise are those whose ears you fill with good that you hear of them, and the people of the Fire are those whose ears you fill with evil that you hear of them. I heard Hamdan ibn Ali say: I heard Muslim say: It reached me that Uqbah ibn Abi Thubayt used to call birds and they would answer him."
"5162","Ahmad ibn Sinan narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who witnesses is not like one who is (merely) informed: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, informed Musa that his people had been put to trial, yet he did not cast the tablets; but when he saw them, he cast the tablets. (Here ends the portion of forty.) And praise be to Allah abundantly as He deserves, and blessings upon Muhammad the Chosen and his family, and peace in abundance."
"5163","Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib ibn Yahya al-Raqqi informed us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Hisham Abu al-Miqdam narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, created Paradise white; so the most beloved garments to Allah are white - let your living wear them and shroud your dead in them. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except through this channel; and Habib ibn al-Shahid did not narrate with a connected chain from Ata from Ibn Abbas any hadith other than this one, nor did anyone narrate it from Habib except Kathir ibn Hisham. And Hisham is a Basran man, unobjectionable, from whom a group of the people of knowledge narrated."
"5164","Isa ibn Harun al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: For a boy are two aqiqahs, and for a girl one aqiqah. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except through this channel with this chain; rather what is narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is: For a boy two sheep, and for a girl one sheep. And Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad did not narrate with a connected chain from Ata from Ibn Abbas any hadith other than this one, nor did anyone narrate it from Yazid except Imran ibn Uyaynah and Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash."
"5165","Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Kufi Abu Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And there is disagreement over this hadith from Ata: it is narrated from Ata from Habibah bint Maysarah from Umm Kurz, thus; Amr ibn Dinar and al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated it so. And Qays ibn Sa'd narrated it from Ata from Umm Kurz, without inserting Habibah bint Maysarah between them."
"5166","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari and Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Sa'igh narrated to us, they said: Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The value of the shield (for the theft-cutting threshold) in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was ten dirhams. And we only mentioned this hadith - though nothing of it is attributed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in words - because he said: Its value in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was ten dirhams, which indicates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only cut (the hand) for a shield worth ten dirhams. Ibn Abbas mentioned the value on his own authority, just as Abd Allah ibn Umar mentioned on his own authority, saying: Its value was three dirhams. And we do not know of Ayyub ibn Musa narrating from Ata from Ibn Abbas any hadith other than this one."
"5167","Al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah ibn al-Bazzar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Salim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik - meaning Ibn Abi Sulayman - narrated to me, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first with which a servant is recompensed after his death is that all who followed his funeral are forgiven. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel, nor do we know anyone who narrated it except Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Marwan ibn Salim is lenient in hadith; Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan Abu Hammam al-Ahwazi and Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated it from him. And we do not know of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman narrating with a connected chain from Ata from Ibn Abbas except two hadiths, this being one of them, the other being: I spent the night at my aunt Maymunah's."
"5168","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas. He did not establish it (with wording) because we had already brought it through others besides Abd al-Malik from Ata; and two men narrated it from Abd al-Malik: Khalid ibn al-Harith and Ishaq ibn Yusuf. (A registrar entry without the raised wording recorded here.)"
"5169","Muhammad ibn Mu'awiyah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, he said: Al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling palm-fruits two or three years (in advance): that they be bought atop the palms by measure, or that fruit be sold until its ripeness appears. And we do not know anyone who narrates this hadith with this wording with a chain better than this chain."
"5170","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not stone (the pillars) until the sun had declined - meaning: in what was after the Day of Sacrifice. And we do not know this hadith narrated with this wording except from Ibn Abbas; rather it is narrated that he (the Prophet) used to stone in the forenoon."
"5171","Al-Hasan ibn Khalaf al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gifted one hundred sacrificial camels, garlanded and caparisoned. And this hadith has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); it is narrated from Ibn Abbas through other channels that he gifted one hundred camels, among them a camel of Abu Jahl - without saying garlanded and caparisoned."
"5172","Ubayd Allah ibn Sa'd ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: My uncle Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while I was circumcised (khatin, i.e. already circumcised). And this hadith has been narrated from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, but they differed in its wording: Abu Ishaq reported from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while I was circumcised; while Abu Bishr reported from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while I was twelve years old. So we mentioned the hadith of al-Hajjaj from Ata from Ibn Abbas because he corroborated Abu Ishaq from Sa'id from Ibn Abbas in his narration."
"5173","Abd Allah ibn Sa'id al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj. And this hadith has been narrated from others besides Ibn Abbas, so we mentioned this hadith in this place with this wording; Ibn Jurayj also narrated it."
"5174","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"5175","Abd Allah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a dead sheep with its leg raised and said: What harm would it do its owners if they benefited from its hide? So Sawdah tanned it and made nabidh in it. And we only mentioned this hadith because it contains an addition we wished to bring out, on account of the status of the addition therein."
"5176","Ubayd ibn Bakhit narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Khasif narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I declared zihar upon my wife, then I saw her leg in the moonlight and had intercourse with her before expiating. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Expiate, and do not repeat. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ata from Ibn Abbas except through this channel, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Khasif except Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Rahman."
"5177","Amr ibn Ali and Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Ammi narrated to us, they said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If the son of Adam had a valley filled with wealth, he would love to have another like it; and nothing fills the soul of the son of Adam but dust, and Allah turns to whoever turns (to Him). And we only mentioned this hadith - though it is narrated from a group from the Prophet - because Yazid ibn al-Asamm narrated it from Ibn Abbas from Ubayy (ibn Ka'b), while in the hadith of Ibn Jurayj from Ata from Ibn Abbas he said: I heard the Prophet - so we mentioned it to clarify that discrepancy. And Ibn Jurayj is more retentive than those who narrated it from Yazid al-Asamm, and Ata is more retentive than Yazid ibn al-Asamm."
"5178","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that he invited his brother Ubayd Allah on the Day of Arafah and food was brought; he (Ubayd Allah) said: I am fasting. He (Ibn Abbas) said: You are a household taken as an example; I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought a milk-pail of milk on such a day as this, and he drank. And this hadith has been narrated from Ibn Abbas with another chain: Ayyub narrated it from Ikrimah, and they differed over Ayyub - some said from Ikrimah, others said from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. And Ibn Jurayj from Ata from Ibn Abbas is dearer to us than Ayyub from Ikrimah."
"5179","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: I attended with Ibn Abbas the funeral of Maymunah, and he said: This is the wife of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so do not shake or disturb her (bier), for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had nine wives; he would apportion among eight and not apportion to one. Ata said: The one to whom he did not apportion was Safiyyah bint Huyayy ibn Akhtab. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas with a chain better than this chain; though it has been narrated with a different chain from Ibn Abbas. What is otherwise preserved from Ibn Abbas through another channel is that the one to whom no portion was assigned was Sawdah bint Zam'ah, because she gifted her day to A'ishah."
"5180","Abu Kurayb and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ramal (brisk walking) in his Hajj and his Umrah, as did Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman and the caliphs. And Amr ibn Ali added: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ramal for three (circuits) and walked four. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas with this wording except through this channel; and we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith with a connected chain from Ibn Jurayj except Abu Mu'awiyah, while others besides Abu Mu'awiyah narrated it from Ibn Jurayj from Ata without a connected chain (mursal)."
"5181","Muhammad ibn Harb al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Silah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs Hajj on behalf of his parents, or settles a debt on their behalf, will be raised with the righteous. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel, nor do we know for it any channel other than this one; and Silah ibn Sulayman is a Wasiti man whose family originated in Basrah then moved to Wasit, and Silah was not corroborated in this hadith."
"5182","Muhammad ibn Harb al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Umayr ibn Imran narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel, nor do we know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Umayr ibn Imran, a Basran man, and he was not corroborated in this hadith."
"5183","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you eats food, let him not wipe his hand until he licks it, or has it licked. And the like of these words has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through other channels; and we do not know any chain narrated in this regard better or sounder than this chain."
"5184","Abd Allah ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas and Jabir ibn Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with them), they said: There was no call to prayer (adhan) for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on (the days of) Fitr or Adha. And this hadith has been narrated from Jabir through other channels, and it is narrated from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas; and the hadith of Ibn Jurayj from Ata is better than the hadith of al-Hakam from Miqsam. And we do not know anyone who joined both of them - from Ata from Ibn Abbas and Jabir - except Ibn Jurayj; and we have not heard anyone narrate it from Abu Asim except Abd Allah ibn Ishaq, and he was well-known and trustworthy in hadith."
"5185","Ahmad ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed forty sa's (of grain) from a man of the Ansar. The Ansari then needed it and came to him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing has come to us yet. He said: Then he needed it again and came to him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing has come to us yet. The man then wished to speak, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say nothing but good, for I am the best of borrowers. Then he gave him forty extra and forty for his loan, giving him eighty. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a connected chain except through this channel with this chain; and we heard this hadith only from Ahmad ibn Khuzaymah, and he was trustworthy."
"5186","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I owe a sacrificial camel (badanah) while I can afford it, but cannot find one. He said: Slaughter a sheep. And we do not know anyone who narrated this with a connected chain except Yahya ibn Ayyub from Ibn Jurayj; others narrated it as stopped (mawquf)."
"5187","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Qudamah ibn Muhammad ibn Qudamah narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Shaybah al-Ta'ifi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None shall enter the gate of the Fire except a man who satisfies his rage at the cost of Allah's wrath. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except through this channel with this chain; and Qudamah ibn Muhammad is unobjectionable, while Isma'il ibn Shaybah is one from whom Ibn Jurayj narrated several hadiths in which he was not corroborated."
"5188","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim, the associate of al-Sabiri, narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He fixed Dhat Irq as the miqat for the people of the East. And we do not know this hadith narrated except from Ibn Abbas with this chain, nor do we know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Muslim ibn Khalid."
"5189","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), regarding one in ihram: He may wear leather socks if he cannot find sandals - and he did not say: Let him cut them. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Muslim ibn Khalid; and Muslim was unobjectionable, though not retentive, and was among the jurists of Makkah."
"5190","Muhammad ibn Abi Ghalib narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about ghayl (intercourse while nursing), and said: Had it harmed anyone, it would have harmed Persia and Rome. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas except through this channel, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Ibn Jurayj except Isa ibn Yunus."
"5191","Amr ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Al-Harith ibn Ghassan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every newborn is born upon the fitrah; then his parents make him a Jew or a Christian. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj from Ata from Ibn Abbas except al-Harith ibn Ghassan, a Basran man, unobjectionable."
"5192","Shu'ayb ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that Muhammad saw his Lord - meaning with his heart. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Sufyan al-Thawri from Ibn Jurayj other than Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham."
"5193","Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi Hayyah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Religion shall remain firmly established as long as twenty men of Quraysh remain. And we do not know this hadith narrated with this wording from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel; and Ibrahim ibn Abi Hayyah is one whom we do not know to have been corroborated in this hadith, and he is a man not strong in hadith. We only recorded it because we have not preserved it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel. And Ibn Abi Hayyah is a Yemeni."
"5194","Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Shabib narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abbad al-Sa'di narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded a crier to cry out in the valley of Makkah ordering the charity of Fitr, saying: It is a due obligation upon every Muslim, male or female, young or old, free or slave, resident or nomad: two mudds of wheat, or a sa' of other foodstuffs. Verily the child belongs to the (marriage) bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Yahya ibn Abbad, nor anyone who narrated it from Yahya ibn Abbad except Dawud ibn Shabib; though most of the words of this hadith have been narrated through other channels - except resident or nomad, for this phrase is not narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel."
"5195","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Al-Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ata, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) say: A sheep died, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the owners of the sheep: Why did you not tan its hide and then benefit from it?"
"5196","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A domestic goat of Maymunah died, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not benefit from its hide?"
"5197","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A sheep belonging to one of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not benefit from its hide? And this hadith has been narrated from Ibn Abbas with different wordings, and it has been narrated from others besides Ibn Abbas with similar meaning but different wording; and we mentioned each hadith in its place with its wording."
"5198","Muqaddam ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Ata ibn Muqaddam narrated to us, he said: My uncle al-Qasim ibn Yahya ibn Ata ibn Muqaddam narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). (An entry preserving the chain to the Prophet, with wording supplied through the parallel narrations about benefiting from the tanned hide.)"
"5199","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). (A parallel chain for the hide-benefit hadith, likewise ending at the Prophet in the preserved text.)"
"5200","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id - meaning Ibn Sulayman - narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Zadham, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I shaved before slaughtering. He said: Slaughter, and no harm. Another said: I shaved before stoning. He said: Stone, and no harm. Another said: I visited the House before stoning. He said: Stone, and no harm. And this wording is the wording of Ibn Khuthaym; while Abd al-Aziz said in his hadith: I visited before stoning - he said: Stone, and no harm; he said: I shaved before stoning - he said: Stone, and no harm; he said: I sacrificed before stoning - he said: Stone, and no harm. And others than those we mentioned narrated this hadith from Ata from Jabir: Usamah ibn Zayd and Qays ibn Sa'd narrated it from Ata from Jabir; so we mentioned it due to their disagreement over Ata, to clarify that. And the hadith of Mansur ibn Zadham is one we do not know anyone to have narrated except Hushaym; and we do not know of Ibn Khuthaym narrating with a connected chain from Ata from Ibn Abbas any hadith other than this, nor of Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay' narrating with a connected chain from Ata from Ibn Abbas any hadith other than this one."
"5201","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim Ja'far ibn Yahya ibn Thawban narrated to us, from his uncle Umarah ibn Thawban, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best rows of men are the first of them, and the worst of them are the last of them; and the worst rows of women are the first of them, and the best of them are the last of them."
"5202","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Yahya ibn Thawban narrated to us, from his uncle Umarah ibn Thawban, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you are those softest in the shoulders during prayer."
"5203","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Yahya ibn Thawban narrated to us, from his uncle Umarah ibn Thawban, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted striking women; then at night he heard a loud clamor and said: I hear a loud clamor. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you permitted striking women. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you are the best of you to their families, and I am the best of you to my family. And we do not know these hadiths narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; and Ja'far ibn Yahya and his uncle are Makkans of concealed (unknown) status."
"5204","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab - meaning Ibn Abd al-Majid - narrated to us, from Habib al-Mu'allim, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to send the weak (the baggage and women) before dawn, and I was among them. And this hadith has been narrated by a group from Ata from Ibn Abbas, and from Ikrimah; and we do not know it narrated through the hadith of Habib al-Mu'allim from Ata from Ibn Abbas except through this channel. And Habib al-Mu'allim is a trustworthy Basran."
"5205","Abd Allah ibn Sa'id Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj and al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Al-Minhal ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) buried a man in a grave at night, kindled a lamp for him, laid him in the lahd from the direction of the qiblah, magnified (takbir) over him four times, and said: May Allah have mercy upon you; you were indeed oft-sighing with the Qur'an, oft-reciting the Qur'an. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Yahya ibn Yaman from Minhal ibn Khalifah with this chain, nor do we know these words narrated except through this channel. Yahya ibn al-Yaman is a well-known trustworthy Kufan, al-Minhal ibn Khalifah a well-known Kufan, and al-Hajjaj ibn Artah also a Kufan; and Hajjaj was over the judiciary of Kufah."
"5206","Abd Allah ibn Sa'id Abu Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Ash'ath ibn Sawwar narrated to us, from Ata. And al-Husayn ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Asal ibn Sufyan, from Ata, he said: Ibn al-Zubayr led the people in the Maghrib prayer and gave salutations after two (rak'ahs), then stood toward the Stone to touch it; they prompted him with glorification (tasbih), so he returned, prayed the remaining rak'ah, gave salutations, and prostrated twice. That was mentioned to Ibn Abbas, and he said: He did not deviate from the practice (sunnah) of his Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith has been narrated from Ata by a group besides those we named, so we sufficed with those we named."
"5207","Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ya'qub ibn Ata - meaning Ibn Abi Rabah - from his father, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he married Maymunah while in ihram."
"5208","Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah while in ihram. And a group narrated this hadith from Ata from Ibn Abbas, among them: Ma'qil ibn Ubayd Allah, Abu al-Zubayr, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir and others. As for the hadith of Ya'qub ibn Ata from his father from Ibn Abbas, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ya'qub except Shu'bah. Ma'qil ibn Ubayd Allah is a trustworthy Jazari."
"5209","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar and al-Sakan ibn Sa'id narrated to us, they said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ya'qub ibn Ata, from his father, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A sheep of Maymunah died, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not make use of its hide? He said: The tanning of the skin is its purification. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ya'qub ibn Ata from his father except Shu'bah; though it has been narrated from Ata from Ibn Abbas through various channels."
"5210","Muhammad ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from Ya'qub ibn Ata, from his father, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr and Asr together on the Day of Arafah, praying Zuhr with adhan and iqamah and Asr with iqamah, without supererogatory prayer between them. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ya'qub ibn Ata with this chain except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash."
"5211","Tulayq ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Mu'ammal - a well-known Makkan - narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mihsan narrated to me, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, raising it (to the Prophet), he said: Whoever enters the House (the Ka'bah) enters into a good deed, then leaves forgiven. And we do not know these words narrated from Ibn Abbas except through this channel."
"5212","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Makhramah ibn Sulayman, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I spent the night at my aunt Maymunah's, and said: I shall surely observe the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). A cushion was laid for me, and I slept across it; he and his family slept, then he rose at midnight, or shortly before or after it, wiping sleep from his face, then recited the last verses of Al Imran until he completed them. Then he stood, went to a hanging waterskin, took it, performed ablution, then stood and prayed. I too stood, did as he had done, then came and stood beside him; he placed his hand upon my head, then turned me, placing me at his right. Then he prayed two rak'ahs, then two, then two, then two, then prayed witr. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from Ibn Abbas; though it has been narrated through various channels, each adding wording over the other, so we mention each hadith in its place with its wording."
"5213","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I stood with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at his left, and he placed me at his right. And we do not know of Abu Sufyan narrating from Kurayb from Ibn Abbas any hadith other than this one."
"5214","Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Rishdin ibn Kurayb narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from Satan - from his hamz (pricking/madness), his nafkh (blowing) - I think he said: and his nafth (spittle-poetry) - and from the punishment of the grave. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this you seek refuge from? He said: As for his hamz, it is what he whispers; as for his nafth, it is poetry; as for his nafkh, it is what is cast of doubts - meaning: in prayer, to interrupt his prayer, or (cast) upon a person (to interrupt) his prayer. As for the punishment of the grave, he used to say: Most of the punishment of the grave is on account of urine. And the like of this hadith's wording has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through other channels; and in this hadith there is an explanation not found in the hadith of others, so for that reason we mentioned it."
"5215","Al-Qasim ibn Wuhayb al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, he said: Mindal narrated to us, from Rishdin ibn Kurayb, from his father, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am the delegate of women to you: this jihad Allah has prescribed upon men - if they strive they are rewarded, and if they are killed they are alive with their Lord, provided for; while we, the company of women, maintain (affairs) for them - so what is for us of that? He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Convey to those women you meet that obedience to the husband and acknowledgment of his right equals that, though few among you do it. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel with this chain; and Rishdin ibn Kurayb is one from whom a group of trustworthy people of knowledge narrated and accepted his hadith."
"5216","Isma'il ibn Ya'qub al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from his father, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The parable of one who prays with his head tied up (in a knot) is like one who prays bound. And this hadith has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through another channel, and this hadith is the finest channel narrated in this regard."
"5217","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, freedman of the family of Talhah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The name of Juwayriyah was Barrah, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed her name and called her Juwayriyah. He passed by her while she was in her prayer-place glorifying Allah and remembering Allah after the forenoon had risen, and said: O Juwayriyah, have you remained in your place? She said: I have remained in this place of mine. He said: I have spoken four phrases better than what you have said. She said: I said: How? He said: I said: Glory be to Allah as many as His creation; glory be to Allah to His own pleasure; glory be to Allah to the weight of His Throne; glory be to Allah to the extent of His words - and praise be to Allah likewise. And this hadith has been narrated similarly through other channels with a different wording, so we brought out each hadith with its wording in its place."
"5218","Abd Allah ibn Sa'id al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Makhramah ibn Sulayman, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not look at a man who approaches a man, or a woman, in the anus. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abbas with a chain better than this chain."
"5219","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, he said: Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Makhul, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-Abbas: When it is the morning of Monday, come to me, you and your children, that I may supplicate for you with a supplication through which Allah will benefit you. So he came in the morning, and we came in the morning with him, and he said: O Allah, forgive al-Abbas and his children with a forgiveness outward and inward, leaving no sin; O Allah, preserve him in his offspring."
"5220","Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Fahham narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Thawr narrated to us, from Makhul, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Thawr except Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata, nor do we know anyone who corroborated him in its narration; nor do we know it narrated from Ibn Abbas except through this channel, nor do we know of Makhul narrating with a connected chain from Kurayb any hadith other than this one. And Abd al-Wahhab is a Basran who moved to Baghdad; nothing was recorded from him in Basrah, then he came to Baghdad and narrated. One of his companions informed me that he wrote to his family that it had been recorded from him, so praise Allah. And this hadith, in my view, has no basis; I think he narrated it in the days of al-Rashid because he gave him something."
"5221","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Duba'i, he said: told us Ali ibn Ghurab, he said: told us Rashdin ibn Kurayb, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he drank would breathe twice in the vessel. And this hadith has been reported from Anas that he would breathe three times, and we do not know it reported with this wording from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through the narration of Ibn Abbas from him, and we do not know for it any chain other than this chain."
"5222","And narrated to us Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah, he said: told us Ubaydullah ibn Musa, he said: told us Sufyan al-Thawri, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept until he snored, then he stood and prayed and did not perform ablution."
"5223","Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Arafah, he said: told us Ibrahim ibn Sulayman Abu Ismail al-Mu'addib, he said: told us Rashdin ibn Kurayb, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not imitate the non-Arabs; change the beards. And this hadith, we do not know it reported with this wording except from Ibn Abbas with this chain."
"5224","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abd al-Jabbar, he said: told us Yunus ibn Bukayr, he said: told us Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn al-Walid ibn Nuwayfi', from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas."
"5225","Narrated to us Salamah, he said: told us Hafs ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn al-Walid, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, and the wording is the wording of Yunus, he said: Dimam ibn Tha'labah, one of Banu Sa'd ibn Bakr, came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was a strong man, hairy, with two braids; so he tied his camel at the door of the mosque, then entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and stood before him while he was among his companions, and said: Which of you is the son of Abd al-Muttalib? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Here I am, the son of Abd al-Muttalib. He said: Are you Muhammad? He said: Yes. He said: O son of Abd al-Muttalib, I am going to ask you and be harsh in the question, so do not feel resentment in yourself. He said: Ask whatever comes to you, and I will not feel resentment toward you in myself. He said: I adjure you by Allah, your God and the God of those before you and the God of those who will come after you: did Allah send you to us as a messenger? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah, your God and the God of those before you and the God of those who will come after you: did Allah command you to order us to cast off these idols which our forefathers used to worship, and to worship Allah associating nothing with Him? He said: O Allah, yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah, your God and the God of those before you and the God of those who will come after you: did Allah command you that we pray these five prayers? He said: O Allah, yes. He said: Then he went through the obligations one by one, naming them to him, until when he finished, he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and messenger, and I will act upon these obligations, neither adding to them nor decreasing. Then he turned away, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the man with the two braids is truthful he will enter Paradise. He said: Then he went to his camel, untied its hobble, then set off until he came to his people; when they gathered to him they said: What is behind you, O Dimam? He began to revile al-Lat and al-Uzza. They said: Stop, fear leprosy, fear elephantiasis, fear madness. He said: Woe to you, you are upon nothing but falsehood; by Allah, they neither harm nor benefit. Allah has sent a messenger and sent down upon him a book and obligated a religion upon him, and I have brought you what he is upon. He said: By Allah, by evening of that day there remained neither man nor woman in his settlement except as a Muslim. He said: We never heard of a delegation like Dimam ibn Tha'labah. And this hadith, we do not know it reported with this wording except from this route with this chain."
"5226","Narrated to us Ali ibn al-Mundhir, he said: told us Muhammad ibn Fudayl, he said: told us al-A'mash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: My father sent me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with some camels he had given him from the charity camels; when I came to him, and it was the night of Maymunah his maternal aunt, he went to the mosque and prayed Isha, then came, meaning to his house, and cast off his garment, then entered with his wife in her garments. He said: Then I took my garment and wrapped myself in it, then lay down, then said: I will not sleep tonight until I see what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) does. So he slept until he snored, until when as much of the night as Allah willed to pass had passed, he stood and went out and came to a vessel or a tied-up waterskin and untied its knot, then poured water over it, then stepped upon the mouth of the waterskin and began to wash his hands and performed ablution until he finished; and I wanted to stand to pour over him. Then he stood praying, so I stood and did the like of what he did, and I stood at his left, so he took hold of me and placed me at his right. He said: So he prayed thirteen rak'ahs, then lay down until Bilal came to him and announced the prayer to him. He said: So he stood and prayed two rak'ahs before Fajr. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who reported it from Habib, from Kurayb, other than Muhammad ibn Fudayl; and al-Thawri and Husayn differed from him, saying: from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abdillah ibn Abbas, from his father, from Ibn Abbas."
"5227","And narrated to us Nasr ibn Ali, he said: Abu Ahmad informed us, he said: told us Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Ali ibn Abdillah ibn Abbas, from his father. And as for the hadith of al-Thawri:"
"5228","Then narrated it to us Abdah ibn Abdillah, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham informed us, from Sufyan, from Habib, meaning Ibn Abi Thabit, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from his father, from Ibn Abbas."
"5229","Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Arafah, he said: told us Hushaym, from Husayn, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Habib, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, with the like of the hadith of Sufyan from Habib."
"5230","Narrated to us Amr ibn Ali, he said: told us Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad, he said: told us Mansur, from Salim, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5231","Narrated it to us Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali, they said: told us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, he said: told us Shu'bah, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If one of you, when he comes to his wife, says: O Allah, keep Satan away from me and keep Satan away from what You provide us, then there is a child between them — Shu'bah said: Satan will not gain power over him, or: Satan will not attend him; and Ibn Abd al-Samad said: Satan will never attend him."
"5232","And narrated it to us Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari, he said: told us Abu Usamah, he said: told us al-A'mash, from Salim, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. And this hadith was reported by a group from Mansur, so we sufficed with those we named; and we do not know this speech reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this route. And as for the hadith of al-A'mash, we do not know anyone who transmitted it in marfu' form except Abu Usamah; and others besides Abu Usamah reported it as mawquf."
"5233","Narrated to us Amr ibn Ali, he said: told us Yahya ibn Sa'id, he said: told us Sufyan, he said: told us Muhammad ibn Uqbah and Ibrahim ibn Uqbah, from Kurayb — one of them said: from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both — that a woman lifted a boy to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Is there Hajj for this one? He said: Yes, and for you is a reward."
"5234","Narrated to us Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani, he said: told us Sa'id ibn al-Hakam, he said: told us Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Kathir, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to me, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a gold ring on a man's hand, so he pulled it off and threw it away and said: One of you resorts to a coal of fire and places it in his hand. It was said to the man after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had gone: Take your ring and benefit from it. He said: No, by Allah, I will never take it, since the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw it away. And this hadith, we do not know it reported with this wording except from Ibn Abbas with this chain; and something like it has been reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from various routes with different wordings."
"5235","Narrated to us Sahl ibn Bahr, he said: told us Muhammad ibn al-Salt Abu Ya'la, he said: told us Yahya ibn Sulaym, from Humayd ibn Ziyad, from Kurayb, he said: A son of Ibn Abbas died, so he said: O Kurayb, go out and see whether anyone has gathered for my son. So I went out and said: Forty or more have gathered. He said: Bring him out, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no dead person over whom forty or more pray and intercede for him except that their intercession for him is accepted. And this hadith, we do not know it from Ibn Abbas except from this route; and it has been reported from others besides Ibn Abbas, and they differed in its chain, so we mentioned the hadith of Ibn Abbas because there is no disagreement in its chain."
"5236","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Umarah ibn Subayh, he said: told us al-Hasan ibn Bishr, he said: told us Sharik, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My sister vowed to perform Hajj walking. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has no need of your sister's hardship; let her perform Hajj riding and let her expiate her oath. And al-Hakam — we do not know that he reported from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas."
"5237","The hadith of Ali ibn Abdillah: Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abdah, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Abdillah ibn Abbas, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate a shoulder, or tore meat from a shoulder, then prayed and did not perform ablution. And this hadith has been reported from Ibn Abbas from various routes, and from others besides Ibn Abbas; we mention each hadith of them in its place with its wording."
"5238","Narrated to us Abdallah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbawayh al-Marwazi, he said: told us Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: told us Ibn Abi Layla, from Dawud ibn Ali, from his father, from his grandfather Abdallah ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not sit in the sitting places; if you must do so, then return the greeting, lower the gazes, guide the way, and help with carrying loads. And this speech, something like it has been reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with different wordings; and we do not know it reported in the hadith: and help with carrying loads, except in this hadith; and we do not know for Ibn Abbas any chain other than this chain. And Dawud ibn Ali was of high lineage but was not strong in hadith, though nothing is imagined of him except truthfulness; and there is only written from his hadith what none other reported."
"5239","Narrated to us Abdallah ibn Ahmad, he said: told us Muhammad ibn Imran, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to me, from Dawud ibn Ali, from his father, from his grandfather Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say."
"5240","And narrated it to us Muhammad ibn al-Wazir al-Wasiti, he said: told us Yazid ibn Harun, he said: told us Qays, from al-Hasan al-Bajali, from Dawud ibn Ali, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, and the wording is the wording of Ibn Abi Layla. He said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he finished his prayer, say: O Allah, I ask You for mercy from Yourself by which You guide my heart, unite my affair, mend my disarray, set right my absent, raise my present, purify my deed, restore my affection, and make me free of need of any besides You. O Allah, grant me faith after which there is no disbelief, and mercy by which I attain the honor of Your nobility in this world and the Hereafter. O Allah, I ask You for the lodging of the martyrs, the life of the felicitous, and victory over the enemies. O Allah, I have laid my need before You; though my judgment fall short, my deed be weak, and I stand in need of Your mercy. O Allah, O Decider of affairs and O Healer of what is in the breasts, grant me refuge from the punishment of the Blaze, from the call of perdition, and from the trial of the graves. O Allah, whatever my judgment falls short of and my asking has not reached of good — I think he said: that You gave to anyone of Your creation, or good that You will give to anyone of Your servants — I desire it of You and ask You for it by Your mercy, O Lord of the worlds. O Allah, I ask You, O Possessor of the strong rope and O Possessor of the right command — O Allah, I ask You for security on the Day of Threat and Paradise on the Day of Eternity with the near, the witnessing, the bowing, the prostrating, those who fulfill the covenants; indeed You are Merciful, Loving, and You are witness over all things, doing what You will. O Allah, make us guides, rightly guided, neither straying nor leading astray, at peace with Your allies, hostile to Your enemies; we love people by Your love and show enmity by Your enmity to whoever opposes You. O Allah, this is the supplication and upon You is the answering, and this is the striving and upon You is reliance. Grant for me light in my grave, light in my heart, light before me, light behind me, light on my right, light on my left, light before me, light behind me, light above me, light beneath me, light in my hearing, light in my sight, light in my hair, light in my skin, light in my flesh, light in my bones — I think he said: and magnify for me light with You. Glory be to Him who wrapped Himself in might, and said thereby; glory be to Allah who clothed Himself in glory and generosity; glory be to Him whom glorification befits none but Him; glory be to the Possessor of bounty and blessings; glory be to the Possessor of glory and nobility; glory be to the Possessor of majesty and honor. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with these wordings and this completeness except from this route with this chain; and our mention of Dawud ibn Ali has preceded, so we sufficed with that from repeating his mention thereafter."
"5241","Narrated to us Mahmud ibn Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: told us Isa ibn al-Mukhtar, from Muhammad ibn Abi Layla, from Dawud ibn Ali ibn Abdillah ibn Abbas, from his father, from Ibn Abbas."
"5242","And narrated it to us Ahmad ibn Uthman, he said: told us Bakr, he said: told us Isa, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Dawud ibn Ali, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while fasting at al-Qahah, and he bled until it was feared for him."
"5243","And narrated it to us Ahmad ibn Uthman, he said: told us Bakr, from Isa ibn al-Mukhtar, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. And this hadith has been reported from Ibn Abbas from various routes: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while fasting; but they did not mention in their hadiths from Ibn Abbas: he bled until it was feared for him."
"5244","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim, he said: told us Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: told us Isa, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Dawud ibn Ali, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said concerning the fast of Ashura: Fast it and differ from the Jews in it; fast a day before it and a day after it. And this hadith has been reported from Ibn Abbas from various routes; and we do not know it reported from Ibn Abbas nor from other than Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that a day before it and a day after it be fasted except in the hadith of Dawud ibn Ali, from his father, from Ibn Abbas. And our mention of Dawud has preceded."
"5245","Narrated to us Mahmud ibn Bakr, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: told us Isa ibn al-Mukhtar, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Dawud ibn Ali, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that some people of Mudar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are people of Mudar, a year of drought has struck us; we have come to you, and no stallion roars for us and no container provisions for us. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, give us rain. And they did not move until they were given rain. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from Ibn Abbas except from this route with this chain."
"5246","Narrated to us Abdallah ibn al-Sabbah al-Attar, he said: told us Yazid ibn Harun, he said: Shayban, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman, informed us, from Isa ibn Ali ibn Abdillah ibn Abbas, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The good omen of horses is in their chestnut color. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this route; and Isa ibn Ali — we do not know that he narrated from his father any musnad hadith other than this hadith."
"5247","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Marzuq ibn Bukayr, he said: told us Salih al-Naji, he said: told us Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Ali ibn Abdillah ibn Abbas, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The orphan, his head is wiped like this — and Salih described that he placed his palm in the middle of his head, then brought it down to its front, or to his forehead; and whoever has a father, like this — and he described that he placed his palm on the front of his head near his forehead, then raised it to the middle of his head. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this route, and we do not know for it any chain other than this chain; and none shared with Muhammad ibn Sulayman in this narration. He was the governor of Basra; and the hadith — we only wrote it as it is because we did not know it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this route, so for that we mentioned it."
"5248","And narrated to us al-Nadr ibn Tahir, he said: told us Ishaq ibn Sulayman ibn Ali ibn Abdillah ibn Abbas, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless for my nation in its early mornings. And this hadith has been reported from Ibn Abbas from another route; and this chain is better than the other chain. And we do not know that Ishaq ibn Sulayman transmitted any hadith in musnad form other than this hadith. And al-Nadr ibn Tahir was a man abundant in remembrance of Allah; he narrated hadiths, in some of which he was not followed."
"5249","Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Sa'id, he said: told us Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi, he said: told us Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abdallah ibn Abi Bakr, from Ali ibn Abdillah ibn Abbas, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Ka'bah, and around the Ka'bah were such-and-such idols; so he began striking them with a stick in his hand, saying: Truth has come and falsehood has perished. And this hadith was reported from Abdallah ibn Mas'ud and from Ibn Abbas; and this chain is rarer than the chain of Abdallah. And in the hadith of Abdallah there is speech not in the hadith of Ibn Abbas; and we do not know that Abdallah ibn Abi Bakr transmitted from Ali anything other than this hadith."
"5250","Narrated to us Raja ibn Muhammad al-Saqati, he said: told us Bakr ibn Yahya ibn Zabban, he said: told us Mindal, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Dawud ibn Ali, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Place the whip where the servant can see it. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who reported it except Ibn Abbas; and we do not know it reported from Ibn Abbas except from this route with this chain."
"5251","Narrated to us Abdallah ibn Sa'id Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj, he said: told us al-Mughirah ibn Jamil, he said: told us Sulayman ibn Ali ibn Abdillah ibn Abbas, he said: my father narrated to me, from my grandfather Abdallah ibn Abbas, in marfu' form, he said: Indeed wala' is neither transferred nor shifted. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except from this route with this chain. And al-Mughirah ibn Jamil is not known in hadith."
"5252","Narrated to us Amr ibn Ali, he said: told us Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Abdillah ibn Abbas, from his father; and from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abdillah ibn Abbas, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate a shoulder or meat, then prayed and did not rinse his mouth nor touch water. And this hadith, we only mentioned it because it is from Hisham ibn Urwah from al-Zuhri, and from Hisham from Muhammad ibn Ali; and we do not know that Hisham transmitted from Muhammad ibn Ali anything other than this hadith, though the wording of this hadith differs from the rest of the wordings reported from Ibn Abbas on that."
"5253","The hadith of Jabir ibn Zayd: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, told us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, he said: told us Shu'bah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas."
"5254","And narrated to us Amr ibn Ali, he said: told us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, he said: told us Shu'bah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he married while in ihram."
"5255","And narrated to us Amr ibn Ali, he said: told us Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, from Amr, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he married Maymunah while in ihram."
"5256","And narrated it to us Ahmad ibn Abdah, he said: Sufyan, meaning Ibn Uyaynah, informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah while in ihram. And this hadith has been reported from Ibn Abbas from various routes, so we sufficed with this chain, unless one of them adds to the wording, in which case it is written due to the addition."
"5257","And narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Amr ibn Ali, they said: told us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, he said: told us Shu'bah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5258","And narrated to us Salamah ibn Shabib, he said: told us Abd al-Razzaq, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5259","And narrated it to us Amr ibn Ali, he said: told us Abu Asim, he said: told us Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu al-Sha'tha', from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5260","And narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik, he said: told us Hammad ibn Zayd, from Amr, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5261","And narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abdah, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr, from Jabir, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5262","And narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali, they said: told us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, he said: told us Shu'bah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The muhrim wears trousers if he does not find the waist-wrapper, and wears the khuffs if he does not find the sandals. Shu'bah said in his hadith: that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Arafat... And Ibn Jurayj said: So I said to him: Do you cut them? He said: I did not hear it."
"5263","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Amr ibn Ali, they said: told us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, he said: told us Shu'bah, from Amr, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed seven together and eight together."
"5264","And narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abdah, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Amr, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): eight and seven. Amr said: And Zuhr and Asr are eight, and Maghrib; and he delayed Maghrib and hastened Isha. And this hadith has been reported from Ibn Abbas from various routes, and the chain is among the soundest chains reported on that."
"5265","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Umarah ibn Subayh and Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Hayyaj, they said: told us Qabisah, from Sufyan, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I was enrolled for such-and-such expedition while my wife wants me to perform Hajj with her. He said: Return and perform Hajj with your wife. And this hadith, Qabisah erred in it in two places, for the hadith is only: I was enrolled for an expedition while my wife wants Hajj, so he said: No woman travels except with a mahram; and Amr only reported it from Abu Ma'bad. Qabisah said: from Jabir ibn Zayd."
"5266","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ma'mar, he said: told us Abu Asim, from Zakariyya ibn Ishaq, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu al-Sha'tha', from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father is a very old man unable to perform Hajj; shall I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: Yes. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from Ibn Abbas with a better chain than this; and Ibn Uyaynah said in it: from Amr, from Ikrimah, except one man who said in it: from Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas."
"5267","And narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ma'mar, he said: told us Abu Asim, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me, he said: My knowledge and what occurs to my mind is that Abu al-Sha'tha' informed him that he heard Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution with the leftover of Maymunah. Thus said Ibn Jurayj; and Zakariyya ibn Ishaq differed from him, saying: from Amr, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas. And Ibn Uyaynah said: from Amr, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bathe, he and she, from one vessel."
"5268","Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn Sahl and Rizqullah ibn Musa, they said: told us Musa ibn Dawud, he said: told us Muhammad ibn Muslim, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every division divided in the Jahiliyyah stands upon what was divided; and every division which Islam reached and which was not divided stands upon the division of Islam. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who reported it from Amr ibn Dinar except Muhammad ibn Muslim, and we do not know it except from the hadith of Musa ibn Dawud."
"5269","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, he said: told us Muhammad ibn Abi Adi, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5270","And narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Taymi, he said: told us Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan, he said: told us Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5271","And narrated it to us Zayd ibn Akhzam and al-Sakan ibn Sa'id, they said: told us Bishr ibn Umar, he said: told us Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was propositioned with the daughter of Hamzah, so the Prophet of Allah said: She is the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding; and what is unlawful through lineage is unlawful through breastfeeding. And this hadith has been reported from Ibn Abbas from other than this route; and this chain is the firmest chain reported from Ibn Abbas. And as for the hadith of Shu'bah from Qatadah, we do not know it reported from Shu'bah except Yahya ibn Sa'id and Bishr ibn Umar."
"5272","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, he said: told us Ibn Abi Adi, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: Breaking the fast while traveling is a binding duty. And this hadith, we do not know it reported with this wording except from this route; and we did not hear anyone narrate it except Abu Musa from Ibn Abi Arubah."
"5273","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, he said: told us Ibn Abi Adi, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Zayd, that Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, used to combine the two prayers while traveling and say: It is the Sunnah. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who mentions it from Jabir ibn Zayd except Qatadah."
"5274","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, he said: told us Abd al-A'la, he said: told us Sa'id, from Qatadah, he said: I said to Jabir ibn Zayd: What cuts off the prayer? He said: Ibn Abbas said: The black dog and the menstruating woman. He said: I said: He used to mention a third. He said: What is it? I said: The donkey. He said: Slowly — the donkey. I said: He used to mention a fourth. He said: What is it? I said: The disbelieving foreigner. He said: If you can manage that neither a disbeliever nor a Muslim passes before you, then do so. And this hadith was transmitted in marfu' form by Yahya ibn Sa'id; and we do not know anyone who transmitted it in marfu' form except Yahya from Shu'bah."
"5275","Narrated to us Sahl ibn Bahr, he said: told us Musaddad, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, in marfu' form."
"5276","Narrated to us Amr ibn Ali, he said: told us Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi, he said: told us Shu'bah, from Abu al-Anbas, from Abu al-Sha'tha', from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set the ransom of the captives of the Jahiliyyah at four hundred. And this hadith, we do not know it reported except from Ibn Abbas with this wording; and we do not know it reported from Shu'bah except Sufyan ibn Habib and Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi."
"5277","Narrated to us Amr ibn Ali, he said: told us Husayn ibn Hafs, he said: told us Sufyan, from Duwayd, from Ismail ibn Thawban, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The evil eye is true. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from Ibn Abbas with this wording except from this route."
"5278","Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah, he said: told us al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman, he said: I heard al-Hakam ibn Aban narrate from al-Ghitrif, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Trustworthy Spirit, he said: The Lord, blessed and exalted, said: The servant's evil deeds and his good deeds are brought and set against one another; if a good deed remains for him, spacious place is made for him in Paradise. And this hadith with this wording, we do not know it reported except from Ibn Abbas; and we do not know for it any chain from Ibn Abbas other than this chain. And we do not know that al-Ghitrif transmitted from Jabir anything other than this hadith; nor did anyone report this hadith from al-Ghitrif except al-Hakam ibn Aban. And al-Hakam is unobjectionable."
"5279","Narrated to us Musa ibn Ishaq al-Khatmi, he said: told us Abd al-Salam ibn Asim, he said: told us al-Sabbah ibn Muharib, he said: told us Salim al-Muradi, from Amr ibn Harim, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed a commander over an army, he would call him and order him to fear Allah and to treat those with him of the Muslims well, then say: Fight in the name of Allah and in the path of Allah; fight those who disbelieve in Allah; do not steal from the spoils, do not betray, do not mutilate, and do not kill a child. And when you meet your enemy of the polytheists, call them to one of three courses: call them to Islam; if they answer, accept from them and refrain from them, then call them to emigration, and inform them that they have what the emigrants have and upon them is what is upon the emigrants. If they answer, accept from them and refrain from them. If they do not do so, inform them that they are like the Bedouin Muslims: they have nothing in the fay' nor in the spoils, while the judgment of Allah that applies to the Muslims applies to them. If they want you to let them come down upon the judgment of Allah, do not do so, for you do not know whether you will hit Allah's judgment concerning them or not; but let them come down upon your judgment. Then if they want you to give them Allah's covenant, do not do so, but give them your covenant and the covenant of your companions; for if you break your covenant and the covenant of your companions, it is better than that you break Allah's covenant. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from Ibn Abbas with this wording except from this route; and we do not know that Salim al-Muradi transmitted from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, anything other than this hadith."
"5280","Narrated to us Khalid ibn Yusuf, he said: my father narrated to me, from Zurarah ibn Abi al-Halal, that he heard Jabir ibn Zayd narrate from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered henna and forbade black. And we do not know that Zurarah transmitted from Jabir anything other than this; nor did anyone report it from him except Yusuf ibn Khalid."
"5281","Narrated to us Amr ibn Ali, he said: told us Husayn ibn Hafs, he said: told us Hisham ibn Sa'd, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution: he scooped a handful and rinsed his mouth and sniffed water and washed his face, then scooped a handful and washed his right hand, then scooped a handful and washed his left hand, then scooped a handful and wiped his head and his ears, and sprinkled upon his feet while on them were sandals, and wiped their outer and inner sides."
"5282","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Marzuq ibn Bukayr, he said: told us Abdallah ibn Raja, he said: told us Abu Amr al-Asqalani, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, in marfu' form to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: One washing suffices for each limb when it reaches the places of ablution."
"5283","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Mahdi, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Nusayr informed us, he said: told us Warqa, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution once each and combined sniffing and rinsing with one handful. And we only gathered these hadiths to clarify each one's addition over his companion in speech and in act, though their meanings are close to one another; and the case belongs to the one who adds, when he is trustworthy. As for the hadith of Ibn Idris, he added wiping the outer and inner ears, and we do not know anyone who said this from Ibn Abbas other than him. As for the hadith of Qabisah, that he performed ablution and sprinkled, he erred in it: it was only that he sprinkled his feet, but he carried it as sprinkling the private part since he abbreviated it. As for the hadith of Hisham ibn Sa'd, we do not know anyone who followed him in its wording; and Hisham is trustworthy. And this, in my view — and Allah knows best — was only that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) showed them the ablution, or he was performing ablution and wiped, saying: do like this, so wash; because reports have been established from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he washed his feet. As for the hadith of Abu Amr al-Asqalani, Muhammad ibn Marzuq erred in it in my view, for Ibn Raja narrates from Abu Amr Sa'id ibn Salamah many hadiths; and Abu Amr al-Asqalani — we do not know him. And the hadith is the meaning of the hadiths, though the wording differs from that. As for the hadith of Warqa, we do not know anyone who narrated it as Hajjaj narrated it, for others besides Hajjaj — it reached me that he narrates it from Zayd ibn Aslam; while Hajjaj said: from Warqa, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar. And we do not know that Amr ibn Dinar reported from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, any hadith."
"5284","Narrated to us Amr ibn Ali, he said: told us Yahya ibn Sa'id, he said: told us Malik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate a shoulder, then prayed and did not perform ablution."
"5285","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Aban, he said: told us Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you doubts in prayer and does not know how much he prayed, three or four, let him pray a rak'ah and prostrate two prostrations while sitting before he greets; if the rak'ah he prayed was a fifth, he pairs it with these two prostrations, and if it was a fourth, they are a humiliation for Satan. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who followed al-Darawardi in it; rather Ibn Ajlan and Dawud ibn Qays and others of Zayd's companions report it from Zayd, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id. But thus said al-Darawardi; and in this hadith that he said: he prostrates two prostrations before he greets."
"5286","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa, he said: told us Rawh ibn Ubadah, he said: told us Malik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while the people were with him; so he stood a long standing, about the length of Surah al-Baqarah, then bowed a long bowing, then stood a long standing shorter than the first standing, then bowed a long bowing shorter than the first bowing, then prostrated, then did in the second rak'ah the like of that, then finished, and the sun had cleared. He said: The sun and the moon are two signs of Allah's signs; they do not eclipse for anyone's death nor for his life. So when you see that, remember Allah. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we saw you reach out in this station of yours, then we saw you draw back. He said: I saw Paradise — or: Paradise was shown to me — and I reached for a bunch of grapes from it; had I taken it, you would have eaten from it as long as the world remains. And I saw the Fire, and I never saw a sight like today; and I saw most of its people are women. They said: Why, O Messenger of Allah? He said: By their ingratitude to the companion — Rawh said: and the companion is the husband — and by their ingratitude for kindness; if you do good to one of them, then she sees something from you, she says: I never saw any good from you at all."
"5287","Narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Isa ibn Sasan al-Susi, he said: told us Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ramli, he said: told us Sulayman ibn Hayyan, he said: told us Hisham ibn Sa'd, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things do not break the fasting person's fast: vomiting, cupping, and wet dream. And this hadith was reported by Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam from his father, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id; and Abd al-Rahman is lax in hadith. And others besides Abd al-Rahman reported it from Zayd, from Ata ibn Yasar, in mursal form. And Sulayman ibn Hayyan reported it from Hisham ibn Sa'd, from Zayd, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas; and this chain is among the best of them in chain and soundest, except that Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz was not a memorizer."
"5288","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, he said: told us Uthman ibn Umar, he said: told us Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Sa'id ibn Khalid, from Ismail ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to them while they were in the sitting, or in the mosque, and said: Shall I not inform you of the best of people in state? We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: A man holding his horse's bridle in jihad in Allah's path until he dies or is killed. Shall I not inform you of the one next to him? A man secluded in a mountain pass, establishing prayer, giving zakah, and withdrawing from people's evils. Shall I not inform you of the worst of people? The one who is asked by Allah and does not give thereby. And this hadith, we do not know it reported with this wording except from this route."
"5289","Narrated to us Amr ibn Ali, he said: told us Abu Mu'awiyah, from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing four: the ant, the bee, the frog, and the shrike. As for the ant, the bee, and the shrike, I have no doubt; and I doubt concerning the fourth, whether it is the frog or another. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who reported it except Ibn Jurayj from al-Zuhri; and we do not know it reported from him except Abu Mu'awiyah. And others besides Abu Mu'awiyah said: from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Zuhri, from a man, from Ibn Abbas. And Muhammad ibn Rabi'ah al-Kilabi said: from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Ibn Abbas."
"5290","Narrated to us Amr ibn Ali, he said: told us Yazid ibn Zuray', he said: told us Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father is a very old man who never performed Hajj; if I carry him on a camel he will not stay upon it, and if I tie him I will not feel safe for him. He said: If you were settling a debt for your father, were there a debt upon your father? He said: Yes. He said: Then perform Hajj on behalf of your father."
"5291","And narrated to us Abd al-A'la ibn Zayd al-Attar and Uthman ibn Amr al-Aruzzi, they said: told us Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi, he said: told us Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. And this hadith, they differed in it: al-Zuhri said from Sulayman ibn Yasar contrary to what Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq said. And we mention each hadith of them in its place with its wording; and we do not know that Muhammad ibn Sirin transmitted from Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq anything other than this hadith."
"5292","Narrated to us Amr ibn Ali, he said: told us Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik, he said: told us Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah, he said: told us al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: A woman of Khath'am came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of the Farewell Hajj and said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah's obligation upon His servants in Hajj has reached my father as a very old man unable to sit upright upon the mount; will it suffice for him that I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: Yes."
"5293","Narrated to us Amr, he said: told us Abu Asim, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Sulayman ibn Yasar narrated to me, from Abdallah ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. And this hadith is the correct one; and Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq omitted from it. And the correct is the hadith of Ibn Jurayj; and Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah dropped a man from the chain, for he did not say: from al-Fadl."
"5294","Narrated to us Amr ibn Ali, he said: told us Abu Asim, he said: told us Ibn Jurayj, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf informed me, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, that he passed by Abu Hurayrah while he was performing ablution, and said: Do you know from what I performed ablution? I performed ablution from crumbs of cottage cheese I ate; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Perform ablution from what fire has touched. So Ibn Abbas said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eat bread and meat and pray without performing ablution. And this hadith, we only mentioned it due to their disagreement in its chain: some of those who reported it from Sulayman ibn Yasar said: from one of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); while in this hadith it says: from Ibn Abbas. So we mentioned it to clarify its disagreement."
"5295","Narrated to us Abu Musa, he said: told us Hammad ibn Mas'adah, he said: told us Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Ata, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: They used to trade at Mina and Arafah and in the days of Hajj, but they feared trading in the Haram, so there was revealed: There is no blame upon you to seek bounty from your Lord, during the seasons of Hajj. Ubayd said: So we used to recite it, meaning: thus. And we do not know that Ubayd ibn Umayr transmitted from Ibn Abbas anything other than this hadith; and we only entered it in the Musnad because he said: it was revealed. And we do not know it reported from other than Ibn Abbas with other than this chain."
"5296","Narrated to us Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, he said: told us Nuh ibn Qays, he said: told us Amr ibn Malik, from Abu al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: There was a woman praying behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), among the most beautiful of people; so some of the people would advance in the row so as not to see her, and some would lag in the last row, so that when he bowed he would look. Then Allah, blessed and exalted, sent down concerning her: And We know those of you who advance and We know those who lag. And this hadith was narrated to us by a group from Nuh ibn Qays, among them: Muhammad ibn Musa, Ismail ibn Hafs, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik, and others; so we sufficed with the hadith of Abu Musa. And we do not know it reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Ibn Abbas; nor does it have any chain except this chain from him. And the name of Abu al-Jawza is Aws ibn Abdillah."
"5297","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi, he said: told us Nuh ibn Qays, he said: told us Yazid ibn Ka'b, from Amr ibn Malik, from Abu al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The scribe of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was called al-Sijill. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who reported it except Ibn Abbas; and we do not know for it any chain except this chain from him."
"5298","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Marzuq, he said: told us Ibrahim ibn Mahan, he said: told us Yahya ibn Amr ibn Malik, from his father, from Abu al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, glory be to Allah the Magnificent; I seek Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him. Whoever says it, it is written as he said it, then hung upon the Throne; no sin its doer commits erases it until he meets Allah on the day he meets Him, while it is sealed as he said it. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who reported it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Ibn Abbas; and we do not know for it any chain other than this chain."
"5299","Narrated to us Abu Mahdhurah al-Warraq, he said: told us Habban ibn Hilal, he said: told us Yahya ibn Amr ibn Malik, from his father, from Abu al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had you not sinned, Allah would have brought a people who sin, then seek Allah's forgiveness, and He forgives them. Abu Mahdhurah is trustworthy; he used to dictate from the days of Mu'adh, then Abu Dawud and those after him. And this hadith is reported from Anas; and we do not know it reported from Ibn Abbas except from this route with this chain."
"5300","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi, he said: told us Yahya ibn Amr ibn Malik, from his father, from Abu al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a man pitched his tent over a grave while not knowing it was a grave, and recited Surah Tabarak; then he heard a speaker say from the grave: It is the deliverer, it is the deliverer. He mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: It is the deliverer from the punishment of the grave. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who reported it with this wording except Ibn Abbas; and we do not know for it any chain from him except this chain."
"5301","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik, he said: told us Yahya ibn Amr, from his father, from Abu al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he finished the prayer, would say: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise; in His hand is good, and He is over all things Capable. O Allah, none withholds what You give, none gives what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him nothing against You. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from Ibn Abbas except from this route with this chain."
"5302","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan al-Wasiti, he said: told us Muhammad ibn Abi Nu'aym, he said: told us Sa'id ibn Zayd, from Amr ibn Malik, from Abu al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the land is fertile, shorten in travel and give the mounts their share, for Allah is Gentle and loves gentleness; and when the land is barren, press on through it, and upon you is night travel, for the land is folded at night. And beware the highway, for it is the shelter of snakes and the resting place of beasts. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Sa'id ibn Zayd except Muhammad ibn Abi Nu'aym; and we do not know it reported from Ibn Abbas except from this route. And something like it has been reported from Abu Hurayrah and Anas."
"5303","Narrated to us Zayd ibn Akhzam, he said: told us Muslim ibn Ibrahim, he said: told us Abu Hilal, from Uqbah ibn Abi Thubayt, from Abu al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise are those who do not die until their ears — or: their hearing — are filled with good praise."
"5304","I heard Hamdan ibn Ali al-Warraq say: I heard Muslim ibn Ibrahim say: told us Abu Hilal, from Uqbah ibn Abi Thubayt, from Abu al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, with the like of it. Hamdan said: I heard Muslim ibn Ibrahim say: It reached me that Uqbah ibn Abi Thubayt used to call the birds and they would answer him; and Uqbah was a Basran man, trustworthy, reliable, devout."
"5305","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Qurashi, he said: told us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, he said: told us Awf, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On the night I was taken by night and I awoke in Makkah, I was alarmed by my affair and knew that the people would belie me; so I sat apart, grieved. Then the enemy of Allah Abu Jahl passed by me; he came and sat down and said as if mocking me: Was there anything? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. He said: What is it? He said: I was taken by night tonight. He said: To where? He said: To Bayt al-Maqdis. He said: Then you awoke among us?! He said: Yes. He said: He did not show him that he belied him, but said: What if I call your people — will you narrate to them what you narrated to me? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. So he said: O company of Banu Ka'b ibn Lu'ayy. The gatherings dispersed to him and they came until they sat to him. He said: Narrate to your people what you narrated to me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was taken by night tonight. They said: To where? He said: To Bayt al-Maqdis. They said: And you awoke among us? He said: Yes. He said: Some clapping and some placing his hand upon his head in belying denial. They said: Can you describe the mosque to us? He said: So I went on describing until some of the description became confused to me. He said: Then the mosque was brought while I looked, until it was placed before the house of Ghifar, or Aqil. He said: So I described it while looking at it. He said: And among the people were those who had seen it, so the people said: As for the description, by Allah he is right. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Awf from Zurarah; and we do not know that Awf transmitted from Zurarah except two hadiths, one of them from Ibn Abbas and the other from Abdallah ibn Salam."
"5306","Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Yahya, he said: told us Amr ibn Asim, he said: told us Salih al-Murri, from Qatadah, from Zurarah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which deed is most beloved to Allah? He said: The solver, the resumer. They said: O Messenger of Allah, who is the solver, the resumer? He said: The companion of the Qur'an, who strikes from its beginning to its end; whenever he solves, he resumes. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatadah except Salih al-Murri."
"5307","Abu Jamrah: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, he said: told us Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Shu'bah, he said: told us Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: A red velvet cloth was placed in the grave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith, we do not know anyone who reports it from Ibn Abbas except Abu Jamrah."
"5308","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, he said: told us Shu'bah, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray thirteen rak'ahs at night. And this hadith has been reported from Ibn Abbas from other than this route, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed thirteen rak'ahs; and in this hadith is evidence that that was his prayer and that he used to persist in it."
"5309","Narrated to us Ismail ibn Mas'ud, he said: told us Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal, he said: told us Qurrah, meaning Ibn Khalid, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ashajj Abd al-Qays: In you are two traits which Allah and His messenger love: forbearance and deliberation. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who reported it from Abu Jamrah except Qurrah."
"5310","Narrated to us Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam al-Qaysi, he said: told us Muhammad ibn Sawa, he said: told us Shubayl ibn Azrah, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best people of the east are Abd al-Qays. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who reported it except Ibn Abbas with this wording; and we do not know it reported from him except Abu Jamrah. And we do not know it reported from Abu Jamrah except Shubayl ibn Azrah; and Shubayl is a well-known man of Basra. And we do not know it reported from him except Ibn Sawa."
"5311","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Qurashi, he said: told us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, he said: told us Awf, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On the night I was taken by night and I awoke in Makkah, I was alarmed by my affair and knew that the people would belie me; so I sat apart, grieved. Then the enemy of Allah Abu Jahl passed by me; he came and sat down and said as if mocking me: Was there anything? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. He said: What is it? He said: I was taken by night tonight. He said: To where? He said: To Bayt al-Maqdis. He said: Then you awoke among us?! He said: Yes. He said: He did not show him that he belied him, but said: What if I call your people, will you narrate to them what you narrated to me? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. So he said: O company of Banu Ka'b ibn Lu'ayy. The gatherings dispersed to him and they came until they sat to him. He said: Narrate to your people what you narrated to me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was taken by night tonight. They said: To where? He said: To Bayt al-Maqdis. They said: And you awoke among us? He said: Yes. He said: Some clapping and some placing his hand upon his head in belying denial. They said: Can you describe the mosque to us? He said: So I went on describing until some of the description became confused to me. He said: Then the mosque was brought while I looked, until it was placed before the house of Ghifar, or Aqil. He said: So I described it while looking at it. He said: And among the people were those who had seen it, so the people said: As for the description, by Allah he is right. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Awf from Zurarah; and we do not know that Awf transmitted from Zurarah except two hadiths, one of them from Ibn Abbas and the other from Abdallah ibn Salam."
"5312","Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Yahya, he said: told us Amr ibn Asim, he said: told us Salih al-Murri, from Qatadah, from Zurarah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which deed is most beloved to Allah? He said: The solver, the resumer. They said: O Messenger of Allah, who is the solver, the resumer? He said: The companion of the Qur'an, who strikes from its beginning to its end; whenever he solves, he resumes. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatadah except Salih al-Murri."
"5313","Abu Jamrah: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, he said: told us Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Shu'bah, he said: told us Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: A red velvet cloth was placed in the grave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith, we do not know anyone who reports it from Ibn Abbas except Abu Jamrah."
"5314","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, he said: told us Shu'bah, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray thirteen rak'ahs at night. And this hadith has been reported from Ibn Abbas from other than this route, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed thirteen rak'ahs; and in this hadith is evidence that that was his prayer and that he used to persist in it."
"5315","Narrated to us Ismail ibn Mas'ud, he said: told us Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal, he said: told us Qurrah, meaning Ibn Khalid, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ashajj Abd al-Qays: In you are two traits which Allah and His messenger love: forbearance and deliberation. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who reported it from Abu Jamrah except Qurrah."
"5316","Narrated to us Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam al-Qaysi, he said: told us Muhammad ibn Sawa, he said: told us Shubayl ibn Azrah, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best people of the east are Abd al-Qays. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who reported it except Ibn Abbas with this wording; and we do not know it reported from him except Abu Jamrah. And we do not know it reported from Abu Jamrah except Shubayl ibn Azrah; and Shubayl is a well-known man of Basra. And we do not know it reported from him except Ibn Sawa."
"5317","Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn Sahl, he said: told us Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi, he said: told us Ibrahim al-Ijli, from Hajjaj al-A'ishi, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the disputant of whoever wrongs Abd al-Qays. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who reported it except Muhammad ibn Bishr, and Ibrahim al-Ijli and Hajjaj al-A'ishi, for we do not know them mentioned except in this hadith. And we only mentioned this hadith despite the defect in its chain because we do not know it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this route."
"5318","Narrated to us Ismail ibn Sayf Abu Ishaq al-Quta'i, he said: told us Amr ibn Musawir, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless for my nation in its early mornings on its Thursday. He said: And Ibn Abbas said: Do not ask a man for a need at night, and do not ask a blind man for a need, for modesty is in the two eyes. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from Abu Jamrah except Amr; and Amr was reported from by Affan and a group of hadith scholars, and he was not strong. And we do not know for him other than these two hadiths."
"5319","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Musa, he said: told us Abbad ibn Abbad, he said: told us Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are this tribe of Rabi'ah, and we cannot reach you except in a sacred month; so order us with a matter which we take and call to it those behind us. He said: I order you with four and forbid you from four: I order you with bearing witness that there is no god but Allah, establishing prayer, giving zakah, and that you render to Allah a fifth of what you gain; and I forbid you from al-dubba, al-hantam, al-muzaffat, and al-naqir."
"5320","Ubadah: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Marzuq ibn Bukayr, he said: Harami ibn Hafs narrated to me, he said: told us Sadaqah ibn Ubadah, from his father Ubadah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and we slept past the prayer, the morning prayer, until the sun rose. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a caller, and he called as he used to call every day, and prayed the two rak'ahs of Fajr as he used to pray every day, then prayed the morning prayer as he used to pray every day. And this hadith has been reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with different wordings, that he slept past the prayer until the sun rose; and we do not know it reported from Ibn Abbas except from two routes, this route and another route reported by Ubaydah ibn Humayd, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to me, from Tamim ibn Salamah, from Masruq, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); al-Sari ibn Asim narrated it to us from Ubaydah ibn Humayd. And we do not know that Masruq reported from Ibn Abbas anything other than this hadith; nor did anyone report this hadith except Ubaydah ibn Humayd in connected form, while others besides Ubaydah reported it in mursal form."
"5321","Al-Nadr ibn Anas from Ibn Abbas: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa, he said: told us Mu'adh ibn Hisham, he said: my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, he said: A man came to Ibn Abbas and said: I am a man of Iraq who makes these pictures. So Ibn Abbas said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever makes a picture will be burdened on the Day of Resurrection to breathe into it, and he is not one to breathe, or: he will not breathe into it."
"5322","And narrated to us Nasr ibn Ali and Ahmad ibn Bakkar al-Bahili, they said: Abd al-A'la ibn Abd al-A'la informed us, he said: told us Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Abi al-Hasan, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5323","And narrated it to us Abu Kurayb, he said: told us Abu Mu'awiyah, he said: told us Ismail ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan, from his brother Sa'id, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5324","And narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, he said: told us Ibn Abi Adi, from Awf, from Sa'id ibn Abi al-Hasan, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5325","And narrated it to us Muhammad ibn Umar ibn al-Hayyaj, he said: told us Qabisah, he said: told us Sufyan, from Awf, from Sa'id ibn Abi al-Hasan, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever makes a picture will be burdened to breathe into it on the Day of Resurrection, and he is not one to breathe. And we only gathered these chains to clarify each hadith for what we mentioned. As for the hadith of Qatadah from al-Nadr ibn Anas from Ibn Abbas, we do not know it reported except Mu'adh ibn Hisham from his father from Qatadah; and we do not know that al-Nadr ibn Anas reported from Ibn Abbas except this hadith, and Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah also reported it from al-Nadr. As for the hadith of Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq, we do not know it reported from Yahya except Abd al-A'la. As for the hadith of al-Hasan from his brother, we do not know it reported except Ismail ibn Muslim from al-Hasan; and al-Hasan did not transmit from his brother in musnad form except this hadith. As for the hadith of Awf, it is well-known from Awf, so we mentioned it so it be known that it is well-known from Awf; and we do not know it reported from al-Thawri except Qabisah, and Shu'bah reported it from Awf; Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghazwan reported it, adding from Shu'bah."
"5326","Narrated to us Abu Musa, he said: told us Ghassan ibn Mudar, he said: told us Sa'id ibn Yazid, from Abu Nadrah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I spent the night at my maternal aunt Maymunah; then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at night praying. So I performed ablution, then went and stood at his left; when he knew I wanted prayer, he turned me to his right. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed and prayed witr with five, or with seven, and turned me; then he slept until I heard his whistling, then the prayer was established and he prayed without performing ablution. Sa'id said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was protected. And this hadith has been reported from Ibn Abbas with different wordings; and we do not know it reported from Ibn Abbas with this wording except from this route with this chain."
"5327","Narrated to us Nasr ibn Ali, he said: told us Ghassan ibn Mudar, he said: told us Sa'id ibn Yazid, from Abu Nadrah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: Whoever is pleased to forbid what Allah and His messenger forbade, let him forbid the nabidh of the jar. And this hadith with this wording, we do not know it reported except from Ibn Abbas; and Abu Salamah did not transmit from Sa'id ibn Yazid, from Abu Nadrah, from Ibn Abbas, except these two hadiths. And the name of Abu Nadrah is al-Mundhir ibn Malik ibn Qit'ah, and the name of Abu Jamrah is Nasr ibn Imran."
"5328","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ma'mar, he said: told us Muslim ibn Ibrahim, he said: told us Shaddad ibn Sa'id Abu Talhah, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of Quraysh youth, do not commit adultery; indeed whoever Allah preserves his private part for, he enters Paradise. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except from this route with this chain."
"5329","Narrated to us Nasr ibn Ali, he said: Khalid ibn al-Harith informed us, he said: told us Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Abu Talib al-Duba'i, from Ibn Abbas."
"5330","And narrated to us Abu Musa, he said: told us al-Ansari, he said: told us Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Abu Talib al-Duba'i, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a cupper cupped the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), called Abu Taybah; so he gave him his wage and reduced from his yield. He said: And Ibn Abbas used to say: Had it been unlawful, the Messenger of Allah would not have given it to him. And we do not know that Abu Talib al-Duba'i transmitted from Ibn Abbas, nor from other than Ibn Abbas, anything other than this hadith; nor did anyone report it from him other than Qatadah."
"5331","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, he said: told us Ibn Abi Adi, from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Abu Hassan al-A'raj, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both — and the name of Abu Hassan is Muslim — he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed at Dhu al-Hulayfah, and I saw him mark his sacrificial camel on the hump on the right side, then wipe the blood from it and garland it with two sandals, then mount his riding beast; when al-Bayda became level with him, he entered ihram and raised his voice with Hajj."
"5332","Narrated to us Abu Salamah Yahya ibn Khalaf, he said: told us Abd al-A'la, from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Abu Hassan, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. And this act, we do not know anyone who reported it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Ibn Abbas; and we do not know for it from Ibn Abbas any chain except this chain."
"5333","And narrated to us Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, he said: told us Ibn Abi Adi, he said: told us Shu'bah, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Abu Hassan al-A'raj say: A man said to Ibn Abbas: What is this fatwa which has spread, or branched out, among the people, that whoever circumambulates the House has become released? He said: That is the Sunnah of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), though you dislike it. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who reports it with this wording except Ibn Abbas; and we do not know for it any chain other than this chain. And Abu Hassan did not report from Ibn Abbas except these two hadiths."
"5334","Abu al-Aliyah: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, he said: told us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, he said: told us Shu'bah, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Abu al-Aliyah say: The cousin of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me, meaning Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: It is not for a servant to say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta, attributing him to his father. And it was mentioned from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he was taken by night, so he said: Musa is tall as if of the men of Shanu'ah; and he said: Isa is curly, of medium stature; and he mentioned Malik, keeper of Hell, and he mentioned the Dajjal. And this hadith, we do not know it reported with this wording except from Ibn Abbas with this chain; and Ibn Abi Arubah and others reported it from Qatadah."
"5335","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, he said: told us Mu'adh ibn Hisham, from his father, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say at distress: There is no god but Allah, the Knowing, the Forbearing; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the Magnificent Throne; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the heavens and Lord of the earth, Lord of the Noble Throne. And this hadith, we do not know it reported with this wording except from Ibn Abbas with this chain; and more than one reported it from Qatadah, so we sufficed with Hisham."
"5336","Narrated to us Zayd ibn Akhzam Abu Talib al-Ta'i, he said: told us Bishr ibn Umar, he said: told us Aban, meaning Ibn Yazid, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the wind contended with a man for his cloak and he cursed it; that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Do not curse it, for it is commanded; and whoever curses a thing undeserving of it, the curse returns upon its utterer."
"5337","And this hadith was reported by Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah and Hisham ibn Abi Abdillah together, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Aliyah, and they did not say: from Ibn Abbas. Narrated it to us Abu Musa from Mu'adh ibn Hisham from his father from Qatadah from Abu al-Aliyah."
"5338","And from al-Ansari from Sa'id from Qatadah from Abu al-Aliyah."
"5339","Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Hani, he said: told us Muhammad ibn Bakkar, he said: told us Sa'id ibn Bashir, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Were it not for the weakness of the weak and the sickness of the sick, I would have delayed the last Isha prayer; I think: to a third of the night. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who transmitted it in musnad form from Qatadah, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, with this wording, except Sa'id ibn Bashir."
"5340","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim, keeper of al-Sabiri, he said: told us al-Hasan ibn Musa, he said: told us Hammad ibn Salamah, from Yusuf ibn Abdillah ibn al-Harith, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Abdallah ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: When a matter befell the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would say: There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Magnificent; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the Magnificent Throne; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the Noble Throne; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the heavens and the earth and Lord of the Noble Throne; then he would supplicate. And this hadith, we do not know it reported with this wording except from this route; and we do not know that Yusuf ibn Abdillah ibn al-Harith transmitted from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, anything other than this hadith."
"5341","Narrated to us Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani, he said: told us Ahmad ibn Abdillah, he said: told us Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from al-A'mash, from Ziyad ibn Husayn, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I learned al-Muhkam, meaning al-Mufassal, in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when I was then twelve, or twelve years old. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who reported it from al-A'mash except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash."
"5342","Narrated to us Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, he said: told us Abd al-Razzaq, he said: al-Thawri informed us, from al-A'mash, from Ziyad ibn Husayn, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people shooting and said: Shoot, O sons of Ismail, for your father was an archer. And this hadith has been reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from various routes; and we do not know it reported from Ibn Abbas except from this route. And we do not know it reported from al-A'mash other than al-Thawri."
"5343","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, he said: told us Ibn Abi Adi, he said: told us Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he traveled until he came upon a pass and said: Which pass is this? We said: It is Harsha, or Lift. He said: As if I look at Musa ibn Imran upon a red she-camel, wearing a woolen cloak, his she-camel's halter of fiber, passing through this valley reciting talbiyah."
"5344","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Hayyaj, he said: told us Qabisah, he said: told us Sufyan, from Awf, from Ziyad ibn Husayn, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me on the morning of Muzdalifah: Pick for me pebbles of the pebbles of khadhf. So I brought them to him and he placed them in his hand and said: With the like of these, with the like of these; beware of going deep, for those before you perished only, I think he said: by going deep in religion. And this hadith was reported by a group from Awf, so we mentioned it from al-Thawri and sufficed with him."
"5345","Narrated to us Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Kabir, he said: told us Sa'id ibn Suwayd, he said: told us Imran al-Qattan, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The worst food is the food of the wedding feast: the rich is invited to it and the poor is left. And this hadith, we heard it only from Abd al-Quddus from Sa'id ibn Suwayd, and he was not followed in it."
"5346","Narrated to us Dawud ibn Sulayman Abu al-Mutarrif, he said: told us Malik ibn Su'ayr, from al-A'mash, from Ziyad ibn Husayn, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas."
"5347","Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Jarawi, he said: told us Amr ibn Abi Salamah, he said: told us Sa'id ibn Bashir, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas."
"5348","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, he said: told us Abd al-Wahhab, he said: told us Ayyub, from Abu Raja, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, say: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said — or he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I looked into Paradise and saw most of its people are the poor; and I looked into the Fire and saw most of its people are women. And this hadith differed in its chain: Awf said, from Abu Raja, from Imran ibn Husayn; while Ayyub and Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah said, from Abu Raja, from Ibn Abbas."
"5349","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik, he said: told us Hammad ibn Zayd, from al-Ja'd Abu Uthman, from Abu Raja, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reporting it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever sees from his commander something he dislikes, let him be patient; for there is none who leaves the community a span then dies except that he dies a death of Jahiliyyah. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who reported it with this wording except al-Ja'd, from Abu Raja, from Ibn Abbas."
"5350","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik, he said: told us Ja'far ibn Sulayman, he said: told us al-Ja'd Abu Uthman, from Abu Raja, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), reporting, he said: Whoever intends a good deed, write it for him as a good deed; if he does it, write it for him as ten; if he intends an evil deed, do not write it; if he leaves it, write it for him as a good deed; and if he does it, write it as an evil deed. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who reported it with this wording except Ibn Abbas; and we do not know for it any chain other than this chain. And the name of Abu Raja is Imran ibn Taym."
"5351","Al-Sha'bi from Ibn Abbas: Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari, he said: told us Abdallah ibn Numayr, he said: told us Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the one who speaks on Friday while the imam preaches is the likeness of the donkey carrying books. And this hadith, we do not know it reported with this wording from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this route with this chain; and we do not know it narrated from Mujalid except Abdallah ibn Numayr."
"5352","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abd al-Karim al-Azdi, he said: told us Muhammad ibn Mahan, told us Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj, from Ibn Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas."
"5353","And narrated to us Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Wasiti, he said: told us Abu Amr al-Lakhmi ibn al-Hajjaj, he said: told us Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Abdallah ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: A delegation of Bakr ibn Wa'il came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when they finished their affair, he said to them: Is there among you one who knows Quss ibn Sa'idah al-Iyadi? They said: Yes, all of us know him. He said: What happened to him? They said: He perished. He said: I do not forget him at the market of Ukaz, in the sacred month, upon a red camel, addressing the people, saying: O people, gather and listen and heed: everyone who lives dies, everyone who dies passes, and all that is coming comes. In the heaven is news, and in the earth are lessons: a spread bed, a raised roof, stars running, seas unfathomable, and a trade never perishing. Quss swore truly: if there be pleasure in the matter, there will be wrath; and Allah has a religion dearer to Him than this religion of yours upon which you are. Why do I see people go and not return? Were they pleased and so stayed, or were they left and so slept? Then he began to recite. The people of the generations — Abu Bakr said: In other than this hadith it is reported that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Bakr: How did he say? He said: So Abu Bakr began to recite this poetry which is mentioned from Quss ibn Sa'idah. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from any route except this route; and we do not know it reported from Mujalid except Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj. And Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj narrated hadiths in which he was not followed; and a group of scholars narrated from him. And when we did not find this hadith with other than him, we found no escape from producing it from him."
"5354","Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Yusuf, he said: told us Hafs ibn Ghiyath, from Asim al-Ahwal, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a grave. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from Asim al-Ahwal except from this route, and we heard it only from Ibrahim; and I think Ibrahim ibn Yusuf erred in it, for it is only known from Hafs from al-Shaybani from al-Sha'bi from Ibn Abbas."
"5355","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ma'mar and al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad, they said: told us Wahb ibn Jarir, he said: told us Shu'bah, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a grave. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Ismail except Shu'bah, nor narrated from Shu'bah except Wahb ibn Jarir."
"5356","Narrated to us Abdallah ibn Sa'id al-Kindi, he said: told us Abdallah ibn Idris, he said: told us al-Shaybani, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a grave and magnified over it four times. And this hadith was reported from al-Shaybani by a group, and none of them said: he magnified over it four times, except Abdallah ibn Idris."
"5357","And narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Yunus al-Baghdadi, he said: told us Ishaq ibn Mansur, he said: told us Huraym ibn Sufyan, from al-Shaybani, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a grave after three. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who said in it, from al-Shaybani: he prayed over a grave after three, except Huraym; and Huraym is a man of Kufa, unobjectionable. And he added over the rest of the narrations from al-Shaybani, so it was written for that reason."
"5358","And narrated to us Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti and Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan al-Wasiti, they said: told us Yazid ibn Harun, he said: Sharik informed us, from al-Shaybani, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over a grave, and he placed me at his right. And this wording, we do not know anyone who reported it from al-Shaybani except Sharik; and we do not know it reported from Sharik except Yazid ibn Harun. So we mentioned it for the addition which he added over the rest of the hadiths."
"5359","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abdah, he said: Sufyan, meaning Ibn Uyaynah, informed us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drink standing from Zamzam."
"5360","And narrated to us Abdallah ibn al-Sabbah al-Attar, he said: told us Abu Ali al-Hanafi Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid, he said: told us Sharik, from al-Shaybani, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank from Zamzam standing. And the hadith of al-Shaybani, we do not know it reported except Sharik from al-Shaybani. As for the hadith of Asim, a group reported it from Asim, so we sufficed with those we mentioned."
"5361","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi, he said: told us Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad, he said: told us Asim al-Ahwal, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night, and I stood at his left, so he turned me and placed me at his right. And this hadith has been reported from Ibn Abbas from various routes; and we do not know it reported from al-Sha'bi except from this route. And we do not know it reported from al-Sha'bi except Asim."
"5362","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa, he said: told us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, he said: told us Shu'bah, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he was cupped, was cupped in the two jugular veins. He said: So he called a boy of Banu Bayadah and gave the cupper his wage, a mudd and a half. He said: And he spoke to his masters, and they reduced from him half a mudd; and upon him were two mudds. And this hadith, we do not know it reported with this wording except from this route with this chain; and something close to it with other than its wording has been reported from Ibn Abbas and from others. And Jabir — a group of scholars spoke about him, yet they narrated from him."
"5363","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, he said: told us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, he said: told us Shu'bah, from Jabir, he said: I heard al-Sha'bi narrate from Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established prayer in travel as two rak'ahs, and it is complete; and witr in travel is Sunnah. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who reports it from al-Sha'bi except Jabir; and our mention of him has preceded."
"5364","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Umarah ibn Subayh, he said: told us Nasr ibn Muzahim, he said: told us Qays, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, when were you written as a prophet? He said: While Adam was between spirit and body. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from Ibn Abbas except from this route; and we do not know it reported from Jabir except Qays, nor from Qays except Nasr ibn Muzahim. And he was not strong; but when this hadith was not heard except from him, we produced it from him. And Nasr was not a liar, but there was Shi'ism in him."
"5365","Narrated to us Abu Musa, he said: told us Wahb ibn Jarir, he said: told us Shu'bah, from Asim al-Ahwal, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Zamzam and asked for drink; so I brought him a bucket, and he drank standing."
"5366","Muhammad ibn Mu'awiyah ibn Malij al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, he said: 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey, and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complained of thirst, so he said: Bring me water. They brought him a vessel containing water, and he placed his hand in the water, and the water began to gush forth from between the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as if it were the staff of Musa. The people drank and filled their vessels. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from 'Ata from al-Sha'bi except Khalaf ibn Khalifah, and we do not know that 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated with an isnad from al-Sha'bi from Ibn 'Abbas any hadith other than this one. And Abu Kudaynah narrated it from 'Ata, from Abu al-Duha, from Ibn 'Abbas."
"5367","Muhammad ibn 'Umar ibn Hayyaj al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), regarding: Say: I do not ask you for any reward for it except love for the relatives: he said: Except that you maintain ties with my kin."
"5368","And Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: my father informed me, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn 'Abbas, similarly. And this hadith has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas by more than one chain, and we do not know for it an isnad better than this isnad, and we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Shu'bah except 'Ali ibn Nasr."
"5369","Ibrahim ibn Yusuf al-Sayrafi narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: This verse was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at 'Arafah: This day I have perfected for you your religion and completed upon you My favor and approved for you Islam as religion. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Sha'bi except Dawud, nor from Dawud except Ibn Idris, and we did not hear it except from Ibrahim ibn Yusuf. And Yusuf ibn Mihran narrated it from Ibn 'Abbas."
"5370","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, he said: I heard 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrating from his father, from Abu al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he passed by a woman far advanced in pregnancy at the door of a tent, and he said: Perhaps he intends to have intercourse with her. They said: Yes. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had resolved to curse him with a curse that would enter the grave with him. How can he make him an heir when he is not lawful for him?! And how can he enslave him when he is not lawful for him?!"
"5371","[...] Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn 'Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Maghrib prayer is the witr of the daytime, so make the night prayer odd-numbered (witr). And this hadith about the Maghrib prayer being the witr of the daytime - we do not know anyone who narrated it except 'Abd al-'Aziz from Hisham; and the combination of the two hadiths about the night prayer being two by two is well known from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Ibn 'Umar."
"5372","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from Yunus ibn 'Ubayd, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5373","And Muslim ibn Hatim narrated to us; 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly to the hadith: The night prayer is two by two."
"5374","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ibn 'Umar, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in an army, and we met the enemy. When we returned to Madinah we said: If only we could meet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); if it (amnesty) is granted to us... So we met him at the Fajr prayer and said to him: We are the deserters. He said: Rather, you are the returners (to battle). They said: Such and such happened, and they informed him. He said: Do not do (that again), for I am the rallying force of the Muslims. He said: And we kissed his hand. And we do not know that Ibn Abi Layla narrated from Ibn 'Umar any hadith other than this one."
"5375","And 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us; Abu Qutaybah narrated to us; Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Zuhayr ibn Abi Thabit, from Tamim ibn 'Iyad - or so-and-so ibn 'Iyad - from Ibn 'Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took sahur one night, then 'Alqamah ibn 'Ulathah came, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a head (of livestock to eat) and began eating from it. Then Bilal came to announce the Fajr prayer to him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Gently, O Bilal, until 'Alqamah finishes his sahur. And this hadith - we do not know it narrated from Ibn 'Umar except through this chain. Bilal used to call the adhan before dawn, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Gently, until 'Alqamah finishes his sahur, because 'Alqamah did not know that Bilal calls the adhan before dawn; had Bilal called the adhan, 'Alqamah would have refrained (from eating) due to his little knowledge that Bilal calls the adhan before dawn."
"5376","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Tawbah al-'Anbari, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn 'Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a lizard (dabb), and one of his wives found it distasteful, so he said: Eat it; it is lawful, there is no harm in it. And this hadith - we do not know it narrated from Ibn 'Umar with this wording except through the narration of al-Sha'bi from him."
"5377","Al-Hasan [...] Ibrahim ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us; 'Amr ibn Mansur narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from [...] and he said: Place the knife in it, and mention the name of Allah. [...] it is not narrated from Ibn 'Umar except through this chain, and we do not know anyone who narrated it except [...]"
"5378","[...] 'Ali; 'Uthman ibn 'Umar narrated to us; Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Junayd, from Ibn 'Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hell has seven gates; one of them is for whoever draws the sword against my ummah - or he said: against the ummah of Muhammad. And this hadith - we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this chain."
"5379","'Amr narrated to us; Yazid narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Marzuq, from 'Atiyyah, he said: I recited to Ibn 'Umar: Allah is the One who created you from weakness. He said: From weakness. Then he said: I recited it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as: from weakness."
"5380","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us; Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from 'Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drags his lower garment out of arrogance, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. Then I met Ibn 'Umar at al-Balat and mentioned to him the hadith of Abu Sa'id from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: My ears heard it and my heart retained it."
"5381","And 'Amr narrated to us; Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us; Jabalah ibn Suhaym narrated to us, from Ibn 'Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drags a garment of his garments out of arrogance or pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"5382","Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Haddadi narrated to us; 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us; Shayban narrated to us, from Firas, from 'Atiyyah al-'Awfi, from Ibn 'Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last seven nights."
"5383","And Muhammad ibn al-Layth narrated to us; 'Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Shayban, from Firas, from 'Atiyyah, from Ibn 'Umar, he said: The mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was made of palm trunks. It fell into ruin in the time of Abu Bakr, so he rebuilt it with palm trunks and palm fronds. Then it fell into ruin in the time of 'Umar, so he rebuilt it with palm trunks and palm fronds. Then it fell into ruin during the caliphate of 'Uthman, so he built it with baked bricks, and its structure has remained so until now. He said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the lizard (dabb), and he said: I do not eat it, nor do I forbid it. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Each of you is a shepherd, and each of you is accountable for his flock. The imam is a shepherd and is accountable for his flock; the man is a shepherd in his house and is accountable for his flock; the woman is a shepherdess in her house and is accountable for her flock; and the slave is (a shepherd) regarding the wealth of his master and is accountable for his flock. He said: Ibn 'Umar said: I divorced my wife while she was menstruating, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to take her back."
"5384","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us; Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us; Asbagh ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Abu Bishr informed me, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever hoards food has disassociated himself from Allah, and Allah has disassociated Himself from him. He said: And whenever the people of a courtyard spend the night with a Muslim among them hungry, the protection of Allah is absolved from them. And this hadith - we do not know it narrated from Ibn 'Umar except through this chain, nor do we know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this chain."
"5385","'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabuwayh al-Marwazi narrated to us; Abu al-Yaman narrated to us; Abu al-Mahdi Sa'id ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every tree has its fruit, and [...] the hearts are the offspring. Allah does not have mercy on one who does not have mercy on his child. By the One in whose Hand is my soul, Allah shows mercy only to the merciful [...] except the merciful. We said: O Messenger of Allah, all of us show mercy. He said: It is not mercy that one of you shows mercy to his companion; rather [...]"
"5386","'Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; Abu al-Yaman narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah [...] from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Five things are part of faith; whoever lacks any of them has no faith: [...] contentment with the decree of Allah, entrusting affairs to Allah, reliance upon Allah, and patience at [...] No man attains the reality of Islam until people feel safe from him regarding their blood and their wealth. Someone said: O Messenger of Allah, [...] which is best? He said: The one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. Landmarks like the beacons of the road: testimony that [...] Allah alone with no partner, establishing the prayer, giving the zakah, judging by the Book of Allah, obeying the unlettered Prophet, and greeting the children of Adam when you meet them."
"5387","And 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; Abu al-Yaman narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to recite in the witr: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High; and: Say: O you disbelievers; and: Say: He is Allah, the One."
"5388","And 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; Abu al-Yaman narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Ibn 'Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: What is the earth upon? He said: The earth is upon water. It was said: What is the water upon? He said: Upon a green rock. It was said: What is the rock upon? He said: Upon the back of a whale whose two ends meet the Throne. It was said: What is the whale upon? He said: Upon the shoulder of an angel whose feet are in the air."
"5389","And 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi' narrated to us; Abu al-Mahdi Sa'id ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The ruler is the shade of Allah on earth; every wronged one among His servants resorts to him. If he is just, he earns reward, and upon the subjects is gratitude. If he acts unjustly, deviates, or oppresses, upon him is the burden, and upon the subjects is patience. When the rulers act unjustly, the sky withholds rain; when zakah is withheld, livestock perish; when adultery becomes widespread, poverty and destitution appear; and when the covenant of protection (dhimmah) is violated, the disbelievers are given ascendancy - or a word like it."
"5390","'Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; Abu al-Yaman narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Ibn 'Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked Abu Bakr and 'Umar (may Allah have mercy on them both) about their witr. Abu Bakr said: I perform witr at the beginning of the night. He said: Cautious. And he said to 'Umar, and he said: I perform witr at the end of the night. He said: Strong and aided."
"5391","And 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; Abu al-Yaman narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Ibn 'Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed back from his Companions for the Fajr prayer until they said: The sun has risen - or: will rise - then he came out and led them in the Fajr prayer, and said: Remain firm in your rows. Then he turned to them and said to them: Do you know what kept me from you? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: I prayed in my prayer place, and heaviness was cast upon my ear, then my Lord - Blessed and Exalted - came to me in the most beautiful form and said: O Muhammad. I said: At Your service, my Lord, and may You be blessed. He said: Regarding what does the highest assembly dispute? I said: I do not know, my Lord. He placed His hand between my shoulders until I felt its coolness between my breasts, and I came to know what He asked me about. Then He said: O Muhammad. I said: At Your service, my Lord, and may You be blessed. He said: Regarding what does the highest assembly dispute? I said: Regarding expiations and ranks. He said: And what are the expiations and ranks? I said: The expiations are perfecting ablution in disliked circumstances, walking on foot to the Friday prayers, and sitting in the mosques after the prayers. As for the ranks: feeding food, speaking good words, and prostrating at night while people sleep. My Lord, Blessed and Exalted, said to me: Ask Me, O Muhammad. I said: I ask You for performance of good deeds, abandonment of evil deeds, and love of the poor. I ask You to forgive me and have mercy on me; and if You intend tribulation for a people, take me to You without being tribulated. O Allah, I ask You for Your love, the love of whoever loves You, and the love of deeds that bring me closer to Your love. O Allah, I ask You for faith that touches my heart, so that I know that nothing will befall me except what You have written for me, and contentment with what You have decreed for me."
"5392","And 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; Abu al-Yaman narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Three things break the back. Abu Bakr said: One of them slipped my mind. A bad wife whom her husband trusts while she betrays him; an imam (leader) who angers Allah and pleases people. The deed of the believing woman is like the deed of seventy truthful ones, and the deed of the immoral woman is like the immorality of a thousand immoral women."
"5393","Salamah narrated to us; Abu al-Mughirah 'Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Ibn 'Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate with these words: O Allah - I think he said - faith that touches my heart, so that I know that nothing will befall me except what You have written for me, and contentment in livelihood with what You have apportioned for me. The hadiths of Sa'id ibn Sinan from Abu al-Zahiriyyah from Ibn 'Umar were written down only for the beauty of their wording; we do not know anyone who shared with him in most of them. Sa'id is not a preserver (of hadith); he is Syrian, and people narrated from him despite his poor memory and tolerated his hadith. What comes after him in the rest of the isnad is sound."
"5394","'Ubayd ibn Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us; my father narrated to us; al-A'mash narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abdullah, from Sa'd, the freedman of Talhah, from Ibn 'Umar, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrating a hadith which, had I heard it only once or twice - until he counted seven times - but I heard it more than that. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Al-Kifl of the Children of Israel would not refrain from any sin he committed. A woman came to him, and he gave her sixty dinars on condition that he sleep with her. When he sat with her as a man sits with his wife, she trembled and wept. He said: What makes you weep? She said: No (illness), but it is a deed I have never done, and only need drove me to it. He said: So you do this while you have never done it? Go, it is yours - meaning the dinars. And he said: By Allah, I will never disobey Allah again after this. He spent the night, and in the morning it was written on his door: Allah has forgiven al-Kifl. And this hadith - we do not know for it any chain from Ibn 'Umar except this chain."
"5395","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us; 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Firas, he said: Abu Salih narrated to me, from Zadham, he said: I was with Ibn 'Umar when he called a slave of his who had angered him and freed him, then said: I gain no reward from it worth even this - or: the measure of this. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever strikes a slave of his as a prescribed punishment, or slaps him - 'Abd al-Rahman doubted - his expiation is to free him. And this hadith - we do not know for it any chain from Ibn 'Umar better than this chain."
"5396","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Sa'd ibn 'Ubaydah, from Ibn 'Umar, that a man swore by the Ka'bah, so Ibn 'Umar said: Swear by the Lord of the Ka'bah; for 'Umar used to swear by his father, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not swear by your father, for whoever swears by other than Allah has committed associating partners with Allah (shirk)."
"5397","And 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated it to us; Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Sufyan [...] Mansur, from Sa'd ibn 'Ubaydah, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: And he swore by [...] he has committed shirk."
"5398","And Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn 'Ubaydah narrated it to us: Abu 'Asim narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us; my father narrated to me [...] from Sa'd ibn 'Ubaydah, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"5399","And 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated it to us; 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Sa'd ibn 'Ubaydah, from Ibn 'Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears by other than Allah has committed shirk."
"5400","Salamah narrated to us; 'Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Ibn 'Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Knowledge is about to be lifted. He repeated it three times. Ziyad ibn Labid said: O Prophet of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, how will knowledge be lifted from us when we have recited this Book of Allah and teach it to our children, and our children will teach it to their children?! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to him saying: May your mother be bereaved of you, O Ziyad ibn Labid! I used to count you among the jurists of Madinah!! Are not these Jews and Christians - with them the Torah and the Gospel?! What did it avail them?! Allah does not take away knowledge by lifting it up; rather He takes it away with its bearers - I think he said - and no scholar departs from this ummah except that it leaves a breach in Islam that will not be closed until the Day of Resurrection. These are known by their kunyahs: Sa'd ibn Sinan is Abu al-Mahdi, Kathir ibn Murrah is Abu Shajarah, and Abu al-Zahiriyyah's name is Hudayr."
